h its branch ready. When the last step passes, a workspace set to merge merges the branch into its base on the host; one set to leave keeps the branch. |"," | D42 | Governance is per step. A step may change files or only reads, and the gate refuses a write from a step that only reads. Dials, notices, artifacts and evals name steps. |","+| D43 | A step may name its own model and budget. The model wins over the job's and the server's. The budget is how often its failure may send work back (two by default) and the most its turns may cost; past the cost, the factory starts no more turns there by itself, but a person's retry, note or answer still runs. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":118,"oldLines":12,"newStart":118,"newLines":19,"lines":[" 0, and graded the same, 7. The run found that a change from zero read"," \"same\" and that a zero drew a sliver of bar; both are fixed."," ","+### U7. A model and a budget per step (D43)","+","+- A step's options: its model, the most revisions its failure sends back,","+  and the most its turns may spend.","+- The step's model wins over the job's and the server's.","+- Past its spend, the factory starts no more turns at the step by itself;","+  a person's retry, note or answer still runs.","+- The workflow editor shows the three options on a step.","+"," ## After this plan"," "," - A step is named `workflow/step`, and constraints and capabilities apply","   per workflow step, not per kind of step. This changes D42 and the gate.","-- A model and a budget per step, chosen in the workflow editor: the most","-  revisions a step may take, and the most it may spend."," - Workflows that branch: a step can name a step to go to on failure, so a","   workflow draws as a flowchart. Today a failure waits for you or goes back","   to the step that writes. This changes the core, so it needs a decision"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"39fd3f90-4c06-412b-bd02-8d13e71b9cf7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":13,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"55abb7df-124c-498a-9ece-2a837a75251f","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
