{"parentUuid":"9f3f90c4-7202-4d0c-9270-8fccaa52640c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwxNRfr7yAtfAJQbpR1G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2387,"cache_read_input_tokens":681235,"output_tokens":905,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":126},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2387,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":905,"cache_read_input_tokens":681235,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2387},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"cf8492e9-f975-4733-81a0-cb443819260f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwxNRG3yaK6tko6QLyWW","attributionMcpServer":"cmux-cua","attributionMcpTool":"get_window_state","type":"assistant","uuid":"de3a320b-b987-4bfb-aee6-dce45c8b867e","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:48:12.320Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"de3a320b-b987-4bfb-aee6-dce45c8b867e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwxNRfr7yAtfAJQbpR1G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Each step now has its own model and budget. Under the hood that's D43, committed as U7 (`dea6edf`) and pushed. The app also says \"engine\" everywhere it used to say \"stack\". All checks and the CodeScene safeguard pass.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Model:** a step can name its own model, and it overrides both the job's model and the server's default.\n- **Revisions:** a step can set how many times its failure may send work back to be fixed. Without a setting it's 2, as before.\n- **Spending limit:** a step can set the most its turns may cost. Once that's spent, Bastion won't start another turn at that step by itself, and the job waits for you instead. Your own retry, note or answer still runs, because the limit restricts the machine, not you.\n- **Editor:** a step's panel shows a model picker (defaulting to \"The job's or the server's model\"), a dollar limit, and the revision count. Shell steps show only the revision count, since they run no model.\n\n**What I checked live**\n- A copy of Short kept all three settings through a save and reload.\n- The test job with DeepSeek set on the plan step landed `quadruple(x)` on `demo-local`.\n- With the plan step set to `anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` and the server's default on DeepSeek, the plan turn's session shows Anthropic. So the step's model wins. I stopped that job after the plan turn.\n- The spending limit and the revision count are covered by tests only. I didn't run them live.\n- Fixed: the model checks pushed a code-health score over its limit, so I moved them into their own function.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **Leftover test workflow:** \"Short, options test\" (`w7d1a5dd3`) is still on `local`. Delete it when you like.\n- **Dev engine restart:** the local dev server's engine needed a restart along the way. Stopping the server stops the engine too, so I started it again through the Engine route.\n- **Bug fix plan step:** its instructions say \"Do not change any file\", but its \"Only reads\" box is unchecked. That's stored data from an earlier conversion, not this change, and I left it alone.\n\n**Next in PLAN.md:**\n1. Step names as `workflow/step`, with constraints and capabilities set per workflow step. This changes D42 and how the gate looks up rules.\n2. Workflows that branch on failure, drawn as flowcharts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2387,"cache_read_input_tokens":681235,"output_tokens":905,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":126},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2387,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":905,"cache_read_input_tokens":681235,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2387},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"cf8492e9-f975-4733-81a0-cb443819260f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwxNRG3yaK6tko6QLyWW","attributionMcpServer":"cmux-cua","attributionMcpTool":"get_window_state","type":"assistant","uuid":"be9839b4-81b5-442d-871e-974eeb05469f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:48:13.074Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
