unction, &call.function) && binds(c, call))\n    };''','''/// Judge one call at a step no workflow names: only the grants for its\n/// kind and the constraints for every step apply.\npub fn gate(\n    call: &Call,\n    stage: Stage,\n    constraints: &[Constraint],\n    grants: &[Capability],\n) -> Verdict {\n    gate_at(call, stage, \"\", constraints, grants)\n}\n\n/// The most specific grant for a call at `step` of kind `stage`: a grant for\n/// the step wins over one for its kind, then an exact function over a\n/// pattern, then the longer pattern.\nfn grant_for<'a>(\n    call: &Call,\n    stage: Stage,\n    step: &str,\n    grants: &'a [Capability],\n) -> Option<&'a Capability> {\n    let fits = |g: &&Capability| {\n        let here = (g.step.is_empty() && g.stage == stage) || (!step.is_empty() && g.step == step);\n        here && matches(&g.function, &call.function)\n    };\n    grants\n        .iter()\n        .filter(fits)\n        .max_by_key(|g| (!g.step.is_empty(), !g.function.ends_with('*'), g.function.len()))\n}\n\n/// Judge one call at `step`, named `workflow/step`, of kind `stage`. A\n/// write to the charter is refused first, then any call an enforced\n/// constraint that applies at the step binds. Then the most specific grant\n/// decides, and a call no grant covers is refused.\npub fn gate_at(\n    call: &Call,\n    stage: Stage,\n    step: &str,\n    constraints: &[Constraint],\n    grants: &[Capability],\n) -> Verdict {\n    let broken = || {\n        constraints.iter().filter(|c| {\n            applies(c, step) && matches(&c.function, &call.function) && binds(c, call)\n        })\n    };'''),\n('''        let grant = grants\n            .iter()\n            .filter(|g| g.stage == stage && matches(&g.function, &call.function))\n            .max_by_key(|g| (!g.function.ends_with('*'), g.function.len()));\n        match grant.map(|g| g.rung) {''','''        match grant_for(call, stage, step, grants).map(|g| g.rung) {'''),\n])\nedit('eval.rs',[('''                .filter(|g| g.stage == *stage && &g.function == function)''','''                .filter(|g| g.step.is_empty() && g.stage == *stage && &g.function == function)''')])\nEOF\ngrep -n \"steps: Vec::new()\\|step: String::new()\" charter.rs govern.rs | wc -l; cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && cargo fmt --all; CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test -p bastion-core 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error|test result|FAILED\" -A4 | head -20","description":"Step-scoped grants and constraints in core","timeout":300000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01XN5Buh912E2Lr5bqydyXmj":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-core/src"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7818d779-4e42-455b-8e12-5582bb0983f0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwyghuH5d9top8XA1d29","type":"assistant","uuid":"cd332d79-c984-477b-84ab-286f7d195545","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:05:34.618Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-core/src","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
