{"parentUuid":"d4fa0de9-fd48-4c38-bc2a-7dc30cbfc79c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bb2fbfce-0794-4784-bb9f-fd3599167038","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019LfDLJFQwduUUm87xSpc4o","type":"tool_result","content":"70:| D44 | A step is known as `workflow/step`. A grant may be for one workflow step, and it wins over the grant for its kind; a constraint may apply at some steps only, and with none named it applies at every step. The gate reads the step from the turn. |\nnote: to see what the problems were, use the option `--future-incompat-report`, or run `cargo report future-incompatibilities --id 1`","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"aeb7be7d-b029-4301-9623-366f147dddfa","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:10:23.959Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"70:| D44 | A step is known as `workflow/step`. A grant may be for one workflow step, and it wins over the grant for its kind; a constraint may apply at some steps only, and with none named it applies at every step. The gate reads the step from the turn. |\nnote: to see what the problems were, use the option `--future-incompat-report`, or run `cargo report future-incompatibilities --id 1`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":67,"oldLines":6,"newStart":67,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D41 | A job ends with its branch ready. When the last step passes, a workspace set to merge merges the branch into its base on the host; one set to leave keeps the branch. |"," | D42 | Governance is per step. A step may change files or only reads, and the gate refuses a write from a step that only reads. Dials, notices, artifacts and evals name steps. |"," | D43 | A step may name its own model and budget. The model wins over the job's and the server's. The budget is how often its failure may send work back (two by default) and the most its turns may cost; past the cost, the factory starts no more turns there by itself, but a person's retry, note or answer still runs. |","+| D44 | A step is known as `workflow/step`. A grant may be for one workflow step, and it wins over the grant for its kind; a constraint may apply at some steps only, and with none named it applies at every step. The gate reads the step from the turn. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":135,"oldLines":10,"newStart":135,"newLines":17,"lines":[" The spending limit and the revision count are covered by tests, not run"," live. The user-facing word \"stack\" is now \"engine\" everywhere."," ","+### U8. Rules per workflow step (D44)","+","+- A step is known as `workflow/step`, and each turn tells the gate which.","+- A grant may be for one workflow step; it wins over its kind's grant.","+- A constraint may apply at some steps only; with none, at every step.","+  An agent is told only the rules that apply at its step.","+- Capabilities lists the steps' own grants with a form to add one, and","+  each constraint shows its steps with a picker to add one.","+"," ## After this plan"," ","-- A step is named `workflow/step`, and constraints and capabilities apply","-  per workflow step, not per kind of step. This changes D42 and the gate."," - Workflows that branch: a step can name a step to go to on failure, so a","   workflow draws as a flowchart. Today a failure waits for you or goes back","   to the step that writes. This changes the core, so it needs a decision"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f4761598-eeae-4894-98e8-b692df1891eb","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":14,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d4fa0de9-fd48-4c38-bc2a-7dc30cbfc79c","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
