{"parentUuid":"812a5fae-b15e-4be4-b4ca-79c200c70bfc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwzQKRMpp4DrgPJ9EZhE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012Yz6EPvLB5DLXGYsSKGteZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i '' \"s/            \\\"At most 2 times a step, within the workspace's revision budget.\\\",/            \\\"As often as each step allows, 2 times by default, within the workspace's revision budget.\\\",/\" crates/bastion-server/src/api/govern.rs && grep -n \"As often as each step\" crates/bastion-server/src/api/govern.rs && cargo fmt --all && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\na='''- Capabilities lists the steps' own grants with a form to add one, and\n  each constraint shows its steps with a picker to add one.\n'''\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,a+'''\nDone 2026-11-11. Migration 6 rebuilt the grants table with the step in\nits key. Live: with `sandbox::fs::write` denied at the test workflow's\nbuild step, the gate refused the build's two writes there; the agent then\nwrote through `sandbox::exec`, which its kind still allows, and the job\nlanded. So a step's grant binds only the function it names: to stop all\nwrites at a step, deny `sandbox::exec` there too. A refusal now names the\nstep. The grant showed under \"For one workflow step\" and its Remove took\nit back.\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nCARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test --workspace 2>&1 | grep -E \"FAILED|panicked\"; cargo fmt --all -- --check && scripts/check-seams.sh | tail -1 && CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A6 | head; git add PLAN.md DECISIONS.md crates","description":"Fix text; record U8; run CI; stage","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":223,"cache_read_input_tokens":762327,"