{"parentUuid":"55a934af-cd48-4d4f-a5b9-6c6cf9bbab6d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwzU2UEy35xebhRKwGcZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":763921,"output_tokens":947,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":191},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":947,"cache_read_input_tokens":763921,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f7b726c2-9be8-4de4-ba03-1a0fda16872f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwzU11gCX1yegRRcSsXM","type":"assistant","uuid":"df2cda04-c1e9-40f6-8fe7-2a5949a30e4f","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:15:41.792Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"df2cda04-c1e9-40f6-8fe7-2a5949a30e4f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwzU2UEy35xebhRKwGcZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Steps now go by `workflow/step` names, and each grant and constraint can be tied to a single workflow step. It's D44, committed as U8 (`eea3ac3`) and pushed. All checks and the CodeScene safeguard pass.\n\n**How it works**\n- **Step name:** every turn tells the gate its step, such as `short/plan`.\n- **Grants:** a grant for one workflow step wins over the grant for its kind of step. When the gate refuses a call, the reason now names the step.\n- **Constraints:** a constraint can apply at only some steps. With none named, it applies at every step, as before. An agent is told only the rules that apply at its step.\n- **Capabilities page:** a new \"For one workflow step\" section lists the steps' own grants, each with Demote, Promote and Remove, plus a form to add one.\n- **Constraints page:** each constraint shows where it applies (\"every step\", or its steps with a ✕ each) and has a picker to add a step.\n- **Database:** migration 6 adds the step to a grant's key. It ran on the dev database.\n\n**Live check, and one thing to know**\nI denied `sandbox::fs::write` at the test workflow's build step, then ran a job on that workflow. The gate refused both of build's file writes at that step. The agent then wrote the file through `sandbox::exec`, which its kind still allows, and the job landed.\n\nSo a step's grant only blocks the function it names. To stop all writes at a step, deny `sandbox::exec` there too. I removed the test grant through the app's Remove button.\n\n**Also fixed:** the factory's text \"at most 2 times a step\" now says each step sets it, 2 by default.\n\n**Last item in PLAN.md: workflows that branch.** This changes how a job moves, so I'd like your call before I build it. My proposal (D45):\n- A link can carry a condition: \"on success\" (the default, as today) or \"on failure\".\n- When a step fails and has an \"on failure\" link, the job goes to that step instead of waiting for you or sending the work back to be fixed.\n- With no \"on failure\" link, nothing changes from today.\n- The canvas draws failure links in red, so a workflow reads as a flowchart.\n- A loop is allowed only on a failure link, and the step's revision count bounds it, so a job can't loop forever.\n\nShould I build it this way?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":763921,"output_tokens":947,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":191},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":947,"cache_read_input_tokens":763921,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f7b726c2-9be8-4de4-ba03-1a0fda16872f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgwzU11gCX1yegRRcSsXM","type":"assistant","uuid":"682973fd-04a5-4f7b-a709-e62b8f8b1f81","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:15:42.533Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
