{"parentUuid":"58661fb6-89fd-4ffe-b383-5b243b652107","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b712eadb-fc3b-498e-ba2d-43adcc2977d0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015YQmKPnhZgLm6UoWVG85iH","type":"tool_result","content":"[This command modified 4 files you've previously read: PLAN.md, DECISIONS.md, VISION.md, README.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"09aab8fe-e6a4-4b1e-88cb-7bedb52ff16e","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:20:45.798Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 4 files you've previously read: PLAN.md, DECISIONS.md, VISION.md, README.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":68,"oldLines":6,"newStart":68,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D42 | Governance is per step. A step may change files or only reads, and the gate refuses a write from a step that only reads. Dials, notices, artifacts and evals name steps. |"," | D43 | A step may name its own model and budget. The model wins over the job's and the server's. The budget is how often its failure may send work back (two by default) and the most its turns may cost; past the cost, the factory starts no more turns there by itself, but a person's retry, note or answer still runs. |"," | D44 | A step is known as `workflow/step`. A grant may be for one workflow step, and it wins over the grant for its kind; a constraint may apply at some steps only, and with none named it applies at every step. The gate reads the step from the turn. |","+| D45 | A step is a prompt, an agent, a skill or a shell script. A repository's command is not a kind of its own: a prompt that reads its file does what it did, and that is what migration 7 makes of each command step. This narrows D39. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":153,"oldLines":6,"newStart":153,"newLines":12,"lines":[" step. The grant showed under \"For one workflow step\" and its Remove took"," it back."," ","+### U9. No command steps (D45)","+","+- A step is a prompt, an agent, a skill or a shell script.","+- Migration 7 turns each command step into a prompt that reads its","+  command's file, and the grants for commands go.","+"," ## After this plan"," "," - Workflows that branch: a step can name a step to go to on failure, so a"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":8,"newStart":2,"newLines":8,"lines":[" "," Bastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work"," it through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph","-of steps that you see on a canvas. Each step is a prompt, an agent, a skill, a","-command or a shell script, each with one text you edit, and each waits for","+of steps that you see on a canvas. Each step is a prompt, an agent, a skill","+or a shell script, each with one text you edit, and each waits for"," your approval or runs on its own, as you set it. Bastion ships the common"," workflows with their text filled in, and every word of them is yours to"," change. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs the factory on"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":33,"oldLines":7,"newStart":33,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **Workspaces:** the repositories it works in, each with its checks, its","   setup, its VM image, and what happens to a job's branch at the end."," - **Workflows:** series of steps. A step is a prompt, one of the","-  repository's agents, skills or commands, or a shell script. Each step has","+  repository's agents or skills, or a shell script. Each step has","   one text to edit, a dial (a sun when a person decides, a moon when it runs","   on its own), and the results it passes on."," - **Capabilities and constraints:** what an agent may call, and the rules"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/README.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"51582364-7fc2-446d-bc99-f0741d5d1eb0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":8,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"58661fb6-89fd-4ffe-b383-5b243b652107","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
