{"parentUuid":"5b645130-276b-4a69-8b10-7496ee43a9c4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx12SCtdT2tauMGGcxRJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XgsYxctS7FBBpwRVHCpLcN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('DECISIONS.md').read()\nlines=s.split('\\n')\nfor k,l in enumerate(lines):\n    if l.startswith('| D39 |'):\n        lines[k]=\"| D39 | A workflow is a series of steps, and nothing else runs. A step is a prompt, an agent (`.agents/agents`), a skill (`.agents/skills`) or a shell script (D45), each with one text. Bastion's built-in stages are gone. |\"\ni=[k for k,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| D45 |')][0]\nlines.insert(i+1,\"| D46 | A repository's charter is `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/`: `.agents/settings.json` holds its permissions and hooks, and `.agents/agents` and `.agents/skills` hold the agents and skills its steps run. Bastion assumes no one vendor's files. The harness, the rules on an agent's calls, is Bastion's own. |\")\nopen('DECISIONS.md','w').write('\\n'.join(lines))\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\na='''## After this plan\n'''\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,'''### U10. The charter is AGENTS.md and .agents/ (D46)\n\n- The charter is `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/settings.json`; `CLAUDE.md` and\n  `.claude/` are no longer read, and a turn may not write `AGENTS.md` or\n  anything under `.agents/`.\n- An agent step reads `.agents/agents/<name>.md`, a skill step\n  `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.\n- The harness, the rules on an agent's calls, stays Bastion's own.\n\n'''+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"D46\\|D39\" DECISIONS.md | cut -c1-120; ls -a /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e/scratchpad/demo-local | head","description":"D39 and D46; U10 in PLAN; inspect demo repo"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"