{"parentUuid":"a2df2fdc-731f-4a7a-b5ca-143691372557","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b712eadb-fc3b-498e-ba2d-43adcc2977d0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016PZevwEzQSUFvqkGxwUJ9i","type":"tool_result","content":"seams ok\n[This command modified 2 files you've previously read: PLAN.md, DECISIONS.md. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2466670e-6b44-4607-af4f-034e0c851756","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:31:50.399Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"seams ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 2 files you've previously read: PLAN.md, DECISIONS.md. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":70,"oldLines":6,"newStart":70,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D44 | A step is known as `workflow/step`. A grant may be for one workflow step, and it wins over the grant for its kind; a constraint may apply at some steps only, and with none named it applies at every step. The gate reads the step from the turn. |"," | D45 | A step is a prompt, an agent, a skill or a shell script. A repository's command is not a kind of its own: a prompt that reads its file does what it did, and that is what migration 7 makes of each command step. This narrows D39. |"," | D46 | A repository's charter is `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/`: `.agents/settings.json` holds its permissions and hooks, and `.agents/agents` and `.agents/skills` hold the agents and skills its steps run. Bastion assumes no one vendor's files. The harness, the rules on an agent's calls, is Bastion's own. |","+| D47 | A link may be a failure link: when its step fails, the job goes along it instead of back to the step that writes. A failure link orders nothing, so it may go back to an earlier step; a step reached only by failure links is skipped otherwise. The failing step's revisions bound any loop, and past them a person decides. A step has at most one failure link. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":180,"oldLines":12,"newStart":180,"newLines":24,"lines":[" rule that denies `git push`. A workspace with only `.claude/` files, such"," as `bastion-gh`, shows no charter until it has `.agents/`."," ","-## After this plan","-","-- Workflows that branch: a step can name a step to go to on failure, so a","-  workflow draws as a flowchart. Today a failure waits for you or goes back","-  to the step that writes. This changes the core, so it needs a decision","-  first.","+### U11. Workflows that branch (D47)","+","+- A link may be a failure link. When its step fails, the job goes along","+  it instead of back to the step that writes.","+- A failure link orders nothing, so it may go back; a step only failure","+  links reach is skipped otherwise.","+- The failing step's revisions bound a loop; past them a person decides.","+- The canvas draws a failure link red and dashed; a picked link has an","+  \"On failure\" box.","+","+Done 2026-11-11. Live, on a copy of Short whose checks exit 1 and whose","+failure link goes to a lights-on `report` step: plan and build ran, the","+checks failed, the job went to `report` instead of back to build,","+`report` ran, and the job waited there; it was stopped so nothing","+landed. The canvas drew the link red and dashed.","+","+Known gap: the job's steps show a step that failed and branched as done,","+as the job keeps no outcome per step."," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e4e7d330-0add-472e-a062-0af21e3d575b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":12,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal"