{"parentUuid":"3ef4a925-ad73-4abc-95b6-efc9ba8db620","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx21UtTJjEmC2u82GKgU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three changes are done, pushed, and CI passed on Linux and macOS for each push.\n\n**Command steps are gone (U9, D45)**\n- A step is now a prompt, an agent, a skill or a shell script.\n- Migration 7 turns each command step into a prompt that reads the command's file, keeping the step's own words. The grants for commands are removed.\n- The tricky part: the stored word `command` meant a shell step before migration 4, and a repository command after it. Each migration now reads it the way its own era meant it.\n- Tested live: a workflow I saved with a command step on the old build came back after migration 7 as a prompt reading `.claude/commands/release-notes.md`.\n\n**The charter is `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/` (U10, D46)**\n- The charter is now `AGENTS.md` plus `.agents/settings.json`. An agent step reads `.agents/agents/<name>.md`, and a skill step reads `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.\n- `CLAUDE.md` and `.claude/` are no longer read. An agent may not write to `AGENTS.md` or anything under `.agents/`.\n- The harness, Bastion's own rules on an agent's calls, is part of the product and unchanged.\n- I applied this to agent and skill steps too, not only the charter, since you didn't want Claude assumed anywhere. Say if you meant the charter only.\n- Tested live: I committed an `AGENTS.md` and an `.agents/settings.json` to my scratch repo `demo-local`, and the server read both, including its \"deny `git push`\" rule.\n- **Your `bastion-gh` workspace** (`~/Code/bastion`) now shows no charter, because it only has `.claude/` files. Its rules come back once it has `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/settings.json`. I didn't touch that repo.\n\n**Workflows can branch (U11, D47)**\n- In the editor, pick a link and tick \"On failure\". The canvas draws it as a red dashed line.\n- When that step fails, the job follows the failure link instead of going back to the step that writes code.\n- A failure link can point back to an earlier step. The failing step's revision count limits the loop, and after that you decide.\n- A step that only failure links lead to is skipped when things succeed.\n- Tested live: in a copy of Short whose checks fail on purpose, the job went from checks to `report` instead of back to build. `report` ran, and the job waited there. I stopped it so nothing landed.\n- **Known gap:** the job page shows a step that failed and branched as \"done\", because the job doesn't yet record each step's outcome. It's noted in PLAN.md.\n\nAll the items in PLAN.md are now done.\n\n**Test leftovers on `local`:** the workflows \"Short, options test\", \"Command test\" and \"Branch test\", and a test commit in `demo-local`. I can delete the workflows when you like."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":775,"cache_read_input_tokens":832143,"output_tokens":954,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":775,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":954,"cache_read_input_tokens":832143,"cache_creation_input_tokens":775,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":775},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5a951daf-d688-4d14-9149-266c940bb243","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgx21UBoBqHjHe55YVJPd","type":"assistant","uuid":"621f257c-9bca-4182-8fd8-8e36c6bf2100","timestamp":"2026-11-11T23:35:55.581Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
