{"parentUuid":"1fa9cc56-90af-421e-a973-985c291cf656","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_016t59jiYhF3CHmyaYCBvhJ5","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7412ecd8-d5e0-4457-ba05-1b25a3bc8cdb","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:23:14.431Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"7412ecd8-d5e0-4457-ba05-1b25a3bc8cdb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx5ct9X7hvdtkj8jjQyq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The workflows page now shows each agent step's constraints and capabilities, and capabilities no longer have \"denied\". It's U13 / D48, committed as `837528a`; CI passed on Linux and macOS.\n\n**On the workflows page** (agent steps only, since a shell step runs no agent):\n- **Constraints:** every constraint that applies at the step, marked \"every step\" or tied to particular steps. A step-tied one has a \"Not here\" button. A picker adds one that's tied to other steps.\n- **Capabilities:** a step uses its kind's grants until you click \"Give this step its own grants\", which copies them as a starting point. From then on, the step's own list replaces its kind's: you can add a grant, promote or demote one, or click \"Use its kind's instead\" to go back.\n\n**No \"denied\" grants:**\n- A grant is now \"ask\" or \"allowed\", and a call that no grant covers is refused.\n- Demoting a grant from \"ask\" removes it; the button reads \"Remove\" at that point.\n- **What changed from U8:** a step's own grants now replace its kind's entirely, rather than overriding them one function at a time. Without \"denied\", that's the only way a step can allow less than its kind does.\n- Migration 8 limits stored grants to \"ask\" and \"allowed\" and drops any \"denied\" ones. Your server had none.\n\n**One guard:** you can't take a constraint off the only step it's tied to, because an empty list means \"every step\". The page says so and points to the Constraints page.\n\n**What I tested live:** on Bug fix's build step, I gave the step its own grants (a copy of `sandbox::*` allowed). Then I demoted it to \"ask\" and removed it, and the step went back to its kind's grants. The audit log recorded all three changes, each with who made it.\n\nThat finishes everything you've asked for so far. Is there anything else you'd like next?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":281,"cache_read_input_tokens":905533,"output_tokens":597,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":281,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":597,"cache_read_input_tokens":905533,"cache_creation_input_tokens":281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":281},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3f93ea68-361b-4010-ba5c-138e198f187e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgx5csT6qN6jibHtYeJwo","type":"assistant","uuid":"05dadeb8-ef11-4692-9df4-a766ca7c21fc","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:23:14.427Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
