{"parentUuid":"074d25d3-43d1-44df-b453-3144504a1d02","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e723e4bd-fa24-4e01-8cef-c0ff7712a74f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018GnH5umEnc1SCihHkPThsw","type":"tool_result","content":"# Voice scenarios\n\n`~/.claude/VOICE.md` is the voice. A scenario tunes it for one kind of writing. Pick one per\npiece, say which, and read its file after VOICE.md. Never blend two.\n\n| Scenario | File |\n|---|---|\n| Practitioner post | `practitioner-post.md` |\n| Essay for anyone | `essay-for-anyone.md` |\n| Technical walkthrough | `technical-walkthrough.md` |\n| Mentor | `mentor.md` |\n| Talk | `talk.md` |\n| Selling without marketing | `selling-without-marketing.md` |\n| Memo to leaders | `memo-to-leaders.md` |\n| Social short | `social-short.md` |\n| Work writing | `work-writing.md` |\n\n## What a scenario may change\nFocus, audience and entry point, the evidence it leads with, emphasis, how casual it gets, length,\nand person targets inside the bands VOICE.md allows.\n\n## What no scenario changes\nHow it should sound (friendly, concise, comprehensible, flowing), the banned list, em dashes at\nzero, never inventing facts or first-person experience, the flow rules, and the Hemingway caps.\nIf a scenario seems to need one of these changed, that's a change to VOICE.md, and it's Ian's call.\n\nFormat files (`post-voice.md`, `book-voice.md` in all-the-things) still own word bands and\nmechanics. A scenario says how a piece should sound; a format file says how long it is and where it ships.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cd549899-7760-491e-8755-33bae4179dc9","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:30:13.544Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Voice scenarios\n\n`~/.claude/VOICE.md` is the voice. A scenario tunes it for one kind of writing. Pick one per\npiece, say which, and read its file after VOICE.md. Never blend two.\n\n| Scenario | File |\n|---|---|\n| Practitioner post | `practitioner-post.md` |\n| Essay for anyone | `essay-for-anyone.md` |\n| Technical walkthrough | `technical-walkthrough.md` |\n| Mentor | `mentor.md` |\n| Talk | `talk.md` |\n| Selling without marketing | `selling-without-marketing.md` |\n| Memo to leaders | `memo-to-leaders.md` |\n| Social short | `social-short.md` |\n| Work writing | `work-writing.md` |\n\n## What a scenario may change\nFocus, audience and entry point, the evidence it leads with, emphasis, how casual it gets, length,\nand person targets inside the bands VOICE.md allows.\n\n## What no scenario changes\nHow it should sound (friendly, concise, comprehensible, flowing), the banned list, em dashes at\nzero, never inventing facts or first-person experience, the flow rules, and the Hemingway caps.\nIf a scenario seems to need one of these changed, that's a change to VOICE.md, and it's Ian's call.\n\nFormat files (`post-voice.md`, `book-voice.md` in all-the-things) still own word bands and\nmechanics. A scenario says how a piece should sound; a format file says how long it is and where it ships.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"11a7e159-7b34-4b18-b9be-47245efbe6ac","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"074d25d3-43d1-44df-b453-3144504a1d02","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
