{"parentUuid":"a09e45bf-2900-40f5-b55f-e4c3e3e66384","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx6EdMmo98AUwXurCVk2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now README.md: the new lede, and \"engine\" in place of \"stack\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1733,"cache_read_input_tokens":915964,"output_tokens":1325,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":64},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1733,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1325,"cache_read_input_tokens":915964,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1733},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a27c7735-4430-4d30-812a-a35bb65a3ba7","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgx6Ecxins6qosaj1oPwv","type":"assistant","uuid":"1d49d9cd-9022-493c-9c3c-242e0b76d6c7","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:31:14.559Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"1d49d9cd-9022-493c-9c3c-242e0b76d6c7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx6EdMmo98AUwXurCVk2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DxxfMw4FV6bmkPkDC5foUH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,(a[:70]); s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep('''Bastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\nit through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph\nof steps that you see on a canvas. Each step is a prompt, an agent, a skill\nor a shell script, each with one text you edit, and each waits for\nyour approval or runs on its own, as you set it. Bastion ships the common\nworkflows with their text filled in, and every word of them is yours to\nchange. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs the factory on\nthe [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop app (on\n[iced](https://iced.rs)) and the `bastion` command line talk to it over HTTP.''','''Bastion is an agent control plane. You define workflows and send requests,\nand Bastion fulfills each request as a job that runs agents through the\nworkflow's steps. A workflow is a graph of steps that you see on a canvas.\nEach step is a prompt, an agent, a skill or a shell script, each with one\ntext you edit, and each step carries its own model, budget and rules. A step\nwaits for your approval or runs on its own, as you set it. Bastion ships the\ncommon workflows with their text filled in, and every word of them is yours\nto change. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs jobs on\nthe [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop app (on\n[iced](https://iced.rs)) and the `bastion` command line talk to it over HTTP.''')\nrep('''The client starts a local server if none runs on port 49190, and the server\nstarts the stack in `worker-compose.yaml`. Go to **Engine** to see Doctor and\nthe stack, then **Jobs** and **New request** to start work.''','''The client starts a local server if none runs on port 49190, and the server\nstarts its engine from `worker-compose.yaml`. Go to **Engine** to see Doctor\nand the engine, then **Jobs** and **New request** to start work.''')\nrep('''- A model provider key, set in **Settings**, which keeps it in the stack's\n  vault. A key in the environment works too.\n- A `GH_TOKEN` in the stack's vault for the workflows that open pull''','''- A model provider key, set in **Settings**, which keeps it in the engine's\n  vault. A key in the environment works too.\n- A `GH_TOKEN` in the engine's vault for the workflows that open pull''')\nrep('''| Core | `crates/bastion-core` | The factory's rules, as pure functions. |''','''| Core | `crates/bastion-core` | The rules a job runs by, as pure functions. |''')\nrep('''| Server | `crates/bastion-server` | The HTTP API and its events, the factory, the store, the gate, the audit and the stack. |''','''| Server | `crates/bastion-server` | The HTTP API and its events, the job runner, the store, the gate, the audit and the engine. |''')\nrep('''CI runs the same on macOS and Linux. The live checks need a running stack:''','''CI runs the same on macOS and Linux. The live checks need a running engine:''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"factory\\|stack\" README.md VISION.md | head","description":"Rewrite README lede and wording"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1733,"cache_read_input_tokens":915964,"output_tokens":1325,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":64},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1733,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1325,"cache_read_input_tokens":915964,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1733},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DxxfMw4FV6bmkPkDC5foUH":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,(a[:70]); s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep('''Bastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\nit through a workflow, and a reviewed change comes out. A workflow is a graph\nof steps that you see on a canvas. Each step is a prompt, an agent, a skill\nor a shell script, each with one text you edit, and each waits for\nyour approval or runs on its own, as you set it. Bastion ships the common\nworkflows with their text filled in, and every word of them is yours to\nchange. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs the factory on\nthe [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop app (on\n[iced](https://iced.rs)) and the `bastion` command line talk to it over HTTP.''','''Bastion is an agent control plane. You define workflows and send requests,\nand Bastion fulfills each request as a job that runs agents through the\nworkflow's steps. A workflow is a graph of steps that you see on a canvas.\nEach step is a prompt, an agent, a skill or a shell script, each with one\ntext you edit, and each step carries its own model, budget and rules. A step\nwaits for your approval or runs on its own, as you set it. Bastion ships the\ncommon workflows with their text filled in, and every word of them is yours\nto change. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs jobs on\nthe [iii](https://iii.dev) engine, and the desktop app (on\n[iced](https://iced.rs)) and the `bastion` command line talk to it over HTTP.''')\nrep('''The client starts a local server if none runs on port 49190, and the server\nstarts the stack in `worker-compose.yaml`. Go to **Engine** to see Doctor and\nthe stack, then **Jobs** and **New request** to start work.''','''The client starts a local server if none runs on port 49190, and the server\nstarts its engine from `worker-compose.yaml`. Go to **Engine** to see Doctor\nand the engine, then **Jobs** and **New request** to start work.''')\nrep('''- A model provider key, set in **Settings**, which keeps it in the stack's\n  vault. A key in the environment works too.\n- A `GH_TOKEN` in the stack's vault for the workflows that open pull''','''- A model provider key, set in **Settings**, which keeps it in the engine's\n  vault. A key in the environment works too.\n- A `GH_TOKEN` in the engine's vault for the workflows that open pull''')\nrep('''| Core | `crates/bastion-core` | The factory's rules, as pure functions. |''','''| Core | `crates/bastion-core` | The rules a job runs by, as pure functions. |''')\nrep('''| Server | `crates/bastion-server` | The HTTP API and its events, the factory, the store, the gate, the audit and the stack. |''','''| Server | `crates/bastion-server` | The HTTP API and its events, the job runner, the store, the gate, the audit and the engine. |''')\nrep('''CI runs the same on macOS and Linux. The live checks need a running stack:''','''CI runs the same on macOS and Linux. The live checks need a running engine:''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"factory\\|stack\" README.md VISION.md | head","description":"Rewrite README lede and wording"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01DxxfMw4FV6bmkPkDC5foUH":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a27c7735-4430-4d30-812a-a35bb65a3ba7","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgx6Ecxins6qosaj1oPwv","type":"assistant","uuid":"3184f649-3516-477d-b057-d1ed65498279","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:31:22.401Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45