{"parentUuid":"d8ed27ff-f003-4fa9-b696-0999d1ad60fc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx6KST69yVju2KFZWoLG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014pEJkSibA7VXfeDYrkcqXb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/memory/bastion-orchestrator-terminology.md","content":"---\nname: bastion-orchestrator-terminology\ndescription: \"Bastion is an agent control plane (owner's call, 2026-11-11); jobs and workflows are its core. Replaces the 2026-11-06 'keep factory words' rule.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e\n  modified: 2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z\n---\n\nBastion is an agent control plane, not a factory. Users define workflows and\nsend requests; jobs fulfill them by running agents through the workflow's\nsteps. Jobs and workflows are the most vital concepts.\n\n**Why:** on 2026-11-11 the owner said \"Bastion is not a factory. It is an\nagent control plane.\" An earlier rebrand to orchestrator/control plane was\nrolled back on 2026-11-06 (commits 7ce2901, df201c9, cc8872e reverted); this\ntime the owner asked for it directly, so it stands. Don't say \"orchestrator\".\n\n**How to apply:** user-facing text says control plane, jobs and workflows.\nThe harness/factory split is history: rules are collapsing onto workflows\nand their steps, and that direction is not settled. The code still has\n`factory` module names; renaming them was not asked for.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":935540,"output_tokens":831,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":831,"cache_read_input_tokens":935540,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014pEJkSibA7VXfeDYrkcqXb":{"file_path":"/Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/memory/bastion-orchestrator-terminology.md","content":"---\nname: bastion-orchestrator-terminology\ndescription: \"Bastion is an agent control plane (owner's call, 2026-11-11); jobs and workflows are its core. Replaces the 2026-11-06 'keep factory words' rule.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e\n  modified: 2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z\n---\n\nBastion is an agent control plane, not a factory. Users define workflows and\nsend requests; jobs fulfill them by running agents through the workflow's\nsteps. Jobs and workflows are the most vital concepts.\n\n**Why:** on 2026-11-11 the owner said \"Bastion is not a factory. It is an\nagent control plane.\" An earlier rebrand to orchestrator/control plane was\nrolled back on 2026-11-06 (commits 7ce2901, df201c9, cc8872e reverted); this\ntime the owner asked for it directly, so it stands. Don't say \"orchestrator\".\n\n**How to apply:** user-facing text says control plane, jobs and workflows.\nThe harness/factory split is history: rules are collapsing onto workflows\nand their steps, and that direction is not settled. The code still has\n`factory` module names; renaming them was not asked for.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"3e030961-9a9b-477d-8f44-fd076f1c6422","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgx6KRs7DKTP1AZo4oWAb","attributionSkill":"humanizer:humanizer","attributionPlugin":"humanizer","type":"assistant","uuid":"a4341bfc-bd40-4423-b0bd-c62980552f93","timesta