estrator\\\" / \\\"agent orchestration control plane\\\" rebrand was tried and rolled back (2026-11-06)\"","+description: \"Bastion is an agent control plane (owner's call, 2026-11-11); jobs and workflows are its core. Replaces the 2026-11-06 'keep factory words' rule.\""," metadata:","   node_type: memory","   type: feedback","   originSessionId: 4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","-  modified: 2026-11-06T23:43:36.621Z","+  modified: 2026-11-12T00:32:24.394Z"," ---"," ","-Keep the factory model and its words: Bastion is a factory, with charter,","-harness and factory as its layers. Do not describe it as an orchestrator or a","-control plane, and do not propose that rebrand again.","+Bastion is an agent control plane, not a factory. Users define workflows and","+send requests; jobs fulfill them by running agents through the workflow's","+steps. Jobs and workflows are the most vital concepts."," ","-**Why:** on 2026-11-06 the owner tried it (D37, three commits), then said","-\"I don't like this. Roll this back, let's continue with the factory model.\"","-The commits were reverted (7ce2901, df201c9, cc8872e).","+**Why:** on 2026-11-11 the owner said \"Bastion is not a factory. It is an","+agent control plane.\" An earlier rebrand to orchestrator/control plane was","+rolled back on 2026-11-06 (commits 7ce2901, df201c9, cc8872e reverted); this","+time the owner asked for it directly, so it stands. Don't say \"orchestrator\"."," ","-**How to apply:** user-facing text, DECISIONS.md and README say factory. Workflows","-(D35) are the factory's workflows.","+**How to apply:** user-facing text says control plane, jobs and workflows.","+The harness/factory split is history: rules are collapsing onto workflows","+and their steps, and that direction is not settled. The code still has","+`factory` module names; renaming them was not asked for."]}],"originalFile":"---\nname: bastion-orchestrator-terminology\ndescription: \"Bastion stays a factory; the \\\"orchestrator\\\" / \\\"agent orchestration control plane\\\" rebrand was tried and rolled back (2026-11-06)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e\n  modified: 2026-11-06T23:43:36.621Z\n---\n\nKeep the factory model and its words: Bastion is a factory, with charter,\nharness and factory as its layers. Do not describe it as an orchestrator or a\ncontrol plane, and do not propose that rebrand again.\n\n**Why:** on 2026-11-06 the owner tried it (D37, three commits), then said\n\"I don't like this. Roll this back, let's continue with the factory model.\"\nThe commits were reverted (7ce2901, df201c9, cc8872e).\n\n**How to apply:** user-facing text, DECISIONS.md and README say factory. Workflows\n(D35) are the factory's workflows.\n","userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a4341bfc-bd40-4423-b0bd-c62980552f93","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
