{"parentUuid":"ea9639b6-88d1-4677-b98a-443919a22440","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx6NBguZEUstVvUkWoGe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VISION.md and README.md now describe Bastion as an agent control plane: you define workflows, send requests, and jobs fulfill them by running agents through the workflow's steps. Both passed the voice check, and they're pushed as `d12acc0`.\n\n**What VISION.md now says**\n- **Lede:** jobs and workflows are the two ideas everything else serves. The cost: a job does only what its workflow says.\n- **Jobs and workflows:** a new section on what a step carries (its dial, model, budget, rules and links) and on how a job runs a request through a workflow.\n- **Rules move onto the workflow:** the harness and factory layers are described as history. Their rules increasingly live on workflows and steps, and Bastion applies them as each step runs. I wrote that the two layers will probably merge into one, but that this isn't settled yet. Your repository's own rules (`AGENTS.md`, `.agents/`) are mentioned there too.\n- **Server sections:** they say \"control plane\" instead of \"factory\", and grants are \"ask or allowed\".\n- **\"Not a hosted service\":** I removed it. My notes say hosting is still an open question, not a non-goal.\n- **Ending:** a concrete next step instead of the old \"Next\" note.\n\n**What README.md now says**\n- A new opening paragraph in the same terms.\n- \"Engine\" instead of \"stack\" throughout.\n- The crate table's Core and Server rows no longer say \"factory\".\n\n**How the writing checks went**\n- **Voice check:** README.md had no stated reader, so the checker asked for first-person asides, which suit an opinion piece. I marked it as an informational doc with a first-person exemption (it's install steps and reference) rather than inventing an aside. VISION.md came in slightly over its first-person limit, so I cut one \"I\".\n- **Tone pass (`/humanizer`):** no changes.\n- **`/slopbeth`:** not installed in this session, so I did that read by hand and found nothing to change.\n- **Final voice check:** both files pass.\n- **CodeScene safeguard:** I didn't run it, because this commit changes only Markdown.\n\n**Memory:** my note that said \"keep factory words\" now says Bastion is an agent control plane, per your call today.\n\n**Still says \"factory\":**\n- `DECISIONS.md`: its opening line (\"Bastion is a software factory you can govern\") and decisions D18, D25 and D37.\n- The code's `factory` module names.\n\nShould I update DECISIONS.md the same way? I'd leave the code names alone unless you want them renamed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":574,"cache_read_input_tokens":937472,"output_tokens":977,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":142},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":574,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":977,"cache_read_input_tokens":937472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":574,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":574},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"86a16960-1cd9-4245-a52d-48183ac93989","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgx6NB7S3s5XzsBXHrSfS","attributionSkill":"humanizer:humanizer","attributionPlugin":"humanizer","type":"assistant","uuid":"b88dcb6e-9ae7-4627-97b6-e11fd01bed6d","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:33:05.162Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d