{"parentUuid":"556cfc58-5f14-4e12-9007-d5e1f3d0c024","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01SEa5NAGpnJUweGP6EZX5Hc","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -n \"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR:-}\" ] && [ -x /bin/zsh ]; then exec /bin/zsh -fc 'LC_ALL=C␤export CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-$PPID}␤export CMUX_AGENT_HOOK_INVOKER_PID=$PPID␤cmux_fallback() { { print -rn -- \"$cmux_p\"; /bin/cat; } | /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3; exit $?; }␤zmodload zsh/system zsh/datetime zsh/files 2>/dev/null || exec /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3␤cmux_p= cmux_c= cmux_e=0␤while (( ${#cmux_p} < 262144 )); do sysread -i 0 -s 65536 cmux_c || { cmux_e=$?; break; }; cmux_p+=$cmux_c; done␤[[ -n ${CMUX_SURFACE_ID:-} && ${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED:-} != 1 ]] || { (( cmux_e == 5 )) || /bin/cat >/dev/null; print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3; exit 0; }␤cmux_d=$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR␤(( cmux_e == 5 )) && [[ -f $cmux_d/keys ]] || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤cmux_r=\"cmux-agent-hook-v1\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"claude\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"$2\"$'\\''\\n'\\''␤for cmux_k in ${(f)\"$(<$cmux_d/keys)\"}; do (( ${+parameters[$cmux_k]} )) && cmux_r+=\"$cmux_k=${(P)cmux_k}\"$'\\''\\0'\\''; done␤cmux_r+=$'\\''\\0'\\''\"$cmux_p\"␤(( ${#cmux_r} <= 524288 )) || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤umask 077␤cmux_n=$cmux_d/$epochtime[1].$epochtime[2]-$$␤{ print -rn -- \"$cmux_r\" >| $cmux_n.tmp && mv -f -- $cmux_n.tmp $cmux_n.rec; } 2>/dev/null || { rm -f -- $cmux_n.tmp 2>/dev/null; cmux_fallback \"$1\"; }␤if zsystem flock -t 0 -r -f cmux_l $cmux_d/forwarder.lock 2>/dev/null; then␤  zsystem flock -u $cmux_l␤  rm -- $cmux_n.rec 2>/dev/null && cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤fi␤print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3' cmux-hook 'cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":56},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c513464c-c342-4bcc-a4df-5f6c5597ef63","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:33:19.398Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"556cfc58-5f14-4e12-9007-d5e1f3d0c024","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1117e70a-bebc-4e39-b3dc-a13e1458fb6a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SEa5NAGpnJUweGP6EZX5Hc","type":"tool_result","content":"# Bastion decisions\n\nBastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\nit through a workflow of steps a person can watch and gate, and a reviewed\nchange comes out. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server`\nruns the factory on the iii engine, and clients such as the iced desktop app\nreach it over HTTP.\n\nThis file holds the goals and the decisions the code cites as\n`DECISIONS.md D<n>`. The plans that built Bastion, phase by phase, are in\ngit history.\n\n## Goals and non-goals\n\n**Goals:**\n\n1. A person sees what every job does and decides what it may do.\n2. A change Bastion lands passed the checks the owner asked for, with the\n   evidence on the job.\n3. A restart, an outage or a lost VM never loses a record or corrupts a job.\n4. Any client and any number of servers, through one API.\n\n**Non-goals for now:** a web client, managed hosting, a plugin system for\ncode-defined guards (rules stay data, per D20 and D26), and a sign-in with a\nClaude subscription (D36). Multi-user servers and hosting stay open\nquestions (below), not non-goals.\n\n## Decisions\n\nEach decision keeps the number the code cites. Numbers not listed were\n3:Bastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\n6:runs the factory on the iii engine, and clients such as the iced desktop app\n45:| D18 | The factory's rules live in `bastion-core`: pure functions from an event and a state to a new state and effects, with no I/O and no `async`. |\n51:| D25 | Every rule belongs to one layer: the charter (the repository's own), the harness (an agent's calls), or the factory (the workflow). |\n63:| D37 | The desktop client is a native Rust app on `iced`. It holds no factory logic and reaches a server only through the client library. |\n69:| D43 | A step may name its own model and budget. The model wins over the job's and the server's. The budget is how often its failure may send work back (two by default) and the most its turns may cost; past the cost, the factory starts no more turns there by itself, but a person's retry, note or answer still runs. |\n78:- **Dark to merge.** ghola never lets a factory merge unattended; Bastion's\n## Open questions\n\n- **Dark to merge.** ghola never lets a factory merge unattended; Bastion's\n  dark dial can run to merge. Should merge always need a person, or a machine\n  verdict, such as the `verify.yaml` contract?\n- **Configuration in git.** ghola keeps configuration in files under review;\n  Bastion keeps it in the database with versions (D26). Should rules also be\n  importable as files, such as team rule packs shared by servers?\n- **Multi-user hosting.** A shared server with people and TLS works today.\n  Is hosted Bastion a goal?\n- **Unused stack workers.** C4 lists them; some may be the harness's\n  dependencies.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"884c565c-0de5-435b-8d2d-af778a6edb36","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:33:20.317Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Bastion decisions\n\nBastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\nit through a workflow of steps a person can watch and gate, and a reviewed\nchange comes out. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server`\nruns the factory on the iii engine, and clients such as the iced desktop app\nreach it over HTTP.\n\nThis file holds the goals and the decisions the code cites as\n`DECISIONS.md D<n>`. The plans that built Bastion, phase by phase, are in\ngit history.\n\n## Goals and non-goals\n\n**Goals:**\n\n1. A person sees what every job does and decides what it may do.\n2. A change Bastion lands passed the checks the owner asked for, with the\n   evidence on the job.\n3. A restart, an outage or a lost VM never loses a record or corrupts a job.\n4. Any client and any number of servers, through one API.\n\n**Non-goals for now:** a web client, managed hosting, a plugin system for\ncode-defined guards (rules stay data, per D20 and D26), and a sign-in with a\nClaude subscription (D36). Multi-user servers and hosting stay open\nquestions (below), not non-goals.\n\n## Decisions\n\nEach decision keeps the number the code cites. Numbers not listed were\n3:Bastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\n6:runs the factory on the iii engine, and clients such as the iced desktop app\n45:| D18 | The factory's rules live in `bastion-core`: pure functions from an event and a state to a new state and effects, with no I/O and no `async`. |\n51:| D25 | Every rule belongs to one layer: the charter (the repository's own), the harness (an agent's calls), or the factory (the workflow). |\n63:| D37 | The desktop client is a native Rust app on `iced`. It holds no factory logic and reaches a server only through the client library. |\n69:| D43 | A step may name its own model and budget. The model wins over the job's and the server's. The budget is how often its failure may send work back (two by default) and the most its turns may cost; past the cost, the factory starts no more turns there by itself, but a person's retry, note or answer still runs. |\n78:- **Dark to merge.** ghola never lets a factory merge unattended; Bastion's\n## Open questions\n\n- **Dark to merge.** ghola never lets a factory merge unattended; Bastion's\n  dark dial can run to merge. Should merge always need a person, or a machine\n  verdict, such as the `verify.yaml` contract?\n- **Configuration in git.** ghola keeps configuration in files under review;\n  Bastion keeps it in the database with versions (D26). Should rules also be\n  importable as files, such as team rule packs shared by servers?\n- **Multi-user hosting.** A shared server with people and TLS works today.\n  Is hosted Bastion a goal?\n- **Unused stack workers.** C4 lists them; some may be the harness's\n  dependencies.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6a76d250-cb42-426c-a723-45b97c98b579","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"556cfc58-5f14-4e12-9007-d5e1f3d0c024","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
