{"parentUuid":"e2ec9b29-5433-4adb-859f-262227501c7c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx6Q5c6aemPykiQeXqwS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qb1wUeNXznCrdQmAfr11RZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,(a[:70]); s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep('''Bastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\nit through a workflow of steps a person can watch and gate, and a reviewed\nchange comes out. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server`\nruns the factory on the iii engine, and clients such as the iced desktop app\nreach it over HTTP.''','''Bastion is an agent control plane. You define workflows and send requests,\nand Bastion fulfills each request as a job: agents work through the\nworkflow's steps, which a person can watch and gate, and the job ends with\nits branch ready. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs\njobs on the iii engine, and clients such as the iced desktop app reach it\nover HTTP.''')\nrep('''| D18 | The factory's rules live in `bastion-core`:''','''| D18 | The rules a job runs by live in `bastion-core`:''')\nrep('''| D25 | Every rule belongs to one layer: the charter (the repository's own), the harness (an agent's calls), or the factory (the workflow). |''','''| D25 | Every rule belongs to one layer: the charter (the repository's own), the harness (an agent's calls), or the factory (the workflow). Under review: the harness's and the factory's rules are moving onto workflows and their steps (see the open questions). |''')\nrep('''It holds no factory logic and reaches a server''','''It holds no job or workflow logic and reaches a server''')\nrep('''past the cost, the factory starts no more turns there by itself''','''past the cost, Bastion starts no more turns there by itself''')\nrep('''- **Unused stack workers.** C4 lists them; some may be the harness's\n  dependencies.''','''- **Unused engine workers.** C4 lists them; some may be the harness's\n  dependencies.\n- **Harness and factory.** D25's two layers are collapsing onto workflows\n  and their steps: a step's grants, constraints, model and budget all live\n  on the step. Should the split stay, or should Bastion apply everything\n  from the settings of a workflow and its steps?''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"factory\" DECISIONS.md; python3 ~/.claude/skills/voice-check/voicecheck.py DECISIONS.md --corpus ~/tacoda/tacoda.github.io 2>&1 | sed -n '1,12p'","description":"Update DECISIONS wording; voice-check","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1148,"cache_read_input_tokens":939204,"output_tokens":1605,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":608},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1148,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1605,"cache_read_input_tokens":939204,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1148},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Qb1wUeNXznCrdQmAfr11RZ":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,(a[:70]); s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep('''Bastion is a software factory you can govern. A request goes in, agents work\nit through a workflow of steps a person can watch and gate, and a reviewed\nchange comes out. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server`\nruns the factory on the iii engine, and clients such as the iced desktop app\nreach it over HTTP.''','''Bastion is an agent control plane. You define workflows and send requests,\nand Bastion fulfills each request as a job: agents work through the\nworkflow's steps, which a person can watch and gate, and the job ends with\nits branch ready. Bastion is a server and its clients: `bastion-server` runs\njobs on the iii engine, and clients such as the iced desktop app reach it\nover HTTP.''')\nrep('''| D18 | The factory's rules live in `bastion-core`:''','''| D18 | The rules a job runs by live in `bastion-core`:''')\nrep('''| D25 | Every rule belongs to one layer: the charter (the repository's own), the harness (an agent's calls), or the factory (the workflow). |''','''| D25 | Every rule belongs to one layer: the charter (the repository's own), the harness (an agent's calls), or the factory (the workflow). Under review: the harness's and the factory's rules are moving onto workflows and their steps (see the open questions). |''')\nrep('''It holds no factory logic and reaches a server''','''It holds no job or workflow logic and reaches a server''')\nrep('''past the cost, the factory starts no more turns there by itself''','''past the cost, Bastion starts no more turns there by itself''')\nrep('''- **Unused stack workers.** C4 lists them; some may be the harness's\n  dependencies.''','''- **Unused engine workers.** C4 lists them; some may be the harness's\n  dependencies.\n- **Harness and factory.** D25's two layers are collapsing onto workflows\n  and their steps: a step's grants, constraints, model and budget all live\n  on the step. Should the split stay, or should Bastion apply everything\n  from the settings of a workflow and its steps?''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"factory\" DECISIONS.md; python3 ~/.claude/skills/voice-check/voicecheck.py DECISIONS.md --corpus ~/tacoda/tacoda.github.io 2>&1 | sed -n '1,12p'","description":"Update DECISIONS wording; voice-check","timeout":120000}},"wireIngestC