X_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ed940a62-3e10-45b6-98d5-f1c8ba0817ee","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:51:48.259Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"1a9a74e7-cdcb-4759-af3b-9061b6054759","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"63076884-86c8-4719-937e-cb437c55717e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SAM9fpBn5HN6rvTaECSUUo","type":"tool_result","content":"19:| N3 | pass | 2026-10-30 | Three runs in a row: Rust binds `harness::turn-completed`, and a `pre-trigger` hook rewrites `sandbox_id` on `sandbox::fs::read`. 5.7 s, 3.5 s, 3.5 s. The earlier failure, under the old name, did not recur, and its cause is unknown. |\n31:| N7 | pass | 2026-10-30 | Two runs, 6.7 s and 5.9 s: `worktree::create` made a worktree of a scratch repo, its branch went into a fresh VM as a git bundle (`sandbox::fs::write` with `content_b64`), one `harness` turn on gpt-5-mini committed there through `sandbox::exec` pinned by the `pre-trigger` hook, and the 377-byte bundle came back through the content channel and fast-forwarded the worktree. `content_b64` is for small files; a large repo needs a channel upload. The spike's cleanup sent the wrong id field to `worktree::remove`, which left one scratch worktree registered. |\n37:| N8 | pass | 2026-10-31 | A `harness::hook::pre-trigger` binding answers `{ \"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": … }` or `{ \"decision\": \"hold\", … }`. A denied call's reason reaches the turn verbatim as its result. A held call parks the turn (status stays `running`), and the envelope carries `session_id`, `turn_id` and `call.id`. `harness::function::resolve` takes `session_id`, `turn_id`, `function_call_id`, `action` (`deliver` or `execute`), `content`, `details` and `is_error`; an unknown field such as `mode` is ignored and the default `deliver` sends an empty result. The held arguments arrive without the hook's `sandbox_id` mutation, so on approval the app runs the call itself, pinned to the job's VM, and delivers the result. `harness::stop` exists and answers `{ \"stopping\": … }`. One run: the model gave up after the deny until told to make the second call anyway. |\n43:| N9 | partial | 2026-10-31 | `judge::evaluate` lives in namespace `bastion` and answers `{ \"status\": \"error\", \"code\": \"provider_unavailable\" }`: the stack has the `judge` worker but no `judge-<provider>` worker, so it has no model to grade with. Bastion grades with a harness turn that has no tools instead, and reads its last `GRADE: n` line. `harness::metrics` with `root_session_id` gives each session's `turns`, `function_calls`, `function_call_errors` and `cost_usd`, which the eval tallies. The stock `eval` worker analyzes finished harness sessions; it does not compare two configurations. `worktree::create` takes a commit as `base_ref`, so an eval pins its snapshot as a commit. |\n57:| N13 | pass | 2026-11-06 | A provider key can live in the stack's `secrets` vault and reach `llm-router` with no key in the stack's environment (D34). `secrets::detect` found `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` only in the login shell; `secrets::import` with `source: login_shell`, `store: vault` and `consumers: [\"llm-router\"]` stored it (the worker reads the value itself, so it never passes through the caller) and returned only a masked hint and `secret://ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. `configuration::set` on `bastion-llm-router` with `providers.anthropic.api_key = \"REDACTED\"` turned `router::provider::list` for Anthropic from `credential_source: none` to `secret`, `configured: true`, default model `claude-sonnet-5-5`. A job with the plan stage on `claude-haiku-5-5` then ran its plan turn and reached Approve. The router's entry was `null` before, so a set replaces the whole value: Bastion must read, change one provider and write back. `providers.openai.api_url` reaches another host: pointed at a local recorder ending in `/v1/chat/completions`, `provider-openai` sent Chat Completions (`messages`, `tools`, `stream`, `max_completion_tokens`, `reasoning_effort`, `prompt_cache_key`) with the key as a bearer token, and also sent `/v1/embeddings` to the same base. So one compatible host can stand in for OpenAI, but not beside it, and a host that lacks embeddings or rejects `reasoning_effort` or `prompt_cache_key` would fail; K3's worker stays. The function list carries no request schemas, so payloads were found from the workers' errors. Spike: `n13_keys.rs`. |\n33:const TOOLS: [&str; 4] = [\n34-    \"sandbox::exec\",\n35-    \"sandbox::fs::read\",\n36-    \"sandbox::fs::write\",\n37-    \"sandbox::fs::ls\",\n38-];\n39-const REPO: &str = \"/work/repo\";\n40-\n41-/// Where a request came from, and the workflow it runs.\n42-#[derive(Default)]\n43-pub struct Submission {\n44-    /// The tracker issue it came from, as its URL.\n45-    pub issue: Option<String>,\n--\n731:                \"options\": { \"max_turns\": MAX_TURN_STEPS, \"functions\": { \"allow\": TOOLS }, \"metadata\": { \"sandbox_id\": sandbox, \"job\": job.id, \"stage\": stage, \"step\": step, \"reads_only\": job.step().is_some_and(|s| s.reach.reads_only) } },\n732-            }), 60_000)\n733-            .await?;\n734-        self.arm_cap(&turn, bastion_core::TURN_CAP_SECS);\n735-        Ok(())\n736-    }\n737-\n738-    /// When an effect failed, tell the core: the VM is gone, or `failed`.\n739-    async fn report_failure(\n740-        self: &Arc<Self>,\n741-        id: &str,\n742-        result: Result<(), String>,\n743-        failed: impl FnOnce(String) -> Event,","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c5fcabc3-6db4-4eb6-8740-74f3d5f716dd","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:51:48.785Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"19:| N3 | pass | 2026-10-30 | Three runs in a row: Rust binds `harness::turn-completed`, and a `pre-trigger` hook rewrites `sandbox_id` on `sandbox::fs::read`. 5.7 s, 3.5 s, 3.5 s. The earlier failure, under the old name, did not recur, and its cause is unknown. |\n31:| N7 | pass | 2026-10-30 | Two runs, 6.7 s and 5.9 s: `worktree::create` made a worktree of a scratch repo, its branch went into a fresh VM as a git bundle (`sandbox::fs::write` with `content_b64`), one `harness` turn on gpt-5-mini committed there t