-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":53},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fe6610e1-ad18-404b-8826-aaec394ffb50","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:52:07.999Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"f0b2758a-028c-4103-99ee-b400838ea4a2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"63076884-86c8-4719-937e-cb437c55717e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNFtzJq1XPzcW9ix2449W9","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### harness::send\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/tech-specs/2026-06-08-agentic/harness.md\n\nAccepts an incoming message, ensures the session, appends the user message, and enqueues the first turn step. Returns before the turn runs. If a turn is already running, the message is appended and folded into it instead.\n\n```APIDOC\n## harness::send\n\n### Description\nAccept an incoming message, ensure the session, append the user message, and enqueue the first turn step. Returns before the turn runs. If a turn is already running for the session, the message is appended and folded into it instead — no second turn starts.\n\n### Invocation\n- **Sync** (kicks an async/enqueued loop)\n\n### Request\n\n```typescript\ntype SendRequest = {\n  session_id?: string;            // omit to create a new session\n  message: AgentMessage | string; // string is sugar for a user text message;\n                                  // role must be \"user\" or \"custom\" (else harness/invalid_message_role).\n                                  // \"custom\" content never reaches the model (no wire mapping) —\n                                  // such a send kicks a turn over the existing history only\n  model: string;\n  provider?: string;\n  idempotency_key?: string;       // webhook dedupe: a repeated key returns the original\n                                  // {session_id, turn_id} and appends nothing\n  session?: {                     // applied when this send creates/ensures the session\n    title?: string;\n    metadata?: Record<string, unknown>; // -> SessionMeta.metadata (the tenancy hook)\n  };\n  options?: {\n    system_prompt?: string;\n    max_turns?: number;           // default 16\n    thinking_level?: ThinkingLevel;\n    output?: OutputContract;      // the turn's deliverable; default { type: \"text\" } (see Output contract)\n    functions?: {\n      allow?: string[];           // function_id globs the agent may dispatch to (e.g. \"shell::*\")\n      deny?: string[];\n      expose?: \"agent_trigger\" | \"native\"; // default \"agent_trigger\" (see Functions (the white box))\n    };\n    metadata?: Record<string, unknown>; // tracing passthrough (session_id/message_id propagate)\n  };\n};\n```\n\n### Response\n\n```typescript\ntype SendResponse = {\n  session_id: string;\n  turn_id: string;     // the new turn — or the running turn when merged\n  accepted: true;\n  merged?: boolean;    // true when folded into an in-flight turn (steering)\n  deduplicated?: boolean; // true when idempotency_key matched an earlier send\n};\n```\n\n### Example\n\n```jsonc\n// request\n{ \"message\": \"Summarise the repo README\", \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\", \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n  \"options\": { \"functions\": { \"allow\": [\"shell::*\", \"fs::*\"] } } }\n// response\n{ \"session_id\": \"s_7a1\", \"turn_id\": \"t_001\", \"accepted\": true }\n```\n\n### Idempotency\nWebhook sources redeliver (Telegram updates, Slack retries). When `idempotency_key` is set, the user entry id derives from it (the duplicate append is a no-op) and the key maps to the `{ session_id, turn_id }` it first produced (see State, TTL-bound); a redelivered send returns the same response with `deduplicated: true` and changes nothing.\n\n### Sessions\n`session.metadata` lands on `SessionMeta.metadata` when the send creates/ensures the session — the tenancy hook session trigger configs and `session::list` filter on.\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Conventions > Terminology\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/tech-specs/2026-06-08-agentic/README.md\n\nIn iii there is no \"tool\" worker or domain concept — everything callable is a **function** registered\nvia `iii.registerFunction` and invoked via `iii.trigger`. Message content uses **function_call** and\n**function_result** blocks.\n\nThe one exception is at the **provider adapter boundary**: OpenAI, Anthropic, and similar APIs expose\na `tools` array for function-calling. `llm-router` translates our invocation schema into that wire\nformat. In the harness loop the model sees a **single** provider tool by default — `agent_trigger`,\nwhich takes `{ function, payload }` and can reach any allowed iii function — or one schema per\nallowed function when a turn opts into `functions.expose: \"native\"`. See\n[harness.md § Functions (the white box)](harness.md#functions-the-white-box).\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Consider the agent\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/website/content/blog/add-a-worker.md\n\nAn agent needs to speak MCP to an external tool server. **Add a worker** that\nbridges MCP into `trigger()` calls. The bridge is a worker like any other.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### AgentFunction type for provider function-calling (TypeScript)\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/tech-specs/2026-06-08-agentic/README.md\n\nJSON-schema shape for a provider function-calling entry. `llm-router` passes this as a `tools` array entry at the adapter boundary. In the harness loop, this is a single entry for `agent_trigger` by default; with `functions.expose: \"native\"` it attaches one entry per allowed function.\n\n```typescript\ntype AgentFunction = {\n  name: string;            // invocation surface name (\"agent_trigger\", \"submit_result\", or a\n                           // function id in native exposure mode)\n  description: string;\n  parameters: unknown;     // JSON Schema: { function: string, payload?: object }\n  label?: string;\n  execution_mode?: \"parallel\" | \"sequential\";\n};\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### harness::send request/response example\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/tech-specs/2026-06-08-agentic/harness.md\n\nExample request and response for harness::send. The request sends a user message with model claude-sonnet-4, provider anthropic, and allows shell::* and fs::* functions. The response shows the accepted session and turn IDs.\n\n```jsonc\n// request\n{ \"message\": \"Summarise the repo README\", \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\", \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n  \"options\": { \"functions\": { \"allow\": [\"shell::*\", \"fs::*\"] } } }\n// response\n{ \"session_id\": \"s_7a1\", \"turn_id\": \"t_001\", \"accepted\": true }\n```"}]}]},"uuid":"212e5bdb-5846-4e5b-bd7f-06f4882c84bd","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:52:10.191Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"### harness::send\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/tech-specs/2026-06-08-agentic/harness.md\n\nAccepts an incoming message, ensures the session, appends the user message, and enqueues the first turn step. Returns before the turn runs. If a turn is already running, the message is appended and folded into it instead.\n\n```APIDOC\n## harness::send\n\n### Description\nAccept an incoming message, ensure the session, append the user message, and enqueue the first turn step. Returns before the turn runs. If a turn is already running for the session, the message is appended and folded into it instead — no second turn starts.\n\n### Invocation\n- **Sync** (kicks an async/enqueued loop)\n\n### Request\n\n```typescript\ntype SendRequest = {\n  session_id?: string;            // omit to create a new session\n  message: AgentMessage | string; // string is sugar for a user text message;\n                                  // role must be \"user\" or \"custom\" (else harness/invalid_message_role).\n                                  // \"custom\" content never reaches the model (no wire mapping) —\n                                  // such a send kicks a turn over the existing history only\n  model: string;\n  provider?: string;\n  idempotency_key?: string;       // webhook dedupe: a repeated key returns the original\n                                  // {session_id, turn_id} and appends nothing\n  session?: {                     // applied when this send creates/ensures the session\n    title?: string;\n    metadata?: Record<string, unknown>; // -> SessionMeta.metadata (the tenancy hook)\n  };\n  options?: {\n    system_prompt?: string;\n    max_turns?: number;           // default 16\n    thinking_level?: ThinkingLevel;\n    output?: OutputContract;      // the turn's deliverable; default { type: \"text\" } (see Output contract)\n    functions?: {\n      allow?: string[];           // function_id globs the agent may dispatch to (e.g. \"shell::*\")\n      deny?: string[];\n      expose?: \"agent_trigger\" | \"native\"; // default \"agent_trigger\" (see Functions (the white box))\n    };\n    metadata?: Record<string, unknown>; // tracing passthrough (session_id/message_id propagate)\n  };\n};\n```\n\n### Response\n\n```typescript\ntype SendResponse = {\n  session_id: string;\n  turn_id: string;     // the new turn — or the running turn when merged\n  accepted: true;\n  merged?: boolean;    // true when folded into an in-flight turn (steering)\n  deduplicated?: boolean; // true when idempotency_key matched an earlier send\n};\n```\n\n### Example\n\n```jsonc\n// request\n{ \"message\": \"Summarise the repo README\", \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\", \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n  \"options\": { \"functions\": { \"allow\": [\"shell::*\", \"fs::*\"] } } }\n// response\n{ \"session_id\": \"s_7a1\", \"turn_id\": \"t_001\", \"accepted\": true }\n```\n\n### Idempotency\nWebhook sources redeliver (Telegram updates, Slack retries). When `idempotency_key` is set, the user entry id derives from it (the duplicate append is a no-op) and the key maps to the `{ session_id, turn_id }` it first produced (see State, TTL-bound); a redelivered send returns the same response with `deduplicated: true` and changes nothing.\n\n### Sessions\n`session.metadata` lands on `SessionMeta.metadata` when the send creates/ensures the session — the tenancy hook session trigger configs and `session::list` filter on.\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Conventions > Terminology\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/tech-specs/2026-06-08-agentic/README.md\n\nIn iii there is no \"tool\" worker or domain concept — everything callable is a **function** registered\nvia `iii.registerFunction` and invoked via `iii.trigger`. Message content uses **function_call** and\n**function_result** blocks.\n\nThe one exception is at the **provider adapter boundary**: OpenAI, Anthropic, and similar APIs expose\na `tools` array for function-calling. `llm-router` translates our invocation schema into that wire\nformat. In the harness loop the model sees a **single** provider tool by default — `agent_trigger`,\nwhich takes `{ function, payload }` and can reach any allowed iii function — or one schema per\nallowed function when a turn opts into `functions.expose: \"native\"`. See\n[harness.md § Functions (the white box)](harness.md#functions-the-white-box).\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Consider the agent\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/website/content/blog/add-a-worker.md\n\nAn agent needs to speak MCP to an external tool server. **Add a worker** that\nbridges MCP into `trigger()` calls. The bridge is a worker like any other.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### AgentFunction type for provider function-calling (TypeScript)\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/tech-specs/2026-06-08-agentic/README.md\n\nJSON-schema shape for a provider function-calling entry. `llm-router` passes this as a `tools` array entry at the adapter boundary. In the harness loop, this is a single entry for `agent_trigger` by default; with `functions.expose: \"native\"` it attaches one entry per allowed function.\n\n```typescript\ntype AgentFunction = {\n  name: string;            // invocation surface name (\"agent_trigger\", \"submit_result\", or a\n                           // function id in native exposure mode)\n  description: string;\n  parameters: unknown;     // JSON Schema: { function: string, payload?: object }\n  label?: string;\n  execution_mode?: \"parallel\" | \"sequential\";\n};\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### harness::send request/response example\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/tech-specs/2026-06-08-agentic/harness.md\n\nExample request and response for harness::send. The request sends a user message with model claude-sonnet-4, provider anthropic, and allows shell::* and fs::* functions. The response shows the accepted session and turn IDs.\n\n```jsonc\n// request\n{ \"message\": \"Summarise the repo README\", \"model\": \"claude-sonnet-4\", \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n  \"options\": { \"functions\": { \"allow\": [\"shell::*\", \"fs::*\"] } } }\n// response\n{ \"session_id\": \"s_7a1\", \"turn_id\": \"t_001\", \"accepted\": true }\n```"}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f48a2881-1a1e-44cb-887f-793ea15b270f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Context7","title":"Context7","icons":[{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.svg","mimeType":"image/svg+xml","sizes":["any"]},{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.png","mimeType":"image/png","sizes":["512x512"]}],"version":"4.5.0","websiteUrl":"https://context7.com","description":"Context7 provides up-to-date documentation and code examples for libraries and frameworks."}}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f0b275