{"parentUuid":"ad043bab-e82d-4c50-b2bf-d3a08237e5ff","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:mcp__context7__query-docs","toolUseID":"toolu_012eLuoChpHW8MVLvxh2JGjs","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -n \"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR:-}\" ] && [ -x /bin/zsh ]; then exec /bin/zsh -fc 'LC_ALL=C␤export CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-$PPID}␤export CMUX_AGENT_HOOK_INVOKER_PID=$PPID␤cmux_fallback() { { print -rn -- \"$cmux_p\"; /bin/cat; } | /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3; exit $?; }␤zmodload zsh/system zsh/datetime zsh/files 2>/dev/null || exec /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3␤cmux_p= cmux_c= cmux_e=0␤while (( ${#cmux_p} < 262144 )); do sysread -i 0 -s 65536 cmux_c || { cmux_e=$?; break; }; cmux_p+=$cmux_c; done␤[[ -n ${CMUX_SURFACE_ID:-} && ${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED:-} != 1 ]] || { (( cmux_e == 5 )) || /bin/cat >/dev/null; print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3; exit 0; }␤cmux_d=$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR␤(( cmux_e == 5 )) && [[ -f $cmux_d/keys ]] || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤cmux_r=\"cmux-agent-hook-v1\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"claude\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"$2\"$'\\''\\n'\\''␤for cmux_k in ${(f)\"$(<$cmux_d/keys)\"}; do (( ${+parameters[$cmux_k]} )) && cmux_r+=\"$cmux_k=${(P)cmux_k}\"$'\\''\\0'\\''; done␤cmux_r+=$'\\''\\0'\\''\"$cmux_p\"␤(( ${#cmux_r} <= 524288 )) || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤umask 077␤cmux_n=$cmux_d/$epochtime[1].$epochtime[2]-$$␤{ print -rn -- \"$cmux_r\" >| $cmux_n.tmp && mv -f -- $cmux_n.tmp $cmux_n.rec; } 2>/dev/null || { rm -f -- $cmux_n.tmp 2>/dev/null; cmux_fallback \"$1\"; }␤if zsystem flock -t 0 -r -f cmux_l $cmux_d/forwarder.lock 2>/dev/null; then␤  zsystem flock -u $cmux_l␤  rm -- $cmux_n.rec 2>/dev/null && cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤fi␤print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3' cmux-hook 'cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":60},"type":"attachment","uuid":"22640542-ecab-4993-9971-8084c8b94a02","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:52:19.578Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"ad043bab-e82d-4c50-b2bf-d3a08237e5ff","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"63076884-86c8-4719-937e-cb437c55717e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012eLuoChpHW8MVLvxh2JGjs","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Consider the agent\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/website/content/blog/add-a-worker.md\n\nAn agent needs to speak MCP to an external tool server. **Add a worker** that\nbridges MCP into `trigger()` calls. The bridge is a worker like any other.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### registerWorker\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/reference/sdk-browser.mdx.skill.md\n\nRegisters a worker with a iii instance and returns a connected worker client. The WebSocket connection is established automatically.\n\n```APIDOC\n## registerWorker\n\n### Description\nRegisters the worker with a iii instance, returns a connected worker client. The WebSocket connection is established automatically.\n\n### Signature\n```typescript\nregisterWorker(address: string, options?: InitOptions) => ISdk\n```\n\n### Parameters\n#### address (string) - Required\nWebSocket URL of the III engine (e.g. `ws://localhost:49135`).\n\n#### options (InitOptions) - Optional\nOptional InitOptions for worker name, timeouts, and reconnection.\n\n##### InitOptions fields:\n- **headers** (Record<string, string>) - Optional - Browser WebSocket connections authenticate via query parameters or cookies; the `headers` option is ignored.\n- **invocationTimeoutMs** (number) - Optional - Default timeout for `worker.trigger()` invocations in milliseconds. Defaults to `30000`.\n- **namespace** (string) - Optional - Namespace this worker registers under. When omitted the engine applies its `default` namespace. Scopes worker and function registrations so identically-named entries can coexist across namespaces. The browser has no `process.env`, so there is no environment-variable fallback -- pass the option explicitly.\n- **reconnectionConfig** (Partial<IIIReconnectionConfig>) - Optional - WebSocket reconnection behavior.\n- **workerName** (string) - Optional - Name this worker announces to the engine. Defaults to a unique `browser:<random>` per client: a browser has no pid to disambiguate by, and the engine allows only one live worker per name in a namespace, so two tabs sharing a fixed name would evict each other.\n\n### Example\n```typescript\nimport { registerWorker } from 'iii-browser-sdk'\n\nconst worker = registerWorker('ws://localhost:49135')\n```\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Types > iii_sdk > InitOptions\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/reference/sdk-rust.mdx.skill.md\n\nConfiguration options passed to `register_worker`.\n\n| Name | Type | Required | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `metadata` | Option&lt;iii::[`WorkerMetadata`](#workermetadata)&gt; | No | Custom worker metadata. Auto-detected if `None`. |\n| `headers` | `Option<HashMap<String, String>>` | No | Custom HTTP headers sent during the WebSocket handshake. |\n| `otel` | `Option<iii_helpers::observability::OtelConfig>` | No | OpenTelemetry configuration. |\n| `namespace` | `Option<String>` | No | Namespace this worker belongs to. Resolution order:<br />`namespace` > env `III_NAMESPACE` > `None` (the engine then applies its<br />default namespace). Mirrors the `III_WORKER_NAME` precedence.<br /><br />It scopes more than the registration. The worker and its functions<br />register here, and everything the worker does afterwards follows it: a<br />`IIIClient::trigger` resolves its target here and a<br />`IIIClient::register_trigger` binds here, unless the call names<br />another namespace. |\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Category collapse\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/website/content/blog/building-agents-for-real-world.md\n\n## Category collapse\n\nOnce Worker is the primitive, categories that used to be separate runtimes collapse into the same vocabulary.\n\nSandbox provider is a worker. The 40+ providers we've mapped (E2B, Daytona, Modal, Vercel sandbox and the rest) all express as workers with sandbox-shaped functions. The choice of provider becomes a registry swap rather than an integration rewrite.\n\nBrowser tab is a worker. `iii-browser-sdk` runs on port 49135 and registers the tab as a worker the engine can address. Browser-side events are triggers. DOM operations are functions. The page becomes part of the same execution graph as the backend.\n\nExternal agent is a worker via the A2A protocol. MCP server is a worker via the MCP bridge. The agent itself is a peer worker, not a privileged consumer of tools. The \"agent calls tools\" mental model collapses into \"worker calls function on another worker.\"\n\nIntegration cost goes from quadratic to linear. Each new capability is one registry entry instead of an integration with every consumer. Each new consumer reads from the registry instead of a custom integration per provider.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### register_worker\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/reference/sdk-rust.mdx\n\nRegisters a worker with the III engine and returns a client for further operations. Accepts an address and initialization options.\n\n```APIDOC\n## register_worker\n\n### Description\nRegisters a worker with the III engine and returns a client for further operations.\n\n### Signature\n```rust\nregister_worker(address: &str, options: InitOptions) -> IIIClient\n```\n\n### Parameters\n- **address** (`&str`) - Required - The address of the worker.\n- **options** (`InitOptions`) - Required - Initialization options.\n\n#### InitOptions fields\n- **metadata** (`Option<iii::WorkerMetadata>`) - Custom worker metadata. Auto-detected if `None`.\n- **headers** (`Option<HashMap<String, String>>`) - Custom HTTP headers sent during the WebSocket handshake.\n- **otel** (`Option<iii_helpers::observability::OtelConfig>`) - OpenTelemetry configuration.\n- **namespace** (`Option<String>`) - Namespace this worker belongs to. Resolution order: `namespace` > env `III_NAMESPACE` > `None` (the engine then applies its default namespace). Mirrors the `III_WORKER_NAME` precedence. It scopes more than the registration. The worker and its functions register here, and everything the worker does afterwards follows it: a `IIIClient::trigger` resolves its target here and a `IIIClient::register_trigger` binds here, unless the call names another namespace.\n\n### Returns\n- **IIIClient** - A client for interacting with the III engine.\n```"}]}]},"uuid":"fb90ed8d-6e6c-4f0b-a5e9-03e64cc6dfe0","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:52:21.267Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"### Consider the agent\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/website/content/blog/add-a-worker.md\n\nAn agent needs to speak MCP to an external tool server. **Add a worker** that\nbridges MCP into `trigger()` calls. The bridge is a worker like any other.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### registerWorker\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/reference/sdk-browser.mdx.skill.md\n\nRegisters a worker with a iii instance and returns a connected worker client. The WebSocket connection is established automatically.\n\n```APIDOC\n## registerWorker\n\n### Description\nRegisters the worker with a iii instance, returns a connected worker client. The WebSocket connection is established automatically.\n\n### Signature\n```typescript\nregisterWorker(address: string, options?: InitOptions) => ISdk\n```\n\n### Parameters\n#### address (string) - Required\nWebSocket URL of the III engine (e.g. `ws://localhost:49135`).\n\n#### options (InitOptions) - Optional\nOptional InitOptions for worker name, timeouts, and reconnection.\n\n##### InitOptions fields:\n- **headers** (Record<string, string>) - Optional - Browser WebSocket connections authenticate via query parameters or cookies; the `headers` option is ignored.\n- **invocationTimeoutMs** (number) - Optional - Default timeout for `worker.trigger()` invocations in milliseconds. Defaults to `30000`.\n- **namespace** (string) - Optional - Namespace this worker registers under. When omitted the engine applies its `default` namespace. Scopes worker and function registrations so identically-named entries can coexist across namespaces. The browser has no `process.env`, so there is no environment-variable fallback -- pass the option explicitly.\n- **reconnectionConfig** (Partial<IIIReconnectionConfig>) - Optional - WebSocket reconnection behavior.\n- **workerName** (string) - Optional - Name this worker announces to the engine. Defaults to a unique `browser:<random>` per client: a browser has no pid to disambiguate by, and the engine allows only one live worker per name in a namespace, so two tabs sharing a fixed name would evict each other.\n\n### Example\n```typescript\nimport { registerWorker } from 'iii-browser-sdk'\n\nconst worker = registerWorker('ws://localhost:49135')\n```\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Types > iii_sdk > InitOptions\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/reference/sdk-rust.mdx.skill.md\n\nConfiguration options passed to `register_worker`.\n\n| Name | Type | Required | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `metadata` | Option&lt;iii::[`WorkerMetadata`](#workermetadata)&gt; | No | Custom worker metadata. Auto-detected if `None`. |\n| `headers` | `Option<HashMap<String, String>>` | No | Custom HTTP headers sent during the WebSocket handshake. |\n| `otel` | `Option<iii_helpers::observability::OtelConfig>` | No | OpenTelemetry configuration. |\n| `namespace` | `Option<String>` | No | Namespace this worker belongs to. Resolution order:<br />`namespace` > env `III_NAMESPACE` > `None` (the engine then applies its<br />default namespace). Mirrors the `III_WORKER_NAME` precedence.<br /><br />It scopes more than the registration. The worker and its functions<br />register here, and everything the worker does afterwards follows it: a<br />`IIIClient::trigger` resolves its target here and a<br />`IIIClient::register_trigger` binds here, unless the call names<br />another namespace. |\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Category collapse\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/website/content/blog/building-agents-for-real-world.md\n\n## Category collapse\n\nOnce Worker is the primitive, categories that used to be separate runtimes collapse into the same vocabulary.\n\nSandbox provider is a worker. The 40+ providers we've mapped (E2B, Daytona, Modal, Vercel sandbox and the rest) all express as workers with sandbox-shaped functions. The choice of provider becomes a registry swap rather than an integration rewrite.\n\nBrowser tab is a worker. `iii-browser-sdk` runs on port 49135 and registers the tab as a worker the engine can address. Browser-side events are triggers. DOM operations are functions. The page becomes part of the same execution graph as the backend.\n\nExternal agent is a worker via the A2A protocol. MCP server is a worker via the MCP bridge. The agent itself is a peer worker, not a privileged consumer of tools. The \"agent calls tools\" mental model collapses into \"worker calls function on another worker.\"\n\nIntegration cost goes from quadratic to linear. Each new capability is one registry entry instead of an integration with every consumer. Each new consumer reads from the registry instead of a custom integration per provider.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### register_worker\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/reference/sdk-rust.mdx\n\nRegisters a worker with the III engine and returns a client for further operations. Accepts an address and initialization options.\n\n```APIDOC\n## register_worker\n\n### Description\nRegisters a worker with the III engine and returns a client for further operations.\n\n### Signature\n```rust\nregister_worker(address: &str, options: InitOptions) -> IIIClient\n```\n\n### Parameters\n- **address** (`&str`) - Required - The address of the worker.\n- **options** (`InitOptions`) - Required - Initialization options.\n\n#### InitOptions fields\n- **metadata** (`Option<iii::WorkerMetadata>`) - Custom worker metadata. Auto-detected if `None`.\n- **headers** (`Option<HashMap<String, String>>`) - Custom HTTP headers sent during the WebSocket handshake.\n- **otel** (`Option<iii_helpers::observability::OtelConfig>`) - OpenTelemetry configuration.\n- **namespace** (`Option<String>`) - Namespace this worker belongs to. Resolution order: `namespace` > env `III_NAMESPACE` > `None` (the engine then applies its default namespace). Mirrors the `III_WORKER_NAME` precedence. It scopes more than the registration. The worker and its functions register here, and everything the worker does afterwards follows it: a `IIIClient::trigger` resolves its target here and a `IIIClient::register_trigger` binds here, unless the call names another namespace.\n\n### Returns\n- **IIIClient** - A client for interacting with the III engine.\n```"}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f8359df5-c634-421d-8323-27698227d7fa","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Context7","title":"Context7","icons":[{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.svg","mimeType":"image/svg+xml","sizes":["any"]},{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.png","mimeType":"image/png","sizes":["512x512"]}],"version":"4.5.0","websiteUrl":"https://context7.com","description":"Context7 provides up-to-date documentation and code examples for libraries and frameworks."}}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad043bab-e82d-4c50-b2bf-d3a08237e5ff","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
