-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":63},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b49189fd-aef3-4b5b-aec3-961360edf86f","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:54:53.195Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"0b8afed1-6d01-44cd-9f02-07ff7a0773c9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"63076884-86c8-4719-937e-cb437c55717e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012vPoHCZHBFsdrSHmib5niE","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Worker Manifest Configuration\n\nSource: https://iii.dev/docs/0-13-0/creating-workers/workers\n\nDefines the worker's name, runtime environment, and scripts for installation and starting.\n\n```yaml\nname: math-worker\nruntime:\n  kind: python\n  package_manager: pip\n  entry: math_worker.py\nscripts:\n  install: \"pip install -r requirements.txt\"\n  start: \"python math_worker.py\"\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Workers\n\nSource: https://iii.dev/docs/creating-workers/workers\n\nThe `iii.worker.yaml` file is the worker manifest located at the worker's root directory. It instructs iii on how to install dependencies, run the worker, and pass through configuration. This manifest is used by both the iii worker CLI commands and by workers that iii starts automatically when specified in iii's `config.yaml`.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### registerFunction\n\nSource: https://iii.dev/docs/0-13-0/sdk-reference/node-sdk\n\nRegisters a callable function on a worker. It accepts a function ID, a handler or invocation configuration, and optional settings for description, metadata, and request/response JSON Schemas.\n\n```APIDOC\n## registerFunction\n\n### Description\nRegister a callable function on this worker.\n\n### Method Signature\n```typescript\nworker.registerFunction(\n  functionId: string,\n  handlerOrInvocation: RemoteFunctionHandler | HttpInvocationConfig,\n  options?: RegisterFunctionOptions,\n): FunctionRef;\n```\n\n### Parameters\n* **functionId** (string) - Required - The unique identifier for the function.\n* **handlerOrInvocation** (RemoteFunctionHandler | HttpInvocationConfig) - Required - The function handler or its invocation configuration.\n* **options** (RegisterFunctionOptions) - Optional - Accepts `description`, `metadata`, and optional `request_format` / `response_format` JSON Schemas.\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Add a Worker to the Project\n\nSource: https://iii.dev/docs/0-13-0/using-iii/workers-registry\n\nDemonstrates adding a worker to your project using the 'iii worker add' command. It shows examples for adding from the registry name, a local path, or a Docker/OCI image.\n\n```bash\niii worker add iii-state                # registry name\niii worker add ./workers/my-worker      # local path\niii worker add ghcr.io/org/worker:tag   # Docker or OCI image\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Workers > Scaffold a new worker\n\nSource: https://iii.dev/docs/creating-workers/workers\n\nThe `iii worker init` command scaffolds a new standalone worker, creating a language-specific project directory with the iii SDK, an `iii.worker.yaml` manifest, and example function and trigger registrations. Supported languages include TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, and Rust. The command can target a specific directory name or override it with `--directory`. Rerunning the command on an existing worker directory makes no changes, and it fails on non-empty directories by default unless `--allow-non-empty` is used."}]}]},"uuid":"a0285fc2-8a24-46aa-947b-8839e9f3518e","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:54:54.471Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"### Worker Manifest Configuration\n\nSource: https://iii.dev/docs/0-13-0/creating-workers/workers\n\nDefines the worker's name, runtime environment, and scripts for installation and starting.\n\n```yaml\nname: math-worker\nruntime:\n  kind: python\n  package_manager: pip\n  entry: math_worker.py\nscripts:\n  install: \"pip install -r requirements.txt\"\n  start: \"python math_worker.py\"\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Workers\n\nSource: https://iii.dev/docs/creating-workers/workers\n\nThe `iii.worker.yaml` file is the worker manifest located at the worker's root directory. It instructs iii on how to install dependencies, run the worker, and pass through configuration. This manifest is used by both the iii worker CLI commands and by workers that iii starts automatically when specified in iii's `config.yaml`.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### registerFunction\n\nSource: https://iii.dev/docs/0-13-0/sdk-reference/node-sdk\n\nRegisters a callable function on a worker. It accepts a function ID, a handler or invocation configuration, and optional settings for description, metadata, and request/response JSON Schemas.\n\n```APIDOC\n## registerFunction\n\n### Description\nRegister a callable function on this worker.\n\n### Method Signature\n```typescript\nworker.registerFunction(\n  functionId: string,\n  handlerOrInvocation: RemoteFunctionHandler | HttpInvocationConfig,\n  options?: RegisterFunctionOptions,\n): FunctionRef;\n```\n\n### Parameters\n* **functionId** (string) - Required - The unique identifier for the function.\n* **handlerOrInvocation** (RemoteFunctionHandler | HttpInvocationConfig) - Required - The function handler or its invocation configuration.\n* **options** (RegisterFunctionOptions) - Optional - Accepts `description`, `metadata`, and optional `request_format` / `response_format` JSON Schemas.\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Add a Worker to the Project\n\nSource: https://iii.dev/docs/0-13-0/using-iii/workers-registry\n\nDemonstrates adding a worker to your project using the 'iii worker add' command. It shows examples for adding from the registry name, a local path, or a Docker/OCI image.\n\n```bash\niii worker add iii-state                # registry name\niii worker add ./workers/my-worker      # local path\niii worker add ghcr.io/org/worker:tag   # Docker or OCI image\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Workers > Scaffold a new worker\n\nSource: https://iii.dev/docs/creating-workers/workers\n\nThe `iii worker init` command scaffolds a new standalone worker, creating a language-specific project directory with the iii SDK, an `iii.worker.yaml` manifest, and example function and trigger registrations. Supported languages include TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, and Rust. The command can target a specific directory name or override it with `--directory`. Rerunning the command on an existing worker directory makes no changes, and it fails on non-empty directories by default unless `--allow-non-empty` is used."}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c056951-30a9-42d8-88f4-76e3e3efcdef","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Context7","title":"Context7","icons":[{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.svg","mimeType":"image/svg+xml","sizes":["any"]},{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.png","mimeType":"image/png","sizes":["512x512"]}],"version":"4.5.0","websiteUrl":"https://context7.com","description":"Context7 provides up-to-date documentation and code examples for libraries and frameworks."}}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0b8afed1-6d01-44cd-9f02-07ff7a0773c9","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
