{"parentUuid":"6658b470-a3df-4b55-88f6-e00ee5ea06dd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"63076884-86c8-4719-937e-cb437c55717e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent\n\n**Project:**\n- Bastion is a Rust agent control plane (renamed from \"software factory\" at the user's request).\n- `bastion-server` runs on the iii engine 0.25.0, with the iced desktop client and the `bastion` CLI.\n- Users define workflows and send requests. Jobs fulfill requests by running agents through the workflow's steps.\n- Jobs and workflows are the most vital concepts.\n\n**Completed this segment (all pushed unless noted):**\n- S4: the stage code is removed.\n- U1 to U13 (see the Analysis).\n- VISION/README/DECISIONS rewritten as an agent control plane.\n- Step editor: constraints and capabilities split into separate sections. Committed `3b3370e`; not yet pushed.\n\n**Current request (latest):**\n> \"Good, now I want to add capabilities. The function scope is good. But I also want to add more capabilities: shell scripts, mcp servers, plugins, tools, and so forth. Constraints map to rules, hooks, agents, and so on.\"\n\nThe user's answers to my questions:\n- Shell = \"Named commands (Recommended)\": a grant on `sandbox::exec` bound to command words.\n- MCP = \"Add the bridge now (Recommended)\": add an MCP bridge worker to the stack; a server lists its MCP servers in Settings; a step's capability grants an MCP server's tools.\n- Plugins = \"Not sure yet\": leave out this round.\n- Agents (constraint) = \"A reviewer that must pass (Recommended)\": a named agent from `.agents/agents/` reviews the step's change before the job moves on; its verdict passes or fails the step.\n\n**Standing rules:**\n- No AI attribution or Co-Authored-By in commits, PRs or anything; this overrides the harness reminder.\n- Run the CodeScene `pre_commit_code_health_safeguard` before each commit, and commit only when it passes.\n- Stage files by path.\n- Push only when asked. The user often says \"push and continue\".\n- Before a push, run every CI step:\n  - `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\n  - `scripts/check-seams.sh`\n  - `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n  - `cargo test --workspace`\n- `bastion-core` may depend only on serde and sha2.\n- Use `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`.\n- Respond in STE; caveman and ponytail hooks are active.\n- Published prose (README, VISION, DECISIONS, docs) follows ~/.claude/VOICE.md, checked with the chain voice-check → humanizer → slopbeth (not installed) → voice-check.\n- The user prefers momentum: proceed on stated assumptions and reserve questions for costly forks.\n\n**Security constraints (verbatim and still active):**\n- \"local environments don't need tokens unless they can be automatically setup - credentials are required for remote connections\"\n- Key and token values must never pass through the assistant. Only masked hints may be shown. The minisign private key stays with the user.\n- Never list processes with full arguments (`pgrep -fl`, `ps aux`): iii VM boot lines carry host secrets. Use `ps -o pid=,lstart=,comm=` or `ps -o pid=,comm= -A`.\n- Do not work around classifier denials; ask the user to run `! <command>`.\n- Never read or print tokens. Use `scratchpad/api.sh METHOD PATH [JSON]` (strip its last line with `sed '$d'`):\n  - api.sh now reads `$HOME/Library/Application Support/dev.tacoda.bastion/server/token`.\n  - `api2.sh` targets server two (port 49191).\n- Claude may act for the user on test jobs, naming each action (\"only dark runs unsupervised\"). Don't use drive.sh when approving a wait would land something unwanted.\n- Don't `pkill` the desktop blindly; kill only my `target/debug/bastion-desktop` by pid.\n- The user's repo `~/Code/bastion` (bastion-gh workspace): I committed `50558a4` locally there (charter moved to `.agents/`). It is not pushed; push only if asked.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts\n\n**Steps and options:**\n- Step kinds: `Stage {Prompt, Agent, Skill, Shell}` (Command removed, D45).\n- `Kind {Turn, Factory}`.\n- A step's `Options {model: String, revisions: Option<u32>, spend_micros: Option<u64>}` (D43):\n  - The step model wins over the job model, which wins over settings.\n  - `Bounds.spent: BTreeMap<step, micros>` comes from turns' sessions `<job>-<step>-<rand>` via `turn::session_step`.\n  - `start_within` blocks factory-initiated starts over budget. A person's retry, comment or answer always runs.\n\n**Governance:**\n- Gate (D44/D48):\n  - Step name `workflow/step` is sent in the turn metadata `\"step\"`.\n  - `govern::At {stage, step}`; `gate_at(call, at, constraints, grants)`; `gate(...)` is a wrapper with an empty step.\n  - `grants_at`: the step's own grants replace its kind's grants.\n  - `Access {Ask, Allowed}`: no Denied, and `demote() -> Option` (below ask, the grant is removed).\n  - `Constraint.steps: Vec<String>` (empty = every step); `applies(c, step)`.\n  - `Capability.step: String`.\n  - A refusal names the step (\"not granted at\"/\"No grant covers ... at {place}\").\n- Failure links (D47):\n  - `Link.failure: bool`.\n  - `Step.on_failure: Option<String>` and `Step.failure_only: bool`.\n  - `order()` ignores failure links. At most one failure link per node, and none to itself.\n  - `step_failed` goes along the failure link, else to the fixer. Bounded by revisions.\n  - `advance` skips `failure_only` steps.\n- `Job.failed: BTreeSet<String>` (stored in jobs column `failed_steps`); `StepState::Skipped`.\n- Artifacts carry `step`; `Effect::RecordArtifact {stage, step, body}`, `Effect::CaptureDiff {stage, step}`.\n- Charter (D46):\n  - `AGENTS.md` + `.agents/settings.json` (permissions, hooks).\n  - Agent steps read `.agents/agents/<name>.md`; skill steps read `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.\n  - `BRIEF_FILES = [\"AGENTS.md\"]`, `SETTINGS_DIR = \".agents\"`.\n\n**Migrations (user_version; the dev DB is at 8):**\n- 5: steps.\n- 6: capabilities PK `(stage, step, function)`.\n- 7: commands become prompts: `COMMANDS_AS_PROMPTS` sets the note to \"Read /work/repo/.claude/commands/X.md ...\".\n- 8: capabilities CHECK rung IN ('ask','allowed'); denied rows deleted.\n- `rebuild(t, command)` maps 'command' by era: 'shell' for migrations 1 to 4, 'prompt' for 5 and later.\n- `as_steps` deletes denied capabilities in every rebuild.\n- ALTERS (35):\n  - artifacts.step\n  - workflow_nodes model / revisions / spend_micros\n  - capabilities.step\n  - constraints.steps\n  - workflow_links.failure\n  - jobs.failed_steps\n\n**Desktop:**\n- Top bar: castle SVG `assets/icon/bastion.svg`, the pages, and the switcher (All servers on records pages: Jobs, Audit, Costs, Evals, Verification).\n- `Ctx.all`; `Ctx::shown()`, `Ctx::each(request)`, `Each<A>` type.\n- `Message::OpenOn{server, route}`.\n- `pages/chart.rs`: Bars canvas, tile, compare/Pair, day/last_days.\n- `pages/audit.rs` page.\n- `pages/step_rules.rs`: the step's Constraints and Capabilities sections.\n- `head()`, `problem()`, `on()` helpers in `pages/mod.rs`.\n\n**iii facts:**\n- A turn's tools are iii functions via `harness::send` options `functions: {allow, deny, expose: \"agent_trigger\"|\"native\"}`.\n- Bastion currently passes `TOOLS = [\"sandbox::exec\",\"sandbox::fs::read\",\"sandbox::fs::write\",\"sandbox::fs::ls\"]` (factory.rs ~line 33).\n- \"MCP server is a worker via the MCP bridge.\" There is no MCP worker in our worker-compose.yaml.\n- iii has no plugin concept.\n- The stack workers in worker-compose.yaml: secrets, database, state, queue, harness, llm-router, provider-*, bastion-openai-compat, session-manager, context-manager, iii-directory, fp, judge, worktree, github, approval-gate, opengantry.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (key, this segment)\n\n**Core:**\n- `crates/bastion-core/src/lib.rs`:\n  - Stage has no Command; `Stage::ALL: [Stage; 4]`.\n  - `Bounds{trial, revision_budget, spent}`.\n  - Job has `failed`.\n  - `start_within` and `over_budget`.\n  - `step_failed`: branch via on_failure, per-step revisions limit, inserts into failed.\n  - `shell_ran` removes from failed on Ran.\n  - `advance` skips failure_only.\n  - `steps()` shows Failed/Skipped; the finish stands on the last step that ran; past the finish, Skipped.\n- `crates/bastion-core/src/workflow.rs`:\n  - `Options`, `Link.failure`, `Step.options/on_failure/failure_only`.\n  - `model_fits`, `failure_links_fit`, `failure_only()`.\n- `crates/bastion-core/src/govern.rs`:\n  - `Access{Ask, Allowed}`; `At`; `grants_at`; `grant_for`; `gate_at`; `applies`; `Constraint.steps`; `Capability.step`.\n- `crates/bastion-core/src/charter.rs`: `.agents` and AGENTS.md.\n- `crates/bastion-core/src/brief.rs`: `.agents/agents`, `.agents/skills`.\n\n**Server:**\n- `factory.rs`:\n  - `bounds_for` computes `spent`.\n  - The step model wins.\n  - `step_name(record)` = `workflow/node`.\n  - Metadata includes `\"step\"`.\n  - `gate.rules(&job.id, &step)`.\n- `gate.rs`:\n  - `judge` reads `metadata.step` and uses `gate_at`.\n  - `move_capability(at: govern::At, function, up)`: demote below ask calls `ungrant`.\n  - `grant_at_step`, `ungrant(g)`, `scope_constraint(id, steps)`.\n  - `rules(job, step)`.\n- `govern_store.rs`: `remove_capability`; capabilities and constraints store step/steps.\n- `api/govern.rs`:\n  - `constraint_steps`, `capability_add`, `capability_remove`, `capability_move(cell, g: CapabilityView, up)`.\n  - `grant_of` refuses rungs other than ask/allowed.\n  - The factory text \"As often as each step allows, 2 times by default, ...\".\n- `http.rs`: routes `POST /capabilities` (add), `/capabilities/remove`, `/constraints/{id}/steps`; the Grant struct has `step`.\n- `store/schema.rs`: migrations 1 to 8, ALTERS 35, jobs CREATE has `failed_steps`, `JOB_COLUMNS` includes `failed_steps`.\n- `store/sql.rs`: `failed_steps(j)`; UPDATE includes `failed_steps`.\n- `workflow_store.rs`: node options and link failure stored.\n- `seed_flows.rs`: `graph_of(id)` (test-only).\n- `charter.rs`: `SETTINGS = \".agents/settings.json\"`.\n- `factory/turn.rs`: `Turn::start(job)`, `step_of`, `session_step`.\n- `seed/governance.sql`: grants only prompt, agent and skill `sandbox::*` allowed.\n\n**Protocol:**\n- NodeView `options: OptionsView`, LinkView `failure`, ConstraintView `steps` (Default derived), CapabilityView `step`.\n- ArtifactView `step`, JobSummary `node`, JobDetail Default.\n- api: CapabilityAdd, CapabilityRemove, ConstraintSteps, CapabilityMove.step; `every().len() == 73`.\n\n**Desktop:**\n- `app.rs`: top bar, switcher, `go()` sets route before ctx, OpenOn.\n- `route.rs`: `records()`, `one_record()`.\n- Pages:\n  - `jobs.rs`: scope from ctx, overview tiles and chart.\n  - `job.rs`: title first line; `judged`/`what_approve_does` by node.\n  - `costs.rs`: combine/merge, spend chart.\n  - `audit.rs`.\n  - `evals.rs`: across servers; compare charts `total_pairs`/`grade_pairs`.\n  - `verification.rs`: across servers; `landed_on`.\n  - `govern.rs`: no Audit; step grants section; rungs ask/allowed; Demote is \"Remove\" at ask.\n  - `workflows.rs`:\n    - options_row (model picker, spend, revisions)\n    - FailureLink toggle\n    - `picked_step()`\n    - Rules msg → step_rules\n    - CUSTOM kinds: 4\n  - `step_rules.rs` (Rules, Msg, At, load/update/view returning `Vec<Element>` with panels \"Constraints\" and \"Capabilities\"; `rescoped` guard; `grant_line`, `grant_form`).\n  - `drawing.rs`: failure links red and dashed.\n  - `mod.rs`: mark \"skipped\" ↷.\n- `.codescene/code-health-rules.json`: `chart.rs` exempt from the argument count (like `drawing.rs`).\n\n**Docs:**\n- PLAN.md: U1 to U13 recorded, with \"After this plan\" emptied.\n- DECISIONS.md:\n  - D43 to D48 added.\n  - The intro is an agent control plane.\n  - D25 is marked under review.\n  - New open question \"Harness and factory\".\n  - Header `<!-- voice-register: informational -->`.\n- VISION.md and README.md rewritten as an agent control plane. README declares a first-person exemption via `<!-- voice-first-person content=\"exempt: ...\" -->`.\n\n**Memory:** `memory/bastion-orchestrator-terminology.md` rewritten: \"Bastion is an agent control plane (2026-11-11)\". The MEMORY.md line was updated.\n\n4. Errors and fixes\n\n**go() read under the old route:**\n- The Ctx was built from the previous route, so records pages read a single server.\n- Fix: set `self.route` before `Page::open`.\n\n**Server lifecycle:**\n- Killing the server stopped its stack (D13), and the new server attached to a dying stack (calls timed out).\n- Fix: restart again, and/or `POST /stack/start`.\n- The test build did not rebuild the server binary; I had to run `cargo build -p bastion-server` before restart.\n\n**Pointer file:**\n- `~/Library/Application Support/dev.tacoda.bastion/local-server` pointed at an old data folder (local appeared unreachable).\n- Fix: rewrote it to `.../dev.tacoda.bastion/server`.\n\n**Migration era mapping:**\n- Rebuilds with the new CHECK would fail on 'command' rows.\n- Fix: map by era. Updated the migration tests and split them (Large Method).\n\n**CodeScene failures, each fixed:**\n- Argument counts: introduced the `At` struct; `capability_move` takes a CapabilityView.\n- Mean complexity in `workflow.rs`: extracted `model_fits`.\n- Bumpy road / complexity in step_rules `grants`: extracted `grant_line` and `grant_form`.\n- Large migration test: split it.\n\n**Python edit assertions failed** because `cargo fmt` reflowed code; I re-read the formatted text and reapplied.\n\n**Other:**\n- clippy: `useless_format`, `cloned_ref_to_slice_refs`.\n- Chart hover \"0 ·\" trailing separator: fixed.\n- Eval compare: a change from zero read as \"same\", fixed to count format; a zero drew a sliver, fixed.\n- Refused/held/flagged were colored red: made neutral (`less_is_better: Option<bool>`).\n\n**Live finding (documented, not changed):** a step-level fs::write deny was bypassed by `sandbox::exec`.\n\n5. Problem Solving\n\n**Live checks done:**\n- Switcher.\n- Aggregates with second server \"two\" (port 49191; added through Settings with a clipboard paste of its token file, clipboard cleared).\n- Charts and hover.\n- Step model: Anthropic Haiku on plan, confirmed via the session-manager jsonl.\n- Step grant deny, then the D48 grant/demote/ungrant audit entries.\n- Migration 7 converted a command node.\n- AGENTS.md charter on demo-local.\n- Branching job: checks failed, then the job went to report; steps showed checks failed.\n- Constraints/capabilities split screenshot.\n\n**Clean-up done:** three test workflows deleted; the bastion-gh charter moved to `.agents/`.\n\n6. All user messages (this segment)\n\n- (from prior compaction context) continuing S4\n- \"I also want to change the layout - a top bar seems better, including adding the image - instead of a sidebar\" (earlier, queued)\n- \"Along with most areas belonging to a server, it would be nice to also have some kind of aggregate view that allows access to multiple servers. Audit log and costs are two examples of places where this would be useful.\"\n- \"I also want to have more options for each step - like the ability to choose the model I want to use\"\n- \"It would be nice if it ended up looking more like a workflow (a flowchart) The workflow matches well because failed jobs get raised or retried so only success moves left. This works well, but we may want other kinds of workflows that do want that ability\"\n- \"yes\" (push S4 and hosting docs)\n- \"I guess jobs technically work like this too - each server has jobs and there is also an aggregate\"\n- \"SO I guess I really want to swap between servers (or all servers) for all these concepts in a horizontal menu bar at the top. Seeing aggregates and swapping servers should be easy. Remove the sidebar. Update the pages to be clean and well-organized. Also add some more rich elements like graphs.\"\n- \"steps should probably use workflow and step name for identifiers and I think constraints and capabilities are also per workflow step\"\n- \"Looks good. I could be convinced that evals, costs, and verification lives there too. But I still want easy accessibility in the UI. PUsh and continue\"\n- \"SO I guess each step has a budget really\"\n- \"Graphs for evals would also be nice\" / \"We want to compare A and B\"\n- \"yes, push and then continue\"\n- \"continue\"\n- \"Yes, also I think we can drop the command - anything I can think of would either be an agent skill or a shell command.\"\n- \"Also I don't want to assume claude - For this project assume the harness lives in two places: AGENTS.md and .agents/\"\n- \"the charter - sorry assume that about the charter\"\n- \"the harness is part of the product\"\n- \"THere are some mentions in the UI of 'stack'. Replace these with 'engine'\"\n- \"push and continue\"\n- \"1. yes 2. yes\" (delete test workflows; move the bastion-gh charter)\n- \"Next up I'd like to add a constraints and capabilities section to the workflows page. Each step can have these, so I want to be able to manage them in that view. Also, don't do deny for capabilities - deny is the default.\"\n- \"Awesome, next I want to update the vision and the readme. Bastion is not a factory. It is an agent control plane. It's primary concepts stay the same. The most vital are jobs and workflows. Users primarily define workflows and send requests to have them fulfilled by jobs which run agents. Previously we had a separation between harness and factory. That may still be useful, but things appear to be collapsing onto workflows and so all of these things may end up being done by bastion using the settings from the workflows and/or their steps.\"\n- \"yes, update DECISIONS.md too\"\n- \"[Image #16] It looks like constraints and capabilities are being mixed. They should be in their own sections.\"\n- \"Good, now I want to add capabilities. The function scope is good. But I also want to add more capabilities: shell scripts, mcp servers, plugins, tools, and so forth. Constraints map to rules, hooks, agents, and so on.\"\n- AskUserQuestion answers:\n  - Shell = \"Named commands (Recommended)\"\n  - MCP = \"Add the bridge now (Recommended)\"\n  - Plugins = \"Not sure yet\"\n  - Agents = \"A reviewer that must pass (Recommended)\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks\n\n- Implement the new capability kinds:\n  - Function: exists.\n  - Named commands: `sandbox::exec` bound to command words.\n  - Tools: more iii functions per step, which widens the turn's `functions.allow`, today hard-coded `TOOLS`.\n  - MCP servers via an MCP bridge worker added to the stack; a server lists its MCP servers in Settings; a step capability grants an MCP server's tools.\n- Implement the new constraint kinds:\n  - Rules: exist.\n  - Hooks per step: generalize the charter hooks.\n  - Reviewer agent: a named `.agents/agents/` agent reviews the step's change and its verdict passes or fails the step.\n- Plugins: left out this round.\n- Write a new PLAN.md phase plan and decisions (D49+) for the above.\n- Commit `3b3370e` (split sections) is not pushed. The user hasn't said \"push\" since; only push when asked.\n- Leftovers: the `demo-local` test commits (scratch); bastion-gh local commit `50558a4` not pushed.\n\n8. Current Work\n\nI was researching how to add an MCP bridge to the stack before writing the plan for the new capability and constraint kinds:\n- context7 confirmed iii treats every tool as a function and that \"MCP server is a worker via the MCP bridge\". It did not give the bridge worker's registry name or config.\n- I then ran `iii worker --help`, which failed: \"error: unrecognized subcommand 'worker'\".\n- So the MCP bridge worker's name and configuration are still unknown.\n\nThe last assistant message before that said:\n> \"Your choices: Shell: named commands. MCP: add the bridge now. Plugins: left out of this round. Agent constraints: a reviewer that must pass. Before planning the MCP part, I'm looking up the iii MCP bridge worker: its name, how it's set up, and which functions it registers.\"\n\n9. Optional Next Step\n\nContinue the research for the MCP bridge worker:\n- Try `iii --help` to find the registry/worker subcommand.\n- Or query context7 `/iii-hq/iii` for \"mcp bridge\".\n\nIf it can't be found, state that plainly. Then write the PLAN.md phases (and decisions D49+), proceeding on the stated assumptions:\n- **C1:** per-step tools widen `functions.allow` beyond `TOOLS`, plus named-command grants on `sandbox::exec` with command words.\n- **C2:** MCP servers through the bridge worker.\n- **C3:** per-step hooks.\n- **C4:** a reviewer-agent constraint.\n\nThen implement phase by phase with live checks, CI, safeguard and commits, as before.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"536242c1-8ce1-4686-b5f9-540efd1c11d4","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:56:17.882Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":177,"turnIndex":273},"turnOrigin":"human","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"536242c1-8ce1-4686-b5f9-540efd1c11d4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/memory/bastion-orchestrator-terminology.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/memory/bastion-orchestrator-terminology.md","content":"---\nname: bastion-orchestrator-terminology\ndescription: \"Bastion is an agent control plane (owner's call, 2026-11-11); jobs and workflows are its core. Replaces the 2026-11-06 'keep factory words' rule.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e\n  modified: 2026-11-12T00:32:24.394Z\n---\n\nBastion is an agent control plane, not a factory. Users define workflows and\nsend requests; jobs fulfill them by running agents through the workflow's\nsteps. Jobs and workflows are the most vital concepts.\n\n**Why:** on 2026-11-11 the owner said \"Bastion is not a factory. It is an\nagent control plane.\" An earlier rebrand to orchestrator/control plane was\nrolled back on 2026-11-06 (commits 7ce2901, df201c9, cc8872e reverted); this\ntime the owner asked for it directly, so it stands. Don't say \"orchestrator\".\n\n**How to apply:** user-facing text says control plane, jobs and workflows.\nThe harness/factory split is history: rules are collapsing onto workflows\nand their steps, and that direction is not settled. The code still has\n`factory` module names; renaming them was not asked for.\n","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}},"displayPath":"../../.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/memory/bastion-orchestrator-terminology.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e3ea69b4-ed90-4e07-9a72-cc2d5479b5d4","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:56:18.329Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/tacoda/.claude/projects/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/memory/bastion-orchestrator-terminology.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t---\n2\tname: bastion-orchestrator-terminology\n3\tdescription: \"Bastion is an agent control plane (owner's call, 2026-11-11); jobs and workflows are its core. Replaces the 2026-11-06 'keep factory words' rule.\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: 4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-12T00:32:24.394Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tBastion is an agent control plane, not a factory. Users define workflows and\n12\tsend requests; jobs fulfill them by running agents through the workflow's\n13\tsteps. Jobs and workflows are the most vital concepts.\n14\t\n15\t**Why:** on 2026-11-11 the owner said \"Bastion is not a factory. It is an\n16\tagent control plane.\" An earlier rebrand to orchestrator/control plane was\n17\trolled back on 2026-11-06 (commits 7ce2901, df201c9, cc8872e reverted); this\n18\ttime the owner asked for it directly, so it stands. Don't say \"orchestrator\".\n19\t\n20\t**How to apply:** user-facing text says control plane, jobs and workflows.\n21\tThe harness/factory split is history: rules are collapsing onto workflows\n22\tand their steps, and that direction is not settled. The code still has\n23\t`factory` module names; renaming them was not asked for.\n24\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"e3ea69b4-ed90-4e07-9a72-cc2d5479b5d4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md","content":"# Bastion's vision\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nBastion is an agent control plane. You define workflows and send requests,\nand Bastion fulfills each request as a job: agents work through the\nworkflow's steps, under the rules you set on each step. Jobs and workflows\nare the two ideas everything else serves. The cost is plain: a job does only\nwhat its workflow says, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone.\nBastion runs on your machine, on a remote server, or on both at once.\n\n## Jobs and workflows\n\nA workflow is a series of steps on a canvas. A step is a prompt, one of the\nrepository's agents or skills, or a shell script, and each step has one\ntext to edit. Each step also carries its own settings:\n\n- **Its dial:** a sun when a person decides, a moon when it runs on its\n  own.\n- **Its model and its budget:** how often its failure may send the work\n  back, and the most its turns may spend.\n- **Its rules:** the constraints its agent works under, and the calls the\n  agent may make.\n- **Its links:** the results it passes on, and the step a failure goes to.\n\nA job is one request run through one workflow. It runs the steps in order,\nwaits where a step's dial says a person decides, and ends with its branch\nready, merged or left for you. Bastion ships the common workflows with their\ntext filled in, and you can change every step of them.\n\n## Rules move onto the workflow\n\nBastion used to split its rules into two layers. The harness bound an\nagent's calls. The factory bound the work around them: what a step may do,\nand when a change lands. Both now live more and more on a workflow and its\nsteps, and Bastion applies them as each step runs. I think the two layers\nwill collapse into one, with Bastion applying whatever the workflow and its\nsteps set. The split may still be useful, though, and that isn't settled;\nthe next few workflows people write will settle it.\n\nA repository brings its own rules too: its charter, in `AGENTS.md` and\n`.agents/settings.json`. A turn may read the charter but may not change it.\n\n## Two levels: each server, and all of them\n\nEvery page shows one server, the one you pick at the top. Some pages can\nalso show every server at once, and those are the ones about records.\n\n**Records, per server or across all.** Jobs, Audit Log, Costs, Evals and\nVerification read one server, or every server you added, side by side. All\nservers is one more choice in the server picker, so you filter by server the\nsame way on each of these pages. You open a job, an entry or a turn and act\non it wherever it lives.\n\n**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,\nEngine and Settings belong to the server you pick. A rules page never mixes\ntwo servers, because each server's rules shape only its own jobs, and a sum\nof two rule sets means nothing.\n\n## What a server holds\n\nEach server is a control plane of its own, and everything that shapes it\nlives with it.\n\n- **Workspaces:** the repositories it works in, each with its checks, its\n  setup, its VM image, and what happens to a job's branch at the end.\n- **Workflows:** its series of steps, each step with its settings.\n- **Capabilities and constraints:** what an agent may call, each grant ask\n  or allowed, and the rules its work must keep, each from told to enforced.\n  Both apply to every step of a kind, or to one workflow step.\n- **Settings:** its model providers, its people and their roles, its\n  notifications, and its secrets.\n- **Records:** its jobs, its audit log, its evals, its costs, and what\n  landed.\n\nThese are live controls, not a configuration file you edit and restart. A\nserver runs on the iii engine, and each value you change in the app changes\nhow that engine works for the next call or the next job: which model a turn\nruns on, which calls an agent may make, which image a VM boots, what a step\ndoes. Bastion's job is to turn the values you set into how iii behaves.\n\nThe app itself keeps one thing: the list of servers you added. That list is\nthe only setting that belongs to you and not to a server.\n\n## Local and remote\n\nA local server starts with the app and needs no credentials. A remote\nserver needs a token the server issued you, over TLS. Either kind runs the\nsame control plane, so a workflow written on one works on the other. A job\nruns on one server; your jobs can run on many.\n\n## What does not change\n\n- Agent code runs in a VM, never on your machine. A step reaches the\n  network only when its workflow says so, with the secrets it names.\n- Every action names who took it, in the server's audit log.\n- A seeded default is a starting point, never a lock.\n\n## Not this\n\nNot an editor: the only code you read in Bastion is the change a job\nproposes. Not a web app.\n\n## Next\n\nCopy the Short workflow, give its build step its own model and its own\ngrants, and send it one request. The job page shows what each step did\nunder those settings.\n","numLines":110,"startLine":1,"totalLines":110}},"displayPath":"VISION.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f5e47af0-3676-46dc-a1d0-86997bf99b01","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:56:18.329Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# Bastion's vision\n2\t\n3\t<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n4\t<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n5\t\n6\tBastion is an agent control plane. You define workflows and send requests,\n7\tand Bastion fulfills each request as a job: agents work through the\n8\tworkflow's steps, under the rules you set on each step. Jobs and workflows\n9\tare the two ideas everything else serves. The cost is plain: a job does only\n10\twhat its workflow says, so a check you take out of a workflow is gone.\n11\tBastion runs on your machine, on a remote server, or on both at once.\n12\t\n13\t## Jobs and workflows\n14\t\n15\tA workflow is a series of steps on a canvas. A step is a prompt, one of the\n16\trepository's agents or skills, or a shell script, and each step has one\n17\ttext to edit. Each step also carries its own settings:\n18\t\n19\t- **Its dial:** a sun when a person decides, a moon when it runs on its\n20\t  own.\n21\t- **Its model and its budget:** how often its failure may send the work\n22\t  back, and the most its turns may spend.\n23\t- **Its rules:** the constraints its agent works under, and the calls the\n24\t  agent may make.\n25\t- **Its links:** the results it passes on, and the step a failure goes to.\n26\t\n27\tA job is one request run through one workflow. It runs the steps in order,\n28\twaits where a step's dial says a person decides, and ends with its branch\n29\tready, merged or left for you. Bastion ships the common workflows with their\n30\ttext filled in, and you can change every step of them.\n31\t\n32\t## Rules move onto the workflow\n33\t\n34\tBastion used to split its rules into two layers. The harness bound an\n35\tagent's calls. The factory bound the work around them: what a step may do,\n36\tand when a change lands. Both now live more and more on a workflow and its\n37\tsteps, and Bastion applies them as each step runs. I think the two layers\n38\twill collapse into one, with Bastion applying whatever the workflow and its\n39\tsteps set. The split may still be useful, though, and that isn't settled;\n40\tthe next few workflows people write will settle it.\n41\t\n42\tA repository brings its own rules too: its charter, in `AGENTS.md` and\n43\t`.agents/settings.json`. A turn may read the charter but may not change it.\n44\t\n45\t## Two levels: each server, and all of them\n46\t\n47\tEvery page shows one server, the one you pick at the top. Some pages can\n48\talso show every server at once, and those are the ones about records.\n49\t\n50\t**Records, per server or across all.** Jobs, Audit Log, Costs, Evals and\n51\tVerification read one server, or every server you added, side by side. All\n52\tservers is one more choice in the server picker, so you filter by server the\n53\tsame way on each of these pages. You open a job, an entry or a turn and act\n54\ton it wherever it lives.\n55\t\n56\t**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,\n57\tEngine and Settings belong to the server you pick. A rules page never mixes\n58\ttwo servers, because each server's rules shape only its own jobs, and a sum\n59\tof two rule sets means nothing.\n60\t\n61\t## What a server holds\n62\t\n63\tEach server is a control plane of its own, and everything that shapes it\n64\tlives with it.\n65\t\n66\t- **Workspaces:** the repositories it works in, each with its checks, its\n67\t  setup, its VM image, and what happens to a job's branch at the end.\n68\t- **Workflows:** its series of steps, each step with its settings.\n69\t- **Capabilities and constraints:** what an agent may call, each grant ask\n70\t  or allowed, and the rules its work must keep, each from told to enforced.\n71\t  Both apply to every step of a kind, or to one workflow step.\n72\t- **Settings:** its model providers, its people and their roles, its\n73\t  notifications, and its secrets.\n74\t- **Records:** its jobs, its audit log, its evals, its costs, and what\n75\t  landed.\n76\t\n77\tThese are live controls, not a configuration file you edit and restart. A\n78\tserver runs on the iii engine, and each value you change in the app changes\n79\thow that engine works for the next call or the next job: which model a turn\n80\truns on, which calls an agent may make, which image a VM boots, what a step\n81\tdoes. Bastion's job is to turn the values you set into how iii behaves.\n82\t\n83\tThe app itself keeps one thing: the list of servers you added. That list is\n84\tthe only setting that belongs to you and not to a server.\n85\t\n86\t## Local and remote\n87\t\n88\tA local server starts with the app and needs no credentials. A remote\n89\tserver needs a token the server issued you, over TLS. Either kind runs the\n90\tsame control plane, so a workflow written on one works on the other. A job\n91\truns on one server; your jobs can run on many.\n92\t\n93\t## What does not change\n94\t\n95\t- Agent code runs in a VM, never on your machine. A step reaches the\n96\t  network only when its workflow says so, with the secrets it names.\n97\t- Every action names who took it, in the server's audit log.\n98\t- A seeded default is a starting point, never a lock.\n99\t\n100\t## Not this\n101\t\n102\tNot an editor: the only code you read in Bastion is the change a job\n103\tproposes. Not a web app.\n104\t\n105\t## Next\n106\t\n107\tCopy the Short workflow, give its build step its own model and its own\n108\tgrants, and send it one request. The job page shows what each step did\n109\tunder those settings.\n110\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"f5e47af0-3676-46dc-a1d0-86997bf99b01","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules.rs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules.rs","content":"//! The rules at one workflow step, on the workflows page (D44, D48): the\n//! constraints that apply there, and the grants that decide what its\n//! agent's calls may do. A step uses its kind's grants until it has its own,\n//! which then take their place.\n\nuse bastion_protocol::api::{self, Request};\nuse bastion_protocol::{CapabilityView, ConstraintView};\nuse iced::widget::{Column, button, column, container, pick_list, row, text, text_input};\nuse iced::{Element, Fill, Task};\n\nuse super::{Choice, Ctx, labeled};\nuse crate::theme;\n\n#[derive(Default)]\npub struct Rules {\n    constraints: Vec<ConstraintView>,\n    grants: Vec<CapabilityView>,\n    /// A new grant for the step, as the form holds it.\n    function: String,\n    rung: String,\n    said: String,\n}\n\n#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\npub enum Msg {\n    Constraints(Result<Vec<ConstraintView>, String>),\n    Grants(Result<Vec<CapabilityView>, String>),\n    /// Apply a constraint at the step too, or take it off the step.\n    Scope(String, bool),\n    /// Give the step its own grants, starting from its kind's.\n    Own,\n    /// Take the step's own grants back, so its kind's apply.\n    Kind,\n    Move(CapabilityView, bool),\n    Function(String),\n    Rung(String),\n    Add,\n    Done(Result<(), String>),\n}\n\n/// The step a page shows rules for: its name, `workflow/step`, and its kind.\npub struct At<'a> {\n    pub step: &'a str,\n    pub stage: &'a str,\n}\n\npub fn load(ctx: &Ctx) -> Task<Msg> {\n    Task::batch([\n        ctx.task(&ctx.current, api::Constraints, Msg::Constraints),\n        ctx.task(&ctx.current, api::Capabilities, Msg::Grants),\n    ])\n}\n\nfn send<R>(ctx: &Ctx, request: R) -> Task<Msg>\nwhere\n    R: Request<Answer = ()> + Send + Sync + 'static,\n{\n    ctx.task(&ctx.current, request, Msg::Done)\n}\n\nimpl Rules {\n    fn own(&self, step: &str) -> Vec<&CapabilityView> {\n        self.grants.iter().filter(|g| g.step == step).collect()\n    }\n\n    fn kind(&self, stage: &str) -> Vec<&CapabilityView> {\n        let kind = self.grants.iter();\n        kind.filter(|g| g.step.is_empty() && g.stage == stage)\n            .collect()\n    }\n}\n\n/// The steps a constraint applies at once `step` is added to or taken off\n/// them; none when taking it off would leave none, which means every step.\nfn rescoped(c: &ConstraintView, step: &str, add: bool) -> Option<Vec<String>> {\n    let mut steps: Vec<String> = c.steps.iter().filter(|s| *s != step).cloned().collect();\n    if add {\n        steps.push(step.into());\n    }\n    (!steps.is_empty()).then_some(steps)\n}\n\npub fn update(rules: &mut Rules, msg: Msg, at: &At, ctx: &Ctx) -> Task<Msg> {\n    match msg {\n        Msg::Constraints(Ok(all)) => rules.constraints = all,\n        Msg::Grants(Ok(all)) => rules.grants = all,\n        Msg::Constraints(Err(e)) | Msg::Grants(Err(e)) | Msg::Done(Err(e)) => rules.said = e,\n        Msg::Done(Ok(_)) => {\n            rules.said.clear();\n            return load(ctx);\n        }\n        Msg::Function(f) => rules.function = f,\n        Msg::Rung(r) => rules.rung = r,\n        Msg::Scope(id, add) => {\n            let Some(c) = rules.constraints.iter().find(|c| c.id == id) else {\n                return Task::none();\n            };\n            let Some(steps) = rescoped(c, at.step, add) else {\n                rules.said = format!(\n                    \"This is the only step {id} applies at; taking it off would apply it at every step. Change it on the Constraints page.\"\n                );\n                return Task::none();\n            };\n            return send(ctx, api::ConstraintSteps { id, steps });\n        }\n        Msg::Own => {\n            let copies = rules.kind(at.stage).into_iter().map(|g| CapabilityView {\n                step: at.step.into(),\n                ..g.clone()\n            });\n            return Task::batch(copies.map(|g| send(ctx, api::CapabilityAdd(g))));\n        }\n        Msg::Kind => {\n            let own = rules.own(at.step).into_iter().cloned();\n            return Task::batch(own.map(|g| send(ctx, api::CapabilityRemove(g))));\n        }\n        Msg::Move(g, up) => {\n            let moved = api::CapabilityMove {\n                stage: g.stage,\n                step: g.step,\n                function: g.function,\n                up,\n            };\n            return send(ctx, moved);\n        }\n        Msg::Add => {\n            let grant = CapabilityView {\n                stage: at.stage.into(),\n                step: at.step.into(),\n                function: rules.function.trim().into(),\n                rung: if rules.rung.is_empty() {\n                    \"ask\".into()\n                } else {\n                    rules.rung.clone()\n                },\n            };\n            rules.function.clear();\n            return send(ctx, api::CapabilityAdd(grant));\n        }\n    }\n    Task::none()\n}\n\nfn small<'a>(label: &'a str, msg: Option<Msg>) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n    button(text(label).size(12))\n        .padding([3, 10])\n        .style(theme::secondary)\n        .on_press_maybe(msg)\n        .into()\n}\n\nfn chip<'a>(label: String) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n    container(text(label).size(12).color(theme::MUTED))\n        .padding([2, 8])\n        .style(theme::chip)\n        .into()\n}\n\n/// The constraints that apply at the step, and a picker for one that\n/// applies at other steps to apply here too.\nfn constraints<'a>(rules: &Rules, at: &At, editable: bool) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n    let here = rules\n        .constraints\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|c| c.steps.is_empty() || c.steps.iter().any(|s| s == at.step));\n    let rows = here.map(|c| {\n        let scope = match c.steps.is_empty() {\n            true => chip(\"every step\".into()),\n            false => small(\n                \"Not here\",\n                editable.then(|| Msg::Scope(c.id.clone(), false)),\n            ),\n        };\n        row![\n            chip(c.rung.clone()),\n            text(c.rule.clone()).size(13).width(Fill),\n            scope\n        ]\n        .spacing(8)\n        .align_y(iced::Center)\n        .into()\n    });\n    let elsewhere: Vec<Choice> = rules\n        .constraints\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|c| !c.steps.is_empty() && !c.steps.iter().any(|s| s == at.step))\n        .map(|c| Choice::new(&c.id, &c.rule))\n        .collect();\n    let mut body = Column::with_children(rows).spacing(6);\n    if editable && !elsewhere.is_empty() {\n        let add = pick_list(elsewhere, None::<Choice>, |c| Msg::Scope(c.id, true))\n            .placeholder(\"Also apply here a constraint for other steps…\")\n            .text_size(12)\n            .style(theme::select);\n        body = body.push(add);\n    }\n    body.into()\n}\n\n/// One grant: its rung and its function, with its ladder when the step's\n/// own grant may be changed.\nfn grant_line<'a>(g: &CapabilityView, changeable: bool) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n    let line = row![\n        chip(g.rung.clone()),\n        text(g.function.clone()).size(13).width(Fill)\n    ]\n    .spacing(8)\n    .align_y(iced::Center);\n    if !changeable {\n        return line.into();\n    }\n    let go = |up| Msg::Move(g.clone(), up);\n    let down = if g.rung == \"ask\" { \"Remove\" } else { \"Demote\" };\n    let up = (g.rung != \"allowed\").then(|| go(true));\n    line.push(small(down, Some(go(false))))\n        .push(small(\"Promote\", up))\n        .into()\n}\n\n/// The form for one more of the step's own grants, and the way back to\n/// its kind's.\nfn grant_form(rules: &Rules) -> Element<'_, Msg> {\n    let rungs = vec![\"ask\".to_string(), \"allowed\".into()];\n    let rung = Some(rules.rung.clone()).filter(|r| !r.is_empty());\n    let named = !rules.function.trim().is_empty();\n    row![\n        text_input(\"sandbox::fs::read\", &rules.function)\n            .on_input(Msg::Function)\n            .style(theme::field),\n        pick_list(rungs, rung.or(Some(\"ask\".into())), Msg::Rung).style(theme::select),\n        small(\"Grant\", named.then_some(Msg::Add)),\n        small(\"Use its kind's instead\", Some(Msg::Kind)),\n    ]\n    .spacing(8)\n    .align_y(iced::Center)\n    .into()\n}\n\n/// The grants that decide the step's calls: its own, with their ladder and\n/// a form to add one, or its kind's, which it may take as its own.\nfn grants<'a>(rules: &'a Rules, at: &At, editable: bool) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n    let own = rules.own(at.step);\n    let mine = !own.is_empty();\n    let shown = if mine { own } else { rules.kind(at.stage) };\n    let rows = shown.into_iter().map(|g| grant_line(g, mine && editable));\n    let title = match mine {\n        true => \"This step's own grants. A call none covers is refused.\",\n        false => \"Its kind's grants. A call none covers is refused.\",\n    };\n    let body = Column::with_children(rows).spacing(6);\n    let body = match (editable, mine) {\n        (true, true) => body.push(grant_form(rules)),\n        (true, false) => body.push(small(\"Give this step its own grants\", Some(Msg::Own))),\n        _ => body,\n    };\n    column![text(title).size(12).color(theme::MUTED), body]\n        .spacing(6)\n        .into()\n}\n\nfn panel<'a>(title: &'a str, body: Element<'a, Msg>) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n    labeled(\n        title,\n        container(body).padding(12).width(Fill).style(theme::panel),\n    )\n}\n\n/// The step's constraints and its capabilities, each in its own section,\n/// then why the last change failed, when one did.\npub fn view<'a>(rules: &'a Rules, at: &At, editable: bool) -> Vec<Element<'a, Msg>> {\n    let mut all = vec![\n        panel(\"Constraints\", constraints(rules, at, editable)),\n        panel(\"Capabilities\", grants(rules, at, editable)),\n    ];\n    if !rules.said.is_empty() {\n        all.push(text(&rules.said).size(13).color(theme::BAD).into());\n    }\n    all\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn taking_a_constraint_off_its_only_step_is_refused() {\n        let c = ConstraintView {\n            steps: vec![\"short/build\".into()],\n            ..ConstraintView::default()\n        };\n        assert_eq!(rescoped(&c, \"short/build\", false), None, \"else every step\");\n        assert_eq!(\n            rescoped(&c, \"short/plan\", true),\n            Some(vec![\"short/build\".to_string(), \"short/plan\".to_string()])\n        );\n        let two = ConstraintView {\n            steps: vec![\"short/build\".into(), \"short/plan\".into()],\n            ..ConstraintView::default()\n        };\n        assert_eq!(\n            rescoped(&two, \"short/build\", false),\n            Some(vec![\"short/plan\".to_string()])\n        );\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn a_step_shows_its_own_grants_once_it_has_any() {\n        let grant = |stage: &str, step: &str| CapabilityView {\n            stage: stage.into(),\n            step: step.into(),\n            function: \"sandbox::*\".into(),\n            rung: \"allowed\".into(),\n        };\n        let rules = Rules {\n            grants: vec![\n                grant(\"prompt\", \"\"),\n                grant(\"agent\", \"\"),\n                grant(\"prompt\", \"short/review\"),\n            ],\n            ..Rules::default()\n        };\n        assert_eq!(rules.kind(\"prompt\").len(), 1);\n        assert_eq!(rules.own(\"short/review\").len(), 1);\n        assert!(rules.own(\"short/build\").is_empty());\n    }\n}\n","numLines":327,"startLine":1,"totalLines":327}},"displayPath":"crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules.rs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3480d684-4b7e-4be3-ba14-0dff553b753f","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:56:18.329Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules.rs\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t//! The rules at one workflow step, on the workflows page (D44, D48): the\n2\t//! constraints that apply there, and the grants that decide what its\n3\t//! agent's calls may do. A step uses its kind's grants until it has its own,\n4\t//! which then take their place.\n5\t\n6\tuse bastion_protocol::api::{self, Request};\n7\tuse bastion_protocol::{CapabilityView, ConstraintView};\n8\tuse iced::widget::{Column, button, column, container, pick_list, row, text, text_input};\n9\tuse iced::{Element, Fill, Task};\n10\t\n11\tuse super::{Choice, Ctx, labeled};\n12\tuse crate::theme;\n13\t\n14\t#[derive(Default)]\n15\tpub struct Rules {\n16\t    constraints: Vec<ConstraintView>,\n17\t    grants: Vec<CapabilityView>,\n18\t    /// A new grant for the step, as the form holds it.\n19\t    function: String,\n20\t    rung: String,\n21\t    said: String,\n22\t}\n23\t\n24\t#[derive(Clone, Debug)]\n25\tpub enum Msg {\n26\t    Constraints(Result<Vec<ConstraintView>, String>),\n27\t    Grants(Result<Vec<CapabilityView>, String>),\n28\t    /// Apply a constraint at the step too, or take it off the step.\n29\t    Scope(String, bool),\n30\t    /// Give the step its own grants, starting from its kind's.\n31\t    Own,\n32\t    /// Take the step's own grants back, so its kind's apply.\n33\t    Kind,\n34\t    Move(CapabilityView, bool),\n35\t    Function(String),\n36\t    Rung(String),\n37\t    Add,\n38\t    Done(Result<(), String>),\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\t/// The step a page shows rules for: its name, `workflow/step`, and its kind.\n42\tpub struct At<'a> {\n43\t    pub step: &'a str,\n44\t    pub stage: &'a str,\n45\t}\n46\t\n47\tpub fn load(ctx: &Ctx) -> Task<Msg> {\n48\t    Task::batch([\n49\t        ctx.task(&ctx.current, api::Constraints, Msg::Constraints),\n50\t        ctx.task(&ctx.current, api::Capabilities, Msg::Grants),\n51\t    ])\n52\t}\n53\t\n54\tfn send<R>(ctx: &Ctx, request: R) -> Task<Msg>\n55\twhere\n56\t    R: Request<Answer = ()> + Send + Sync + 'static,\n57\t{\n58\t    ctx.task(&ctx.current, request, Msg::Done)\n59\t}\n60\t\n61\timpl Rules {\n62\t    fn own(&self, step: &str) -> Vec<&CapabilityView> {\n63\t        self.grants.iter().filter(|g| g.step == step).collect()\n64\t    }\n65\t\n66\t    fn kind(&self, stage: &str) -> Vec<&CapabilityView> {\n67\t        let kind = self.grants.iter();\n68\t        kind.filter(|g| g.step.is_empty() && g.stage == stage)\n69\t            .collect()\n70\t    }\n71\t}\n72\t\n73\t/// The steps a constraint applies at once `step` is added to or taken off\n74\t/// them; none when taking it off would leave none, which means every step.\n75\tfn rescoped(c: &ConstraintView, step: &str, add: bool) -> Option<Vec<String>> {\n76\t    let mut steps: Vec<String> = c.steps.iter().filter(|s| *s != step).cloned().collect();\n77\t    if add {\n78\t        steps.push(step.into());\n79\t    }\n80\t    (!steps.is_empty()).then_some(steps)\n81\t}\n82\t\n83\tpub fn update(rules: &mut Rules, msg: Msg, at: &At, ctx: &Ctx) -> Task<Msg> {\n84\t    match msg {\n85\t        Msg::Constraints(Ok(all)) => rules.constraints = all,\n86\t        Msg::Grants(Ok(all)) => rules.grants = all,\n87\t        Msg::Constraints(Err(e)) | Msg::Grants(Err(e)) | Msg::Done(Err(e)) => rules.said = e,\n88\t        Msg::Done(Ok(_)) => {\n89\t            rules.said.clear();\n90\t            return load(ctx);\n91\t        }\n92\t        Msg::Function(f) => rules.function = f,\n93\t        Msg::Rung(r) => rules.rung = r,\n94\t        Msg::Scope(id, add) => {\n95\t            let Some(c) = rules.constraints.iter().find(|c| c.id == id) else {\n96\t                return Task::none();\n97\t            };\n98\t            let Some(steps) = rescoped(c, at.step, add) else {\n99\t                rules.said = format!(\n100\t                    \"This is the only step {id} applies at; taking it off would apply it at every step. Change it on the Constraints page.\"\n101\t                );\n102\t                return Task::none();\n103\t            };\n104\t            return send(ctx, api::ConstraintSteps { id, steps });\n105\t        }\n106\t        Msg::Own => {\n107\t            let copies = rules.kind(at.stage).into_iter().map(|g| CapabilityView {\n108\t                step: at.step.into(),\n109\t                ..g.clone()\n110\t            });\n111\t            return Task::batch(copies.map(|g| send(ctx, api::CapabilityAdd(g))));\n112\t        }\n113\t        Msg::Kind => {\n114\t            let own = rules.own(at.step).into_iter().cloned();\n115\t            return Task::batch(own.map(|g| send(ctx, api::CapabilityRemove(g))));\n116\t        }\n117\t        Msg::Move(g, up) => {\n118\t            let moved = api::CapabilityMove {\n119\t                stage: g.stage,\n120\t                step: g.step,\n121\t                function: g.function,\n122\t                up,\n123\t            };\n124\t            return send(ctx, moved);\n125\t        }\n126\t        Msg::Add => {\n127\t            let grant = CapabilityView {\n128\t                stage: at.stage.into(),\n129\t                step: at.step.into(),\n130\t                function: rules.function.trim().into(),\n131\t                rung: if rules.rung.is_empty() {\n132\t                    \"ask\".into()\n133\t                } else {\n134\t                    rules.rung.clone()\n135\t                },\n136\t            };\n137\t            rules.function.clear();\n138\t            return send(ctx, api::CapabilityAdd(grant));\n139\t        }\n140\t    }\n141\t    Task::none()\n142\t}\n143\t\n144\tfn small<'a>(label: &'a str, msg: Option<Msg>) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n145\t    button(text(label).size(12))\n146\t        .padding([3, 10])\n147\t        .style(theme::secondary)\n148\t        .on_press_maybe(msg)\n149\t        .into()\n150\t}\n151\t\n152\tfn chip<'a>(label: String) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n153\t    container(text(label).size(12).color(theme::MUTED))\n154\t        .padding([2, 8])\n155\t        .style(theme::chip)\n156\t        .into()\n157\t}\n158\t\n159\t/// The constraints that apply at the step, and a picker for one that\n160\t/// applies at other steps to apply here too.\n161\tfn constraints<'a>(rules: &Rules, at: &At, editable: bool) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n162\t    let here = rules\n163\t        .constraints\n164\t        .iter()\n165\t        .filter(|c| c.steps.is_empty() || c.steps.iter().any(|s| s == at.step));\n166\t    let rows = here.map(|c| {\n167\t        let scope = match c.steps.is_empty() {\n168\t            true => chip(\"every step\".into()),\n169\t            false => small(\n170\t                \"Not here\",\n171\t                editable.then(|| Msg::Scope(c.id.clone(), false)),\n172\t            ),\n173\t        };\n174\t        row![\n175\t            chip(c.rung.clone()),\n176\t            text(c.rule.clone()).size(13).width(Fill),\n177\t            scope\n178\t        ]\n179\t        .spacing(8)\n180\t        .align_y(iced::Center)\n181\t        .into()\n182\t    });\n183\t    let elsewhere: Vec<Choice> = rules\n184\t        .constraints\n185\t        .iter()\n186\t        .filter(|c| !c.steps.is_empty() && !c.steps.iter().any(|s| s == at.step))\n187\t        .map(|c| Choice::new(&c.id, &c.rule))\n188\t        .collect();\n189\t    let mut body = Column::with_children(rows).spacing(6);\n190\t    if editable && !elsewhere.is_empty() {\n191\t        let add = pick_list(elsewhere, None::<Choice>, |c| Msg::Scope(c.id, true))\n192\t            .placeholder(\"Also apply here a constraint for other steps…\")\n193\t            .text_size(12)\n194\t            .style(theme::select);\n195\t        body = body.push(add);\n196\t    }\n197\t    body.into()\n198\t}\n199\t\n200\t/// One grant: its rung and its function, with its ladder when the step's\n201\t/// own grant may be changed.\n202\tfn grant_line<'a>(g: &CapabilityView, changeable: bool) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n203\t    let line = row![\n204\t        chip(g.rung.clone()),\n205\t        text(g.function.clone()).size(13).width(Fill)\n206\t    ]\n207\t    .spacing(8)\n208\t    .align_y(iced::Center);\n209\t    if !changeable {\n210\t        return line.into();\n211\t    }\n212\t    let go = |up| Msg::Move(g.clone(), up);\n213\t    let down = if g.rung == \"ask\" { \"Remove\" } else { \"Demote\" };\n214\t    let up = (g.rung != \"allowed\").then(|| go(true));\n215\t    line.push(small(down, Some(go(false))))\n216\t        .push(small(\"Promote\", up))\n217\t        .into()\n218\t}\n219\t\n220\t/// The form for one more of the step's own grants, and the way back to\n221\t/// its kind's.\n222\tfn grant_form(rules: &Rules) -> Element<'_, Msg> {\n223\t    let rungs = vec![\"ask\".to_string(), \"allowed\".into()];\n224\t    let rung = Some(rules.rung.clone()).filter(|r| !r.is_empty());\n225\t    let named = !rules.function.trim().is_empty();\n226\t    row![\n227\t        text_input(\"sandbox::fs::read\", &rules.function)\n228\t            .on_input(Msg::Function)\n229\t            .style(theme::field),\n230\t        pick_list(rungs, rung.or(Some(\"ask\".into())), Msg::Rung).style(theme::select),\n231\t        small(\"Grant\", named.then_some(Msg::Add)),\n232\t        small(\"Use its kind's instead\", Some(Msg::Kind)),\n233\t    ]\n234\t    .spacing(8)\n235\t    .align_y(iced::Center)\n236\t    .into()\n237\t}\n238\t\n239\t/// The grants that decide the step's calls: its own, with their ladder and\n240\t/// a form to add one, or its kind's, which it may take as its own.\n241\tfn grants<'a>(rules: &'a Rules, at: &At, editable: bool) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n242\t    let own = rules.own(at.step);\n243\t    let mine = !own.is_empty();\n244\t    let shown = if mine { own } else { rules.kind(at.stage) };\n245\t    let rows = shown.into_iter().map(|g| grant_line(g, mine && editable));\n246\t    let title = match mine {\n247\t        true => \"This step's own grants. A call none covers is refused.\",\n248\t        false => \"Its kind's grants. A call none covers is refused.\",\n249\t    };\n250\t    let body = Column::with_children(rows).spacing(6);\n251\t    let body = match (editable, mine) {\n252\t        (true, true) => body.push(grant_form(rules)),\n253\t        (true, false) => body.push(small(\"Give this step its own grants\", Some(Msg::Own))),\n254\t        _ => body,\n255\t    };\n256\t    column![text(title).size(12).color(theme::MUTED), body]\n257\t        .spacing(6)\n258\t        .into()\n259\t}\n260\t\n261\tfn panel<'a>(title: &'a str, body: Element<'a, Msg>) -> Element<'a, Msg> {\n262\t    labeled(\n263\t        title,\n264\t        container(body).padding(12).width(Fill).style(theme::panel),\n265\t    )\n266\t}\n267\t\n268\t/// The step's constraints and its capabilities, each in its own section,\n269\t/// then why the last change failed, when one did.\n270\tpub fn view<'a>(rules: &'a Rules, at: &At, editable: bool) -> Vec<Element<'a, Msg>> {\n271\t    let mut all = vec![\n272\t        panel(\"Constraints\", constraints(rules, at, editable)),\n273\t        panel(\"Capabilities\", grants(rules, at, editable)),\n274\t    ];\n275\t    if !rules.said.is_empty() {\n276\t        all.push(text(&rules.said).size(13).color(theme::BAD).into());\n277\t    }\n278\t    all\n279\t}\n280\t\n281\t#[cfg(test)]\n282\tmod tests {\n283\t    use super::*;\n284\t\n285\t    #[test]\n286\t    fn taking_a_constraint_off_its_only_step_is_refused() {\n287\t        let c = ConstraintView {\n288\t            steps: vec![\"short/build\".into()],\n289\t            ..ConstraintView::default()\n290\t        };\n291\t        assert_eq!(rescoped(&c, \"short/build\", false), None, \"else every step\");\n292\t        assert_eq!(\n293\t            rescoped(&c, \"short/plan\", true),\n294\t            Some(vec![\"short/build\".to_string(), \"short/plan\".to_string()])\n295\t        );\n296\t        let two = ConstraintView {\n297\t            steps: vec![\"short/build\".into(), \"short/plan\".into()],\n298\t            ..ConstraintView::default()\n299\t        };\n300\t        assert_eq!(\n301\t            rescoped(&two, \"short/build\", false),\n302\t            Some(vec![\"short/plan\".to_string()])\n303\t        );\n304\t    }\n305\t\n306\t    #[test]\n307\t    fn a_step_shows_its_own_grants_once_it_has_any() {\n308\t        let grant = |stage: &str, step: &str| CapabilityView {\n309\t            stage: stage.into(),\n310\t            step: step.into(),\n311\t            function: \"sandbox::*\".into(),\n312\t            rung: \"allowed\".into(),\n313\t        };\n314\t        let rules = Rules {\n315\t            grants: vec![\n316\t                grant(\"prompt\", \"\"),\n317\t                grant(\"agent\", \"\"),\n318\t                grant(\"prompt\", \"short/review\"),\n319\t            ],\n320\t            ..Rules::default()\n321\t        };\n322\t        assert_eq!(rules.kind(\"prompt\").len(), 1);\n323\t        assert_eq!(rules.own(\"short/review\").len(), 1);\n324\t        assert!(rules.own(\"short/build\").is_empty());\n325\t    }\n326\t}\n327\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
