-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":63},"type":"attachment","uuid":"582db2da-d169-470b-8557-a8e7c951bce9","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:57:28.372Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"f09e83a8-58c8-4a36-b284-6b7f8a58b143","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"63076884-86c8-4719-937e-cb437c55717e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R4D97oWNALKsghrMDiSkDj","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### worker-compose.yaml configuration\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/tutorials/linkly/foundations.mdx\n\nDeclares the system's containers: the 'http' worker from a remote package, the 'state' worker with an in-memory KV store, and the 'link' worker from a local path. The engine section configures the engine URL for compose operations.\n\n```yaml\nnamespace: default\nengine:\n  url: ws://127.0.0.1:49134\ncontainers:\n  http:\n    worker: package://http\n    version: \"0.21.9\"\n    config_name: http\n\n  state:\n    worker: package://state\n    version: \"0.22.8\"\n    config_name: state\n    config_override:\n      adapter:\n        name: kv\n        config:\n          store_method: in_memory\n\n  link:\n    worker: path://./link\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### compose::add\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/using-iii/compose.mdx\n\nDeclares one or more workers in the compose file and reconciles the project once. Accepts worker names or container objects via CLI or JSON payload.\n\n```APIDOC\n## compose::add\n\n### Description\nDeclares one or more workers in the compose file and reconciles the project once. Accepts worker names or container objects via CLI or JSON payload.\n\n### Method\nCLI command\n\n### Endpoint\n`iii trigger compose::add --namespace dev file=./worker-compose.yaml --json '{\"workers\": [...]}'`\n\n### Parameters\n#### CLI Parameters\n- `worker` (string) - Repeatable - A registry package name, package name with version, or directory path.\n- `file` (string) - Required - The project to edit.\n- `--namespace` (string) - Required - Namespace for the trigger.\n- `--json` (string) - Required - JSON payload containing the workers list.\n\n#### JSON Payload Fields\n- `workers` (array) - Required - A JSON list of worker names or container objects.\n- `worker` (string) - Required - A package name, `name@version`, registry reference, or local path. Also accepts `package://` and `path://` sources.\n- `version` (string) - Optional - Package version. Must agree with a version included in `worker`.\n- `start_after` (array) - Optional - Container keys to start first. Compose adds the package's resolved dependencies to this list.\n- `scripts` (object) - Optional - `pre_run`, `pre_run_timeout`, `run`, and `post_run`. `run` is valid only for local workers.\n- `config_name` (string) - Optional - Name of the worker's base configuration.\n- `config_override` (object) - Optional - Configuration value applied over the base configuration.\n- `working_dir` (string) - Optional - Working directory, relative to the compose file.\n- `environment` (object) - Optional - Environment variables with string values.\n- `env_file` (array) - Optional - List of environment file paths, relative to the compose file.\n- `startup_timeout` (string) - Optional - Maximum wait for worker registration, such as `30s`.\n\n### Request Example\n```json\n{\n  \"workers\": [\n    \"database\",\n    {\n      \"worker\": \"./workers/api\",\n      \"start_after\": [\"database\"],\n      \"scripts\": {\n        \"pre_run\": \"pnpm build\",\n        \"pre_run_timeout\": \"60s\",\n        \"run\": \"pnpm start\",\n        \"post_run\": \"echo stopped\"\n      },\n      \"config_name\": \"api\",\n      \"config_override\": { \"port\": 3000 },\n      \"working_dir\": \"./workers/api\",\n      \"environment\": { \"NODE_ENV\": \"development\" },\n      \"env_file\": [\"./api.env\"],\n      \"startup_timeout\": \"30s\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Response\n#### Success Response\n- **file** (string) - The project edited.\n- **workers** (array) - The list of workers declared.\n\n#### Response Example\nNo explicit response example provided.\n\n### Error Handling\nUnknown fields and invalid field types are rejected. Compose validates the complete edited file before writing any changes.\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### worker-compose.yaml > Engine fields\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/using-iii/compose.mdx\n\n### Engine fields\n\n| Field                             | Type    | Default                | Description                                                                              |\n| --------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `url`                             | string  | `ws://127.0.0.1:49134` | Managed engine endpoint used by Compose and its workers.                                 |\n| `registration_namespace_grace_ms` | integer | engine default         | Namespace-registration grace passed to the engine.                                       |\n| `workers`                         | map     | empty                  | Direct configs for engine-owned workers. Values must be mappings; use `{}` for defaults. |\n\nAllowed worker keys are `configuration`, `iii-worker-manager`, `iii-http-functions`, `iii-stream`,\nand `iii-sandbox`. Use `#instance` for another instance of an allowed type, for example\n`iii-worker-manager#rbac`. The engine injects `iii-engine-functions`, `iii-telemetry` for anonymous\nusage analytics, and `iii-observability` for OpenTelemetry traces, metrics, and logs. Do not declare\nthese workers.\n\n<Note>\n  Changes to these worker configurations take effect only after the engine restarts.\n</Note>\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Managed Compose engine configuration in worker-compose.yaml\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/skills/iii-engine-config/SKILL.md\n\nYAML configuration for a managed Compose engine. The presence of 'engine:' means Compose owns the engine process. Worker values are direct mappings with no nested 'config:' field. Allowed worker base names are 'configuration', 'iii-worker-manager', 'iii-http-functions', 'iii-stream', and 'iii-sandbox'. 'iii-engine-functions', 'iii-telemetry', and 'iii-observability' are injected automatically and must not be declared.\n\n```yaml\nnamespace: orders\nengine:\n  url: ws://127.0.0.1:49134\n  registration_namespace_grace_ms: 5000\n  workers:\n    configuration:\n      adapter:\n        name: fs\n        config:\n          directory: ./config\n    iii-worker-manager:\n      host: 127.0.0.1\n      port: 49134\n    iii-http-functions: {}\n    iii-stream:\n      host: 127.0.0.1\n      port: 3112\n    iii-sandbox:\n      auto_install: true\ncontainers: {}\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### worker-compose.yaml: engine.workers map with engine-owned workers\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/upgrading/workers-to-compose.mdx.skill.md\n\nThe new engine section moves five engine-owned worker configs into the engine.workers map. Each value is the worker config; the old nested config: key must not be kept. Multiple instances use a #instance suffix. engine.url defaults to ws://127.0.0.1:49134. Compose writes the engine-only representation to <project-dir>/.iii/compose/<daemon-namespace>/engine-config.yaml by default, or $III_COMPOSE_STATE_DIR/<project-slug>/<daemon-namespace>/engine-config.yaml if set, with owner-only permissions and starts the engine from it; do not edit that generated file.\n\n```yaml\n# namespace: default\nengine:\n  url: ws://127.0.0.1:49134\n  registration_namespace_grace_ms: 5000\n  workers:\n    configuration:\n      adapter:\n        name: fs\n        config:\n          directory: ./config\n    iii-worker-manager:\n      host: 127.0.0.1\n      port: 49134\n    iii-http-functions: {}\n    iii-stream:\n      host: 127.0.0.1\n      port: 3112\n    iii-sandbox:\n      auto_install: true\n\n```"}]}]},"uuid":"d7f5c597-461f-4dfa-be18-5f175edf4a79","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:57:30.304Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"### worker-compose.yaml configuration\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/tutorials/linkly/foundations.mdx\n\nDeclares the system's containers: the 'http' worker from a remote package, the 'state' worker with an in-memory KV store, and the 'link' worker from a local path. The engine section configures the engine URL for compose operations.\n\n```yaml\nnamespace: default\nengine:\n  url: ws://127.0.0.1:49134\ncontainers:\n  http:\n    worker: package://http\n    version: \"0.21.9\"\n    config_name: http\n\n  state:\n    worker: package://state\n    version: \"0.22.8\"\n    config_name: state\n    config_override:\n      adapter:\n        name: kv\n        config:\n          store_method: in_memory\n\n  link:\n    worker: path://./link\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### compose::add\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/using-iii/compose.mdx\n\nDeclares one or more workers in the compose file and reconciles the project once. Accepts worker names or container objects via CLI or JSON payload.\n\n```APIDOC\n## compose::add\n\n### Description\nDeclares one or more workers in the compose file and reconciles the project once. Accepts worker names or container objects via CLI or JSON payload.\n\n### Method\nCLI command\n\n### Endpoint\n`iii trigger compose::add --namespace dev file=./worker-compose.yaml --json '{\"workers\": [...]}'`\n\n### Parameters\n#### CLI Parameters\n- `worker` (string) - Repeatable - A registry package name, package name with version, or directory path.\n- `file` (string) - Required - The project to edit.\n- `--namespace` (string) - Required - Namespace for the trigger.\n- `--json` (string) - Required - JSON payload containing the workers list.\n\n#### JSON Payload Fields\n- `workers` (array) - Required - A JSON list of worker names or container objects.\n- `worker` (string) - Required - A package name, `name@version`, registry reference, or local path. Also accepts `package://` and `path://` sources.\n- `version` (string) - Optional - Package version. Must agree with a version included in `worker`.\n- `start_after` (array) - Optional - Container keys to start first. Compose adds the package's resolved dependencies to this list.\n- `scripts` (object) - Optional - `pre_run`, `pre_run_timeout`, `run`, and `post_run`. `run` is valid only for local workers.\n- `config_name` (string) - Optional - Name of the worker's base configuration.\n- `config_override` (object) - Optional - Configuration value applied over the base configuration.\n- `working_dir` (string) - Optional - Working directory, relative to the compose file.\n- `environment` (object) - Optional - Environment variables with string values.\n- `env_file` (array) - Optional - List of environment file paths, relative to the compose file.\n- `startup_timeout` (string) - Optional - Maximum wait for worker registration, such as `30s`.\n\n### Request Example\n```json\n{\n  \"workers\": [\n    \"database\",\n    {\n      \"worker\": \"./workers/api\",\n      \"start_after\": [\"database\"],\n      \"scripts\": {\n        \"pre_run\": \"pnpm build\",\n        \"pre_run_timeout\": \"60s\",\n        \"run\": \"pnpm start\",\n        \"post_run\": \"echo stopped\"\n      },\n      \"config_name\": \"api\",\n      \"config_override\": { \"port\": 3000 },\n      \"working_dir\": \"./workers/api\",\n      \"environment\": { \"NODE_ENV\": \"development\" },\n      \"env_file\": [\"./api.env\"],\n      \"startup_timeout\": \"30s\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Response\n#### Success Response\n- **file** (string) - The project edited.\n- **workers** (array) - The list of workers declared.\n\n#### Response Example\nNo explicit response example provided.\n\n### Error Handling\nUnknown fields and invalid field types are rejected. Compose validates the complete edited file before writing any changes.\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### worker-compose.yaml > Engine fields\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/using-iii/compose.mdx\n\n### Engine fields\n\n| Field                             | Type    | Default                | Description                                                                              |\n| --------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `url`                             | string  | `ws://127.0.0.1:49134` | Managed engine endpoint used by Compose and its workers.                                 |\n| `registration_namespace_grace_ms` | integer | engine default         | Namespace-registration grace passed to the engine.                                       |\n| `workers`                         | map     | empty                  | Direct configs for engine-owned workers. Values must be mappings; use `{}` for defaults. |\n\nAllowed worker keys are `configuration`, `iii-worker-manager`, `iii-http-functions`, `iii-stream`,\nand `iii-sandbox`. Use `#instance` for another instance of an allowed type, for example\n`iii-worker-manager#rbac`. The engine injects `iii-engine-functions`, `iii-telemetry` for anonymous\nusage analytics, and `iii-observability` for OpenTelemetry traces, metrics, and logs. Do not declare\nthese workers.\n\n<Note>\n  Changes to these worker configurations take effect only after the engine restarts.\n</Note>\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Managed Compose engine configuration in worker-compose.yaml\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/skills/iii-engine-config/SKILL.md\n\nYAML configuration for a managed Compose engine. The presence of 'engine:' means Compose owns the engine process. Worker values are direct mappings with no nested 'config:' field. Allowed worker base names are 'configuration', 'iii-worker-manager', 'iii-http-functions', 'iii-stream', and 'iii-sandbox'. 'iii-engine-functions', 'iii-telemetry', and 'iii-observability' are injected automatically and must not be declared.\n\n```yaml\nnamespace: orders\nengine:\n  url: ws://127.0.0.1:49134\n  registration_namespace_grace_ms: 5000\n  workers:\n    configuration:\n      adapter:\n        name: fs\n        config:\n          directory: ./config\n    iii-worker-manager:\n      host: 127.0.0.1\n      port: 49134\n    iii-http-functions: {}\n    iii-stream:\n      host: 127.0.0.1\n      port: 3112\n    iii-sandbox:\n      auto_install: true\ncontainers: {}\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### worker-compose.yaml: engine.workers map with engine-owned workers\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/upgrading/workers-to-compose.mdx.skill.md\n\nThe new engine section moves five engine-owned worker configs into the engine.workers map. Each value is the worker config; the old nested config: key must not be kept. Multiple instances use a #instance suffix. engine.url defaults to ws://127.0.0.1:49134. Compose writes the engine-only representation to <project-dir>/.iii/compose/<daemon-namespace>/engine-config.yaml by default, or $III_COMPOSE_STATE_DIR/<project-slug>/<daemon-namespace>/engine-config.yaml if set, with owner-only permissions and starts the engine from it; do not edit that generated file.\n\n```yaml\n# namespace: default\nengine:\n  url: ws://127.0.0.1:49134\n  registration_namespace_grace_ms: 5000\n  workers:\n    configuration:\n      adapter:\n        name: fs\n        config:\n          directory: ./config\n    iii-worker-manager:\n      host: 127.0.0.1\n      port: 49134\n    iii-http-functions: {}\n    iii-stream:\n      host: 127.0.0.1\n      port: 3112\n    iii-sandbox:\n      auto_install: true\n\n```"}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"13c7c875-75eb-48b7-8a20-92db79d069f4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Context7","title":"Context7","icons":[{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.svg","mimeType":"image/svg+xml","sizes":["any"]},{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.png","mimeType":"image/png","sizes":["512x512"]}],"version":"4.5.0","websiteUrl":"https://context7.com","description":"Context7 provides up-to-date documentation and code examples for libraries and frameworks."}}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f09e83a8-58c8-4a36-b284-6b7f8a58b143","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
