{"parentUuid":"ae8e55a1-2ab9-4a62-8d71-2038a29abc55","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:mcp__context7__query-docs","toolUseID":"toolu_01XLcPpi924Hqxc5RwNX9KCo","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"if [ -n \"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR:-}\" ] && [ -x /bin/zsh ]; then exec /bin/zsh -fc 'LC_ALL=C␤export CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-$PPID}␤export CMUX_AGENT_HOOK_INVOKER_PID=$PPID␤cmux_fallback() { { print -rn -- \"$cmux_p\"; /bin/cat; } | /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3; exit $?; }␤zmodload zsh/system zsh/datetime zsh/files 2>/dev/null || exec /bin/sh -c \"$1\" >&3␤cmux_p= cmux_c= cmux_e=0␤while (( ${#cmux_p} < 262144 )); do sysread -i 0 -s 65536 cmux_c || { cmux_e=$?; break; }; cmux_p+=$cmux_c; done␤[[ -n ${CMUX_SURFACE_ID:-} && ${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED:-} != 1 ]] || { (( cmux_e == 5 )) || /bin/cat >/dev/null; print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3; exit 0; }␤cmux_d=$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_SPOOL_DIR␤(( cmux_e == 5 )) && [[ -f $cmux_d/keys ]] || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤cmux_r=\"cmux-agent-hook-v1\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"claude\"$'\\''\\n'\\''\"$2\"$'\\''\\n'\\''␤for cmux_k in ${(f)\"$(<$cmux_d/keys)\"}; do (( ${+parameters[$cmux_k]} )) && cmux_r+=\"$cmux_k=${(P)cmux_k}\"$'\\''\\0'\\''; done␤cmux_r+=$'\\''\\0'\\''\"$cmux_p\"␤(( ${#cmux_r} <= 524288 )) || cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤umask 077␤cmux_n=$cmux_d/$epochtime[1].$epochtime[2]-$$␤{ print -rn -- \"$cmux_r\" >| $cmux_n.tmp && mv -f -- $cmux_n.tmp $cmux_n.rec; } 2>/dev/null || { rm -f -- $cmux_n.tmp 2>/dev/null; cmux_fallback \"$1\"; }␤if zsystem flock -t 0 -r -f cmux_l $cmux_d/forwarder.lock 2>/dev/null; then␤  zsystem flock -u $cmux_l␤  rm -- $cmux_n.rec 2>/dev/null && cmux_fallback \"$1\"␤fi␤print -r -- '\\''{}'\\'' >&3' cmux-hook 'cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":67},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1027b970-2685-46b4-8f64-32add0e1fefb","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:57:32.945Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"ae8e55a1-2ab9-4a62-8d71-2038a29abc55","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"63076884-86c8-4719-937e-cb437c55717e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XLcPpi924Hqxc5RwNX9KCo","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Consider the agent\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/website/content/blog/add-a-worker.md\n\nAn agent needs to speak MCP to an external tool server. **Add a worker** that\nbridges MCP into `trigger()` calls. The bridge is a worker like any other.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### registerFunction (Node.js)\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/skills/iii-sdk-reference/SKILL.md\n\nRegisters a local function that can be invoked by the III server. The handler receives an input object and returns a result.\n\n```APIDOC\n## registerFunction(id, handler, options?)\n\n### Description\nRegisters a local function with the III worker.\n\n### Parameters\n- **id** (string) - Required - Unique identifier for the function.\n- **handler** (function) - Required - Async function that processes input and returns a result.\n- **options** (object) - Optional - Additional registration options.\n\n### Example\n```typescript\niii.registerFunction(\"users::lookup\", async (input) => {\n  new Logger().info(\"looking up user\", { userId: input.userId });\n  return { userId: input.userId, name: \"Ada\" };\n});\n```\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Move project workers to containers with worker-compose.yaml\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/upgrading/workers-to-compose.mdx.skill.md\n\nExample Compose configuration for moving project workers to containers. Copy each old worker's config value to config_override, preserve storage paths, and pin the package version. Translate iii-exec commands into pre_run, run, and post_run; custom local workers use path:// while registry workers use package:// plus a version.\n\n```yaml\ncontainers:\n  state:\n    worker: package://api.workers.iii.dev/state\n    version: \"0.22.2\"\n    config_name: state\n    config_override:\n      adapter:\n        name: kv\n        config:\n          store_method: file_based\n          file_path: ./data/state_store.db\n  http:\n    worker: package://api.workers.iii.dev/http\n    version: \"0.21.3\"\n    config_name: http\n    config_override:\n      host: 127.0.0.1\n      port: 3111\n  app:\n    worker: path://.\n    start_after: [state, http]\n    scripts:\n      pre_run: pnpm build\n      run: pnpm start\n      post_run: pnpm cleanup\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Engine-managed exceptions\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/using-iii/workers.mdx.skill.md\n\n`configuration`, `iii-worker-manager`, `iii-http-functions`, `iii-stream`, and `iii-sandbox` remain\nengine-owned. Put them under `engine.workers` for managed Compose, or in `config.yaml` only when an\nexternal supervisor owns the engine. Internal `iii-engine-functions`, `iii-telemetry`, and\n`iii-observability` are injected automatically. They must not be added as Compose package roots.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### worker-compose.yaml > Engine fields\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/using-iii/compose.mdx.skill.md\n\nAllowed worker keys are `configuration`, `iii-worker-manager`, `iii-http-functions`, `iii-stream`,\nand `iii-sandbox`. Use `#instance` for another instance of an allowed type, for example\n`iii-worker-manager#rbac`. The engine injects `iii-engine-functions`, `iii-telemetry` for anonymous\nusage analytics, and `iii-observability` for OpenTelemetry traces, metrics, and logs. Do not declare\nthese workers."}]}]},"uuid":"95aa9177-9f79-4688-809e-5286cb94f53b","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:57:34.622Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"### Consider the agent\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/website/content/blog/add-a-worker.md\n\nAn agent needs to speak MCP to an external tool server. **Add a worker** that\nbridges MCP into `trigger()` calls. The bridge is a worker like any other.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### registerFunction (Node.js)\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/skills/iii-sdk-reference/SKILL.md\n\nRegisters a local function that can be invoked by the III server. The handler receives an input object and returns a result.\n\n```APIDOC\n## registerFunction(id, handler, options?)\n\n### Description\nRegisters a local function with the III worker.\n\n### Parameters\n- **id** (string) - Required - Unique identifier for the function.\n- **handler** (function) - Required - Async function that processes input and returns a result.\n- **options** (object) - Optional - Additional registration options.\n\n### Example\n```typescript\niii.registerFunction(\"users::lookup\", async (input) => {\n  new Logger().info(\"looking up user\", { userId: input.userId });\n  return { userId: input.userId, name: \"Ada\" };\n});\n```\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Move project workers to containers with worker-compose.yaml\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/upgrading/workers-to-compose.mdx.skill.md\n\nExample Compose configuration for moving project workers to containers. Copy each old worker's config value to config_override, preserve storage paths, and pin the package version. Translate iii-exec commands into pre_run, run, and post_run; custom local workers use path:// while registry workers use package:// plus a version.\n\n```yaml\ncontainers:\n  state:\n    worker: package://api.workers.iii.dev/state\n    version: \"0.22.2\"\n    config_name: state\n    config_override:\n      adapter:\n        name: kv\n        config:\n          store_method: file_based\n          file_path: ./data/state_store.db\n  http:\n    worker: package://api.workers.iii.dev/http\n    version: \"0.21.3\"\n    config_name: http\n    config_override:\n      host: 127.0.0.1\n      port: 3111\n  app:\n    worker: path://.\n    start_after: [state, http]\n    scripts:\n      pre_run: pnpm build\n      run: pnpm start\n      post_run: pnpm cleanup\n```\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### Engine-managed exceptions\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/using-iii/workers.mdx.skill.md\n\n`configuration`, `iii-worker-manager`, `iii-http-functions`, `iii-stream`, and `iii-sandbox` remain\nengine-owned. Put them under `engine.workers` for managed Compose, or in `config.yaml` only when an\nexternal supervisor owns the engine. Internal `iii-engine-functions`, `iii-telemetry`, and\n`iii-observability` are injected automatically. They must not be added as Compose package roots.\n\n--------------------------------\n\n### worker-compose.yaml > Engine fields\n\nSource: https://github.com/iii-hq/iii/blob/main/docs/using-iii/compose.mdx.skill.md\n\nAllowed worker keys are `configuration`, `iii-worker-manager`, `iii-http-functions`, `iii-stream`,\nand `iii-sandbox`. Use `#instance` for another instance of an allowed type, for example\n`iii-worker-manager#rbac`. The engine injects `iii-engine-functions`, `iii-telemetry` for anonymous\nusage analytics, and `iii-observability` for OpenTelemetry traces, metrics, and logs. Do not declare\nthese workers."}],"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9f6a1aa1-4c18-4e23-9c5c-e759a459379c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Context7","title":"Context7","icons":[{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.svg","mimeType":"image/svg+xml","sizes":["any"]},{"src":"https://context7.com/context7-icon-green.png","mimeType":"image/png","sizes":["512x512"]}],"version":"4.5.0","websiteUrl":"https://context7.com","description":"Context7 provides up-to-date documentation and code examples for libraries and frameworks."}}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ae8e55a1-2ab9-4a62-8d71-2038a29abc55","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
