{"parentUuid":"1e3c7bb8-3625-40e5-9ef1-eb2385f4a612","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"63076884-86c8-4719-937e-cb437c55717e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XuE2oimhLCu8DkgSy9hDbz","type":"tool_result","content":"# Bastion plan: one bar, every server\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nThe sidebar goes. A bar across the top holds the castle, the pages, and the\nserver switcher. The switcher picks one server, or all of them on the pages\nthat show records: Jobs, Audit Log and Costs. Those pages then add up what\nevery server holds. The pages get one clean layout, and the records get\ngraphs. The cost is width: ten pages and a switcher must fit in one row, so\nthe page names get short and the bar wraps on a narrow window.\n\nThe steps-only plan (S1 to S4) is done; git history holds it. Decisions are\nin [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), and VISION.md says which pages are records\nand which are rules.\n\n## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, is checked live in the app, and is committed before\nthe next.\n\n  that ran.\n\nDone 2026-11-11. Live, the branching job again: plan done, build done,\nchecks failed, report waiting.\n\n### U13. A step's rules on the workflows page (D48)\n\n- An agent's step shows its rules: the constraints that apply there, each\n  marked every step or scoped, with \"Not here\" and a picker to apply one\n  scoped to other steps here too; and its grants.\n- A step uses its kind's grants until \"Give this step its own grants\"\n  copies them as its own, which then take their place; \"Use its kind's\n  instead\" takes them back.\n- A grant is ask or allowed; demoting from ask removes it. Migration 8\n  drops denied grants and limits the rung to ask and allowed.\n\nDone 2026-11-11. Live, on Bug fix's build step: its own grants started as\na copy of the prompt kind's `sandbox::*` allowed, demoted to ask, then\nRemove took it back to the kind's; the audit recorded the grant, the\ndemotion and the removal. Taking a constraint off its only step is\nrefused, as that would apply it at every step.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Where the switcher sits on a narrow window.** The bar wraps. Should the\n  switcher stay on the first row instead?\ncrates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs:33:const TOOLS: [&str; 4] = [\ncrates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs:731:                \"options\": { \"max_turns\": MAX_TURN_STEPS, \"functions\": { \"allow\": TOOLS }, \"metadata\": { \"sandbox_id\": sandbox, \"job\": job.id, \"stage\": stage, \"step\": step, \"reads_only\": job.step().is_some_and(|s| s.reach.reads_only) } },\ncrates/bastion-server/src/factory/onboard.rs:14:use super::{Factory, MAX_TURN_STEPS, NS, TOOL_GUIDE, TOOLS, short_id, turn};\ncrates/bastion-server/src/factory/onboard.rs:108:            \"options\": { \"max_turns\": MAX_TURN_STEPS, \"functions\": { \"allow\": TOOLS },\ncrates/bastion-core/src/charter.rs:20:/// The directory that holds the repository's settings, hooks, agents and\ncrates/bastion-core/src/charter.rs:128:            \"./.agents/hooks/check.sh\",\ncrates/bastion-core/src/eval.rs:97:    /// Calls the repository's hooks refused.\ncrates/bastion-server/src/notify.rs:95:        let url = \"https://hooks.slack.com/services/T000/B000/abcdefgh1234\";\ncrates/bastion-server/src/notify.rs:96:        assert_eq!(masked(url), \"https://hooks.slack.com/…1234\");\ncrates/bastion-server/src/notify.rs:108:        hook.set(\"https://hooks.example/x\").unwrap();\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:3://! permissions become constraints and whose hooks run in the job's VM.\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:18:pub struct Hook {\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:28:    /// `PreToolUse` hooks: they run before a matching call, and exit 2 refuses it.\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:29:    pub before: Vec<Hook>,\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:30:    /// `Stop` hooks: they run when a build turn ends, and their results are kept.\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:62:            found.before = hooks(&settings, \"PreToolUse\");\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:63:            found.stop = hooks(&settings, \"Stop\")\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:76:fn hooks(settings: &Value, event: &str) -> Vec<Hook> {\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:77:    let groups = settings[\"hooks\"][event].as_array().into_iter().flatten();\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:81:            group[\"hooks\"]\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:87:                .map(move |command| Hook {\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:165:        \"hooks\": {\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:166:            \"PreToolUse\": [{ \"matcher\": \"Bash\", \"hooks\": [{ \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"./check.sh\" }] }],\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:167:            \"Stop\": [{ \"hooks\": [{ \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"python3 -m pytest -q\" }] }]\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:172:    fn settings_give_constraints_and_hooks() {\ncrates/bastion-server/src/charter.rs:182:            [Hook {\ncrates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs:490:                    self.gate.stop_hooks(&id, sandbox).await;\ncrates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs:157:            \"{files}; {} rules, {} hooks before calls, {} stop hooks\",\ncrates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs:371:        let hooks: Vec<String> = self\ncrates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs:388:            // The repository's hooks run first, in the VM, so the call waits on them.\ncrates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs:389:            Decision::Continue if !hooks.is_empty() => {\ncrates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs:391:                crate::rt::spawn(async move { gate.before(held, hooks).await });\ncrates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs:392:                json!({ \"decision\": \"hold\", \"reason\": \"The repository's hooks run first.\" })\ncrates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs:457:    /// Run the repository's hooks on a call. Exit 2 from any of them refuses","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"