{"parentUuid":"6ee51d2a-12d4-4ee4-abd9-96a64e84d3b6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01R6mBg9bGwRiPzCPT4LzwXw","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3b52c940-f9ab-4dc1-8e74-88abb5e4f3c8","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:58:29.412Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"3b52c940-f9ab-4dc1-8e74-88abb5e4f3c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx8JGmsEfPSZwqrxkcu6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017iL99vyFRDAwnyUkEHJxKN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","content":"# Bastion plan: more a step may do, more that checks it\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nA step's capabilities grow past iii functions. It may run named shell\ncommands, call more tools, and reach MCP servers. Its constraints grow past\nrules: hooks run before its calls, and a reviewer agent must pass its change\nbefore the job moves on. The cost is reach. Each new capability is a new\nway for an agent to act, so each one starts ungranted and the gate decides\nevery call, the same as today.\n\nThe top-bar plan (U1 to U13) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions\nare in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D49 to D52.\n\n## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, is checked live in the app, and is committed before\nthe next.\n\n### C1. Named commands and more tools (D49)\n\n- A grant on `sandbox::exec` may name a command: `cargo`, or `npm test`.\n  That grant covers a call only when the command line starts with those\n  words.\n- A grant that names a command never covers a line with shell operators\n  (`;`, `&&`, `|`, `` ` ``, `$(`, `>`), because the operators would run a\n  second command. A grant that names no command still covers every line.\n- The most specific grant decides, as today: a named command wins over\n  plain `sandbox::exec`.\n- A turn's `functions.allow` is the four sandbox tools plus every function\n  its step's grants name. Today it is the four tools only, so a grant on\n  any other function can never be called.\n- The step editor's grant form takes the command words.\n- Migration 9 adds `capabilities.command` and puts it in the key.\n\n### C2. Hooks per step (D50)\n\n- A constraint may be a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before\n  each matching call at its steps. Exit 2 refuses the call, and its output\n  is the reason.\n- The charter's `PreToolUse` hooks still run. A step's hooks run after\n  them.\n- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook.\n\n### C3. A reviewer that must pass (D51)\n\n- A constraint may name a reviewer: an agent in `.agents/agents/`. When\n  its step finishes, Bastion runs one turn as that agent on the step's\n  change.\n- The reviewer answers pass or fail with its reasons. A fail fails the\n  step, so the job goes along the failure link or back to the fixer, as\n  D47 says. The step's revisions bound the loop.\n- The reviewer's turn reads only. Its verdict is an artifact on the step,\n  and the job page shows it.\n\n### C4. MCP servers (D52)\n\n- iii ships no MCP bridge; its docs say to write a worker that bridges MCP\n  into `trigger()` calls. `workers/bastion-mcp` is that worker, in Rust\n  (D6).\n- A server lists its MCP servers in Settings: a name, a URL, and the name\n  of the secret that holds its token, if it needs one.\n- The bridge registers each tool of a server as `mcp::<server>::<tool>`.\n  A step's grant on `mcp::github::*` lets its agent call that server's\n  tools, and C1 puts them in the turn's `functions.allow`.\n- Only MCP servers that answer over HTTP, this round. A stdio server runs\n  as a process on the host, outside the VM, and VISION.md says agent work\n  never runs on your machine.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Plugins.** iii has no plugin. Is a plugin a bundle of the above (an\n  agent, its skills, its hooks and its MCP servers) that a step takes as\n  one?\n- **Stdio MCP servers.** Should one run in the job's VM, so a step may use\n  a local MCP server without breaking the VM rule?\n- **Patterns in `functions.allow`.** I don't know yet whether the harness\n  takes `mcp::github::*` or needs each function by name. C1 checks it live,\n  and if it needs names, Bastion expands the pattern from the engine's\n  function list.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_read_input_tokens":113203,"output_tokens":1427,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1427,"cache_read_input_tokens":113203,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017iL99vyFRDAwnyUkEHJxKN":{"file_path":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","content":"# Bastion plan: more a step may do, more that checks it\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nA step's capabilities grow past iii functions. It may run named shell\ncommands, call more tools, and reach MCP servers. Its constraints grow past\nrules: hooks run before its calls, and a reviewer agent must pass its change\nbefore the job moves on. The cost is reach. Each new capability is a new\nway for an agent to act, so each one starts ungranted and the gate decides\nevery call, the same as today.\n\nThe top-bar plan (U1 to U13) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions\nare in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D49 to D52.\n\n## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, is checked live in the app, and is committed before\nthe next.\n\n### C1. Named commands and more tools (D49)\n\n- A grant on `sandbox::exec` may name a command: `cargo`, or `npm test`.\n  That grant covers a call only when the command line starts with those\n  words.\n- A grant that names a command never covers a line with shell operators\n  (`;`, `&&`, `|`, `` ` ``, `$(`, `>`), because the operators would run a\n  second command. A grant that names no command still covers every line.\n- The most specific grant decides, as today: a named command wins over\n  plain `sandbox::exec`.\n- A turn's `functions.allow` is the four sandbox tools plus every function\n  its step's grants name. Today it is the four tools only, so a grant on\n  any other function can never be called.\n- The step editor's grant form takes the command words.\n- Migration 9 adds `capabilities.command` and puts it in the key.\n\n### C2. Hooks per step (D50)\n\n- A constraint may be a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before\n  each matching call at its steps. Exit 2 refuses the call, and its output\n  is the reason.\n- The charter's `PreToolUse` hooks still run. A step's hooks run after\n  them.\n- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook.\n\n### C3. A reviewer that must pass (D51)\n\n- A constraint may name a reviewer: an agent in `.agents/agents/`. When\n  its step finishes, Bastion runs one turn as that agent on the step's\n  change.\n- The reviewer answers pass or fail with its reasons. A fail fails the\n  step, so the job goes along the failure link or back to the fixer, as\n  D47 says. The step's revisions bound the loop.\n- The reviewer's turn reads only. Its verdict is an artifact on the step,\n  and the job page shows it.\n\n### C4. MCP servers (D52)\n\n- iii ships no MCP bridge; its docs say to write a worker that bridges MCP\n  into `trigger()` calls. `workers/bastion-mcp` is that worker, in Rust\n  (D6).\n- A server lists its MCP servers in Settings: a name, a URL, and the name\n  of the secret that holds its token, if it needs one.\n- The bridge registers each tool of a server as `mcp::<server>::<tool>`.\n  A step's grant on `mcp::github::*` lets its agent call that server's\n  tools, and C1 puts them in the turn's `functions.allow`.\n- Only MCP servers that answer over HTTP, this round. A stdio server runs\n  as a process on the host, outside the VM, and VISION.md says agent work\n  never runs on your machine.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Plugins.** iii has no plugin. Is a plugin a bundle of the above (an\n  agent, its skills, its hooks and its MCP servers) that a step takes as\n  one?\n- **Stdio MCP servers.** Should one run in the job's VM, so a step may use\n  a local MCP server without breaking the VM rule?\n- **Patterns in `functions.allow`.** I don't know yet whether the harness\n  takes `mcp::github::*` or needs each function by name. C1 checks it live,\n  and if it needs names, Bastion expands the pattern from the engine's\n  function list.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1cfb9f70-b141-485b-a40f-15f97c16393c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgx8JGT1ydzHN1cYCByCb","type":"assistant","uuid":"4929d0ab-7cbe-4d86-99cf-66d9ceeff76f","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:58:29.411Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
