UX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '\\''{}'\\''; fi' pre-tool-use 3>&1 1>&2; else cmux_cli=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOK_CMUX_BIN:-${CMUX_BUNDLED_CLI_PATH:-}}\"; if [ -z \"$cmux_cli\" ] || [ ! -x \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then cmux_cli=\"$(command -v cmux 2>/dev/null || true)\"; fi; agent_pid=\"${CMUX_CLAUDE_PID:-${PPID:-}}\"; if [ -n \"$CMUX_SURFACE_ID\" ] && [ \"$CMUX_CLAUDE_HOOKS_DISABLED\" != \"1\" ] && [ -n \"$cmux_cli\" ]; then if [ -n \"${CMUX_SOCKET_PATH:-}\" ]; then CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" --socket \"$CMUX_SOCKET_PATH\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; else CMUX_CLAUDE_PID=\"$agent_pid\" CMUXTERM_CLI_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_SEC=0.5 \"$cmux_cli\" hooks enqueue claude pre-tool-use 2>/dev/null || { cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; }; fi; else cat >/dev/null; echo '{}'; fi; fi","durationMs":61},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a5f5098b-f792-4629-9292-40f8d991b3a5","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:58:29.475Z","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"4929d0ab-7cbe-4d86-99cf-66d9ceeff76f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"63076884-86c8-4719-937e-cb437c55717e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017iL99vyFRDAwnyUkEHJxKN","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"0998bc33-0700-43af-9f05-aa79f867286f","timestamp":"2026-11-12T00:58:29.570Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","content":"# Bastion plan: more a step may do, more that checks it\n\n<!-- voice-register: informational -->\n<!-- voice-english: ste -->\n\nA step's capabilities grow past iii functions. It may run named shell\ncommands, call more tools, and reach MCP servers. Its constraints grow past\nrules: hooks run before its calls, and a reviewer agent must pass its change\nbefore the job moves on. The cost is reach. Each new capability is a new\nway for an agent to act, so each one starts ungranted and the gate decides\nevery call, the same as today.\n\nThe top-bar plan (U1 to U13) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions\nare in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D49 to D52.\n\n## Phases\n\nEach phase passes CI, is checked live in the app, and is committed before\nthe next.\n\n### C1. Named commands and more tools (D49)\n\n- A grant on `sandbox::exec` may name a command: `cargo`, or `npm test`.\n  That grant covers a call only when the command line starts with those\n  words.\n- A grant that names a command never covers a line with shell operators\n  (`;`, `&&`, `|`, `` ` ``, `$(`, `>`), because the operators would run a\n  second command. A grant that names no command still covers every line.\n- The most specific grant decides, as today: a named command wins over\n  plain `sandbox::exec`.\n- A turn's `functions.allow` is the four sandbox tools plus every function\n  its step's grants name. Today it is the four tools only, so a grant on\n  any other function can never be called.\n- The step editor's grant form takes the command words.\n- Migration 9 adds `capabilities.command` and puts it in the key.\n\n### C2. Hooks per step (D50)\n\n- A constraint may be a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before\n  each matching call at its steps. Exit 2 refuses the call, and its output\n  is the reason.\n- The charter's `PreToolUse` hooks still run. A step's hooks run after\n  them.\n- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook.\n\n### C3. A reviewer that must pass (D51)\n\n- A constraint may name a reviewer: an agent in `.agents/agents/`. When\n  its step finishes, Bastion runs one turn as that agent on the step's\n  change.\n- The reviewer answers pass or fail with its reasons. A fail fails the\n  step, so the job goes along the failure link or back to the fixer, as\n  D47 says. The step's revisions bound the loop.\n- The reviewer's turn reads only. Its verdict is an artifact on the step,\n  and the job page shows it.\n\n### C4. MCP servers (D52)\n\n- iii ships no MCP bridge; its docs say to write a worker that bridges MCP\n  into `trigger()` calls. `workers/bastion-mcp` is that worker, in Rust\n  (D6).\n- A server lists its MCP servers in Settings: a name, a URL, and the name\n  of the secret that holds its token, if it needs one.\n- The bridge registers each tool of a server as `mcp::<server>::<tool>`.\n  A step's grant on `mcp::github::*` lets its agent call that server's\n  tools, and C1 puts them in the turn's `functions.allow`.\n- Only MCP servers that answer over HTTP, this round. A stdio server runs\n  as a process on the host, outside the VM, and VISION.md says agent work\n  never runs on your machine.\n\n## Open questions\n\n- **Plugins.** iii has no plugin. Is a plugin a bundle of the above (an\n  agent, its skills, its hooks and its MCP servers) that a step takes as\n  one?\n- **Stdio MCP servers.** Should one run in the job's VM, so a step may use\n  a local MCP server without breaking the VM rule?\n- **Patterns in `functions.allow`.** I don't know yet whether the harness\n  takes `mcp::github::*` or needs each function by name. C1 checks it live,\n  and if it needs names, Bastion expands the pattern from the engine's\n  function list.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":230,"newStart":1,"newLines":81,"lines":["-# Bastion plan: one bar, every server","+# Bastion plan: more a step may do, more that checks it"," "," <!-- voice-register: informational -->"," <!-- voice-english: ste -->"," ","-The sidebar goes. A bar across the top holds the castle, the pages, and the","-server switcher. The switcher picks one server, or all of them on the pages","-that show records: Jobs, Audit Log and Costs. Those pages then add up what","-every server holds. The pages get one clean layout, and the records get","-graphs. The cost is width: ten pages and a switcher must fit in one row, so","-the page names get short and the bar wraps on a narrow window.","+A step's capabilities grow past iii functions. It may run named shell","+commands, call more tools, and reach MCP servers. Its constraints grow past","+rules: hooks run before its calls, and a reviewer agent must pass its change","+before the job moves on. The cost is reach. Each new capability is a new","+way for an agent to act, so each one starts ungranted and the gate decides","+every call, the same as today."," ","-The steps-only plan (S1 to S4) is done; git history holds it. Decisions are","-in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), and VISION.md says which pages are records","-and which are rules.","+The top-bar plan (U1 to U13) is done, and git history holds it. Decisions","+are in [DECISIONS.md](DECISIONS.md), D49 to D52."," "," ## Phases"," "," Each phase passes CI, is checked live in the app, and is committed before"," the next."," ","-### U1. The top bar","+### C1. Named commands and more tools (D49)"," ","-- Remove the sidebar. The bar shows the castle, the page names, the count","-  of jobs that wait, and the switcher.","-- The switcher lists each server with a dot for its stream, and \"All","-  servers\" on a records page.","-- If \"All servers\" is picked and you open a rules page, the page shows the","-  last server you picked alone.","-- The Jobs page follows the switcher, and its own server filter goes.","-- Exit, live: switch between `local` and all servers on Jobs, and open a","-  rules page from \"All servers\".","+- A grant on `sandbox::exec` may name a command: `cargo`, or `npm test`.","+  That grant covers a call only when the command line starts with those","+  words.","+- A grant that names a command never covers a line with shell operators","+  (`;`, `&&`, `|`, `` ` ``, `$(`, `>`), because the operators would run a","+  second command. A grant that names no command still covers every line.","+- The most specific grant decides, as today: a named command wins over","+  plain `sandbox::exec`.","+- A turn's `functions.allow` is the four sandbox tools plus every function","+  its step's grants name. Today it is the four tools only, so a grant on","+  any other function can never be called.","+- The step editor's grant form takes the command words.","+- Migration 9 adds `capabilities.command` and puts it in the key."," ","-Done 2026-11-11. The bar holds the castle, the ten pages with the count of","-jobs that wait, and the switcher as one button per server. Live: Jobs","-switched from all servers to `local` and back, and Workflows opened from","-\"All servers\" showed `local` alone.","+### C2. Hooks per step (D50)"," ","-### U2. Records across servers","-","-- Audit Log and Costs read every server when \"All servers\" is picked.","-- Each entry, turn and tally names its server. Costs add up by workspace,","-  step and day across servers.","-- A server that does not answer is named, and the rest still show.","-- Exit, live: Costs and Audit Log show `local` and a second server","-  together.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. The Audit Log is its own page now; Constraints still reads","-one server's audit for each constraint's history. Live: with `two` added,","-Costs showed both servers' totals, a workspace named with its server, and","-the days added up; the Audit Log showed both chains verified and their","-entries in one list. An export writes on one server, so it waits for one.","-The run found that opening a records page read only one server, because","-the page read under the route it left; that is fixed.","-","-### U3. Graphs","-","-- Costs: spend by day as bars, each bar split by server.","-- Jobs: how many jobs are in each state, and jobs started by day.","-- Audit Log: entries by day, split by kind, with the gate's denials marked.","-- Graphs are drawn on iced's canvas, with no new dependency.","-- Exit, live: each graph matches the numbers in its page's table.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. One stacked bar chart over the last 30 days, with a","-legend and a hover line that names the day and each part, serves all three","-pages; Jobs and the Audit Log also get number tiles. Live: on Costs, the","-tallest day reads $0.1937 as its table does, and hovering 11-06 reads","-$0.0658, local $0.0628 and two $0.0029. The Audit Log's tiles read 206","-entries, 1 denial and 21 decisions, as its tallies do. Its chart covers","-only the entries the page read, the newest 200 per server, and says so.","-","-### U4. Clean pages","-","-- One header on every page: the title, one line that says what the page","-  is, and the page's actions on the right.","-- Cards with the same padding and spacing everywhere; tables with aligned","-  columns.","-- Page by page, starting with Jobs and the job page.","-- Exit, live: every page is checked at the window's smallest size and at","-  full screen.","-","-Done 2026-11-11, in a first pass. Every page has one head: its title, a","-line that says what it shows and on which server, and its actions. A","-problem line shows only when there is one, so an empty one leaves no gap.","-Verification gets tiles for jobs landed, escapes and the rate; a job's","-title is its request's first line, with the request in full under it. The","-ledes that still named stages, pipelines or review are rewritten. Live:","-every page checked at full size, and Jobs at 720 by 480, where the bar","-wraps to two rows and nothing is cut.","-","-### U5. Evals and Verification across servers","-","-- Evals and Verification are records pages too, and stay in the bar.","-- Each eval and each landed job names its server and opens on it.","-- A new eval runs on the last server picked, and the form names it.","-- An escape goes to the server that landed its commit, so it can be","-  reported from \"All servers\".","-- Exit, live: both pages show `local` and `two` together.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Live, under \"All servers\": Evals listed each eval with its","-server and opened one on `local`, and Verification named each workspace","-with its server and added up 17 landed and 2 escapes. `two` has no eval","-and no landed job yet, so its rows could not show; the merge is covered by","-tests. A turn's steps on Costs now open on the turn's own server too.","-","-### U6. Eval charts: A against B","-","-- An eval's page compares A and B in total, measure by measure: grade,","-  cost, seconds, turns, calls, refused, held and flagged. Each pair is","-  scaled to its larger value and says how B differs from A.","-- Grade, cost, time, turns and calls are colored better or worse.","-  Refusals, holds and flags are not, as an enforced rung is meant to raise","+- A constraint may be a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before","+  each matching call at its steps. Exit 2 refuses the call, and its output","+  is the reason.","+- The charter's `PreToolUse` hooks still run. A step's hooks run after","   them.","-- A second chart compares each request's grade under A and B.","+- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook."," ","-Done 2026-11-11. Live on \"no-wc told vs enforced\": B cost 40% less, took","-25% less time, 28% fewer turns and 48% fewer calls, refused 5 calls to A's","-0, and graded the same, 7. The run found that a change from zero read","-\"same\" and that a zero drew a sliver of bar; both are fixed.","+### C3. A reviewer that must pass (D51)"," ","-### U7. A model and a budget per step (D43)","+- A constraint may name a reviewer: an agent in `.agents/agents/`. When","+  its step finishes, Bastion runs one turn as that agent on the step's","+  change.","+- The reviewer answers pass or fail with its reasons. A fail fails the","+  step, so the job goes along the failure link or back to the fixer, as","+  D47 says. The step's revisions bound the loop.","+- The reviewer's turn reads only. Its verdict is an artifact on the step,","+  and the job page shows it."," ","-- A step's options: its model, the most revisions its failure sends back,","-  and the most its turns may spend.","-- The step's model wins over the job's and the server's.","-- Past its spend, the factory starts no more turns at the step by itself;","-  a person's retry, note or answer still runs.","-- The workflow editor shows the three options on a step.","+### C4. MCP servers (D52)"," ","-Done 2026-11-11. Live: a copy of Short kept its options through a save","-(plan with a model and $0.50, checks with one revision). With the plan","-step set to `anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` and the server's default","-on DeepSeek, the plan turn ran on Anthropic, as its session records; a","-first run with DeepSeek on the step landed `quadruple(x)` on `demo-local`.","-The spending limit and the revision count are covered by tests, not run","-live. The user-facing word \"stack\" is now \"engine\" everywhere.","+- iii ships no MCP bridge; its docs say to write a worker that bridges MCP","+  into `trigger()` calls. `workers/bastion-mcp` is that worker, in Rust","+  (D6).","+- A server lists its MCP servers in Settings: a name, a URL, and the name","+  of the secret that holds its token, if it needs one.","+- The bridge registers each tool of a server as `mcp::<server>::<tool>`.","+  A step's grant on `mcp::github::*` lets its agent call that server's","+  tools, and C1 puts them in the turn's `functions.allow`.","+- Only MCP servers that answer over HTTP, this round. A stdio server runs","+  as a process on the host, outside the VM, and VISION.md says agent work","+  never runs on your machine."," ","-### U8. Rules per workflow step (D44)","-","-- A step is known as `workflow/step`, and each turn tells the gate which.","-- A grant may be for one workflow step; it wins over its kind's grant.","-- A constraint may apply at some steps only; with none, at every step.","-  An agent is told only the rules that apply at its step.","-- Capabilities lists the steps' own grants with a form to add one, and","-  each constraint shows its steps with a picker to add one.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Migration 6 rebuilt the grants table with the step in","-its key. Live: with `sandbox::fs::write` denied at the test workflow's","-build step, the gate refused the build's two writes there; the agent then","-wrote through `sandbox::exec`, which its kind still allows, and the job","-landed. So a step's grant binds only the function it names: to stop all","-writes at a step, deny `sandbox::exec` there too. A refusal now names the","-step. The grant showed under \"For one workflow step\" and its Remove took","-it back.","-","-### U9. No command steps (D45)","-","-- A step is a prompt, an agent, a skill or a shell script.","-- Migration 7 turns each command step into a prompt that reads its","-  command's file, and the grants for commands go.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Each rebuild reads the old stage `command` as its own","-time meant it: a shell step before migration 4, a repository's command","-after. Live: a workflow saved with a command step before the restart came","-back after migration 7 as a prompt that reads","-`.claude/commands/release-notes.md`, its own words after; no command row","-was left.","-","-### U10. The charter is AGENTS.md and .agents/ (D46)","-","-- The charter is `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/settings.json`; `CLAUDE.md` and","-  `.claude/` are no longer read, and a turn may not write `AGENTS.md` or","-  anything under `.agents/`.","-- An agent step reads `.agents/agents/<name>.md`, a skill step","-  `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`.","-- The harness, the rules on an agent's calls, stays Bastion's own.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Live: with `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/settings.json`","-committed to `demo-local`, the server read both as its charter and its","-rule that denies `git push`. A workspace with only `.claude/` files, such","-as `bastion-gh`, shows no charter until it has `.agents/`.","-","-### U11. Workflows that branch (D47)","-","-- A link may be a failure link. When its step fails, the job goes along","-  it instead of back to the step that writes.","-- A failure link orders nothing, so it may go back; a step only failure","-  links reach is skipped otherwise.","-- The failing step's revisions bound a loop; past them a person decides.","-- The canvas draws a failure link red and dashed; a picked link has an","-  \"On failure\" box.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Live, on a copy of Short whose checks exit 1 and whose","-failure link goes to a lights-on `report` step: plan and build ran, the","-checks failed, the job went to `report` instead of back to build,","-`report` ran, and the job waited there; it was stopped so nothing","-landed. The canvas drew the link red and dashed.","-","-### U12. A step that failed shows failed","-","-- A job keeps which steps last failed; a step that passes later comes off.","-- A step behind the current one shows failed when it last failed, and","-  skipped when only a failure leads to it and none did. Past the finish,","-  a later step shows skipped, and the finish stands on the last step","-  that ran.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Live, the branching job again: plan done, build done,","-checks failed, report waiting.","-","-### U13. A step's rules on the workflows page (D48)","-","-- An agent's step shows its rules: the constraints that apply there, each","-  marked every step or scoped, with \"Not here\" and a picker to apply one","-  scoped to other steps here too; and its grants.","-- A step uses its kind's grants until \"Give this step its own grants\"","-  copies them as its own, which then take their place; \"Use its kind's","-  instead\" takes them back.","-- A grant is ask or allowed; demoting from ask removes it. Migration 8","-  drops denied grants and limits the rung to ask and allowed.","-","-Done 2026-11-11. Live, on Bug fix's build step: its own grants started as","-a copy of the prompt kind's `sandbox::*` allowed, demoted to ask, then","-Remove took it back to the kind's; the audit recorded the grant, the","-demotion and the removal. Taking a constraint off its only step is","-refused, as that would apply it at every step.","-"," ## Open questions"," ","-- **Where the switcher sits on a narrow window.** The bar wraps. Should the","-  switcher stay on the first row instead?","+- **Plugins.** iii has no plugin. Is a plugin a bundle of the above (an","+  agent, its skills, its hooks and its MCP servers) that a step takes as","+  one?","+- **Stdio MCP servers.** Should one run in the job's VM, so a step may use","+  a local MCP server without breaking the VM rule?","+- **Patterns in `functions.allow`.** I don't know yet whether the harness","+  takes `mcp::github::*` or needs each function by name. C1 checks it live,","+  and if it needs names, Bastion expands the pattern from the engine's","+  function list."]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4929d0ab-7cbe-4d86-99cf-66d9ceeff76f","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"type":"last-prompt","lastPrompt":"Good, now I want to add capabilities. The function scope is good. But I also want to add more capabilities: shell scripts, mcp servers, plugins, tools, and so forth. Constraints map to rules, hooks, a…","leafUuid":"0998bc33-0700-43af-9f05-aa79f867286f","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e"}
