{"parentUuid":"db73554b-85a4-41c2-bf12-012fead1d7a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx8KKAXDWSoXjYYhoQM6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NxjesGY4UDPyzGB3sRrimt","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","old_string":"so a step is narrowed by listing what it may call. This replaces D44's \"wins over its kind's\". |\n","new_string":"so a step is narrowed by listing what it may call. This replaces D44's \"wins over its kind's\". |\n| D49 | A grant on `sandbox::exec` may name a command, and then it covers only a line that starts with those words and has no shell operators. A turn may call the four sandbox tools and every function its step's grants name. |\n| D50 | A constraint may be a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before each matching call at its steps, after the charter's hooks. Exit 2 refuses the call. |\n| D51 | A constraint may name a reviewer from `.agents/agents/`. When its step finishes, the reviewer reads the step's change in a turn that only reads, and its fail fails the step as D47 says. |\n| D52 | A server's MCP servers reach a turn through `workers/bastion-mcp`, which registers each tool as `mcp::<server>::<tool>`. Only MCP servers over HTTP: a stdio server would run on the host, outside the VM. |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1483,"cache_read_input_tokens":113735,"output_tokens":618,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1483,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":113735,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1483,"cache_creation":{"e