{"parentUuid":"44bfc70e-60cc-4121-b41a-c2a682c4ae5c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgx97M4QEvKdwL3xPTKGL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013bJTReUgqnAjBxpGwCZ1Ct","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''  the API don't change.\n'''\nnew='''  the API don't change.\n\nDone 2026-11-11. Live, on Short's plan step with its own grants\n`sandbox::fs::*` and `sandbox::exec git`: `git -C /work/repo log\n--oneline -3` ran, and `ls -la /work/repo` was refused with \"No grant\ncovers sandbox::exec at short/plan.\" The four sandbox tools are in every\nturn's list by name, so this did not show whether the harness takes a\npattern such as `sandbox::*`. C4 checks that with the MCP tools.\n'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add DECISIONS.md PLAN.md crates/bastion-core/src/govern.rs crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules.rs crates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs crates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs && git commit -q -m \"C1: a grant may name a command, and a turn may call what its step grants (D49)\n\nA grant on sandbox::exec may name the command after the function, as\n\\`sandbox::exec cargo test\\`. It covers only a line that starts with those\nwords and has no shell operators. A turn's functions.allow is the four\nsandbox tools plus every function its step's grants name.\n\nPLAN.md: the capabilities and constraints plan, C1 to C4.\nDECISIONS.md: D49 to D52.\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Record C1 in the plan and commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":403,"cache_read_input_tokens":158484,"output_tokens":625,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation