{"parentUuid":"8d59fe1e-9ec0-434e-8d26-4b71aaad9d59","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxAAkXzMdgeKr9BCT4BL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NtqEz3vn63f47Z9tieYqzX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e/scratchpad; $S/api.sh POST /jobs/jaf86d11f/stop | tail -1; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook.\n'''\nnew='''- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook. A\n  hook that is only told doesn't run, and only an owner's constraint can\n  be removed: a charter's changes in its repository.\n\nDone 2026-11-11. Live, a hook at Short's plan step that exits 2: the turn's\n`git log` was refused with \"A hook refused this call: hook says no\", and\nthe audit kept the hook's run. In the app, Bug fix's build step added\n`./.agents/hooks/check.sh` as a hook and removed it again; the audit\nrecorded both.\n'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,'w').write(s)\np='DECISIONS.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''after the charter's hooks. Exit 2 refuses the call. |'''\nnew='''after the charter's hooks, unless it is only told. Exit 2 refuses the call. An owner's constraint can be removed; a charter's changes in its repository. |'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add PLAN.md DECISIONS.md crates/bastion-core/src/govern.rs crates/bastion-core/src/charter.rs crates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs crates/bastion-protocol/src/lib.rs crates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs crates/bastion-server/src/govern_store.rs crates/bastion-server/src/store/schema.rs crates/bastion-server/src/api/govern.rs crates/bastion-server/src/http.rs crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules.rs crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/govern.rs && git status --short && git commit -q -m \"C2: hooks per step (D50)\n\nA constraint may carry a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM\nbefore each call it binds at its steps, after the charter's hooks.\nExit 2 refuses the call; a hook that is only told does not run.\n\nThe step editor adds a hook and removes one made for that step. An\nowner's constraint can now be removed (POST /constraints/{id}/remove);\na charter's is refused, since it changes in its repository.\" && git log --oneline -1","description":"Stop the test job, record C2, and commit","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":891,"cache_read_input_tokens":244272,"output_tokens":1198,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":129},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":891,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1198,"cache_read_input_tokens":244272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":891},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NtqEz3vn63f47Z9tieYqzX":{"command":"cd /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion && S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e/scratchpad; $S/api.sh POST /jobs/jaf86d11f/stop | tail -1; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook.\n'''\nnew='''- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook. A\n  hook that is only told doesn't run, and only an owner's constraint can\n  be removed: a charter's changes in its repository.\n\nDone 2026-11-11. Live, a hook at Short's plan step that exits 2: the turn's\n`git log`