{"parentUuid":"fee595f1-cdc9-4bca-a8e4-f0c13f6428c1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"63076884-86c8-4719-937e-cb437c55717e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NtqEz3vn63f47Z9tieYqzX","type":"tool_result","content":"HTTP 200\nM  DECISIONS.md\nM  PLAN.md\nM  crates/bastion-core/src/charter.rs\nM  crates/bastion-core/src/govern.rs\nM  crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/govern.rs\nM  crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules.rs\nM  crates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs\nM  crates/bastion-protocol/src/lib.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/api/govern.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/govern_store.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/http.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/store/schema.rs\n54a5228 C2: hooks per step (D50)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"743bcd1d-2fc8-48f5-a980-6ca9847faae7","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:23:10.794Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"HTTP 200\nM  DECISIONS.md\nM  PLAN.md\nM  crates/bastion-core/src/charter.rs\nM  crates/bastion-core/src/govern.rs\nM  crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/govern.rs\nM  crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules.rs\nM  crates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs\nM  crates/bastion-protocol/src/lib.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/api/govern.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/govern_store.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/http.rs\nM  crates/bastion-server/src/store/schema.rs\n54a5228 C2: hooks per step (D50)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":76,"oldLines":7,"newStart":76,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D47 | A link may be a failure link: when its step fails, the job goes along it instead of back to the step that writes. A failure link orders nothing, so it may go back to an earlier step; a step reached only by failure links is skipped otherwise. The failing step's revisions bound any loop, and past them a person decides. A step has at most one failure link. |"," | D48 | A grant is ask or allowed; a call no grant covers is refused, so there is no denied grant. Demoting a grant from ask removes it. A step's own grants, when it has any, take the place of its kind's, so a step is narrowed by listing what it may call. This replaces D44's \"wins over its kind's\". |"," | D49 | A grant on `sandbox::exec` may name a command, and then it covers only a line that starts with those words and has no shell operators. A turn may call the four sandbox tools and every function its step's grants name. |","-| D50 | A constraint may be a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before each matching call at its steps, after the charter's hooks. Exit 2 refuses the call. |","+| D50 | A constraint may be a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before each matching call at its steps, after the charter's hooks, unless it is only told. Exit 2 refuses the call. An owner's constraint can be removed; a charter's changes in its repository. |"," | D51 | A constraint may name a reviewer from `.agents/agents/`. When its step finishes, the reviewer reads the step's change in a turn that only reads, and its fail fails the step as D47 says. |"," | D52 | A server's MCP servers reach a turn through `workers/bastion-mcp`, which registers each tool as `mcp::<server>::<tool>`. Only MCP servers over HTTP: a stdio server would run on the host, outside the VM. |"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":49,"oldLines":7,"newStart":49,"newLines":15,"lines":["   is the reason."," - The charter's `PreToolUse` hooks still run. A step's hooks run after","   them.","-- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook.","+- The Constraints section of the step editor adds and removes a hook. A","+  hook that is only told doesn't run, and only an owner's constraint can","+  be removed: a charter's changes in its repository.","+","+Done 2026-11-11. Live, a hook at Short's plan step that exits 2: the turn's","+`git log` was refused with \"A hook refused this call: hook says no\", and","+the audit kept the hook's run. In the app, Bug fix's build step added","+`./.agents/hooks/check.sh` as a hook and removed it again; the audit","+recorded both."," "," ### C3. A reviewer that must pass (D51)"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"93c5bb5f-33f4-4307-9d80-b5c7bef97045","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":11,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fee595f1-cdc9-4bca-a8e4-f0c13f6428c1","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
