{"parentUuid":"38f231d2-87ed-427b-b17d-2010e69e5a5e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxACWDKZFzVU1PjUTKuc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HkTx2je5FHi7J9y1yCaCZM","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Map step-end and review flow","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"In the Rust repo /Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion, map how a workflow step ends and how its change is reviewed, so I can add a \"reviewer agent\" constraint (D51): after a step's turn finishes, Bastion runs one read-only turn as a named agent from `.agents/agents/<name>.md` on the step's change; a fail verdict fails the step via the existing `step_failed` path (failure links, D47), bounded by revisions.\n\nReport concisely, with file:line for each item:\n1. In crates/bastion-core/src/lib.rs: the Event(s) the factory sends when a turn ends (success/failure), and how `outcome`/`step`/`advance`/`step_failed` decide what happens next. Which Effect(s) start a turn (`Effect::StartTurn {stage, brief}`), capture a diff (`Effect::CaptureDiff`), or run a review. What `bastion_core::review` does and where its findings feed in (is there an existing post-step review of the diff, e.g. constraints \"checked at review\"?).\n2. In crates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs (and factory/*.rs): what happens when a turn ends (where the turn's result is read, e.g. listen_for_turn / turn ended handler), where CaptureDiff and the review findings are handled, and how `gate.reviewed(...)` is used.\n3. How an agent step reads `.agents/agents/<name>.md` into its brief (crates/bastion-core/src/brief.rs and the server side).\n4. How a turn's text answer is read back (e.g. a plan artifact body) — function names.\n5. Any existing \"judge\" or verdict mechanism (e.g. the judge worker, evals) that parses pass/fail from a model turn.\nDo not propose a design; only map the code. Keep it under 600 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reaso