the review findings are handled, and how `gate.reviewed(...)` is used.\n3. How an agent step reads `.agents/agents/<name>.md` into its brief (crates/bastion-core/src/brief.rs and the server side).\n4. How a turn's text answer is read back (e.g. a plan artifact body) — function names.\n5. Any existing \"judge\" or verdict mechanism (e.g. the judge worker, evals) that parses pass/fail from a model turn.\nDo not propose a design; only map the code. Keep it under 600 words."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"caf128ba-48c7-482b-9be4-73c90aa34a7e","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgxACVkHjeNXXjNrvjgf7","type":"assistant","uuid":"51446658-05eb-4135-9064-d62ae4034014","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:23:24.087Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
