sh stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\n  </when_not_to_use>\n\n  <file_writing_policy>\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\n  </file_writing_policy>\n\n  <output_constraints>\n    <artifact_policy>\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\n    </artifact_policy>\n  </output_constraints>\n  <session_continuity>\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\n  </session_continuity>\n\n</context_window_protection>","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-tacoda-tacoda-bastion/4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e/tasks/aeceea994e737ef81.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"caf128ba-48c7-482b-9be4-73c90aa34a7e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"51446658-05eb-4135-9064-d62ae4034014","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"45edd9f6-cfe4-45d1-889a-47f81ad01ec1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxADVgbswL7bRxznRgUt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"C1 and C2 are done and committed. C3 is starting. A search agent is mapping how a step ends and how its change gets reviewed today. I'll design the reviewer when its report comes back.\n\nSo far:\n- **C1 (`6f56e5f`).** A grant on `sandbox::exec` can name a command, such as `sandbox::exec cargo test`. It covers only a line that starts with those words and has no shell operators. A turn may now call every function its step's grants name, not only the four sandbox tools. In a live job, `git log` ran under a `sandbox::exec git` grant, and `ls -la` was refused.\n- **C2 (`54a5228`).** A constraint can carry a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before matching calls at its steps, and exit 2 refuses the call. The step editor adds and removes hooks. The API can now remove an owner's constraint, but not a charter's. In a live job, the test hook refused `git log`. In the app, I added a hook to Bug fix's build step and removed it again.\n- **Plan.** `PLAN.md` holds C1 to C4, and `DECISIONS.md` holds D49 to D52.\n\nThings you should know:\n- **The MCP bridge (C4) is bigger than planned.** iii doesn't ship one. Its docs say to write a worker that bridges MCP into `trigger()` calls. So C4 means a new worker, `workers/bastion-mcp`, and the plan supports MCP servers over HTTP only. A stdio server would run on your machine, outside the VM.\n- **An open question remains.** I still don't know whether the harness accepts a pattern such as `mcp::github::*` in `functions.allow`. The C1 job can't show it, because the four sandbox tools are in the list by name. C4 will settle it.\n- **Clean-up.** I stopped the test jobs and removed the test grants and hooks.\n- **Not pushed.** `3b3370e`, `6f56e5f` and `54a5228` are local only."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1506,"cache_read_input_tokens":246757,"output_tokens":654,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1506,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":654,"cache_read_input_tokens":246757,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1506},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"32097b0c-6c1d-4cbe-9c78-f82c2c76355e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgxADVJHanyGjaEzqVgnS","type":"assistant","uuid":"881298c1-2763-46e1-a699-c24c9f2d4638","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:23:31.027Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
