{"parentUuid":"121176e9-0b6e-48f6-8639-9a77c2a409fc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6cbe2f9d-8896-4784-9bb3-3b66f1bc9361","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016hGXmx1hu5hH98ZRr9BdFh","type":"tool_result","content":" M DECISIONS.md\n M PLAN.md\n M crates/bastion-core/src/charter.rs\n M crates/bastion-core/src/govern.rs\n M crates/bastion-core/src/lib.rs\n M crates/bastion-core/src/review.rs\n M crates/bastion-core/src/tests.rs\n M crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/govern.rs\n M crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules.rs\n M crates/bastion-protocol/src/lib.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/api/govern.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/evals.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/govern_store.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/store/schema.rs\n?? crates/bastion-server/src/factory/reviewer.rs","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3c60efa4-018b-4412-a2c1-4483f000894b","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:32:18.566Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":" M DECISIONS.md\n M PLAN.md\n M crates/bastion-core/src/charter.rs\n M crates/bastion-core/src/govern.rs\n M crates/bastion-core/src/lib.rs\n M crates/bastion-core/src/review.rs\n M crates/bastion-core/src/tests.rs\n M crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/govern.rs\n M crates/bastion-desktop/src/pages/step_rules.rs\n M crates/bastion-protocol/src/lib.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/api/govern.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/evals.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/factory.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/gate.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/govern_store.rs\n M crates/bastion-server/src/store/schema.rs\n?? crates/bastion-server/src/factory/reviewer.rs","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":77,"oldLines":7,"newStart":77,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D48 | A grant is ask or allowed; a call no grant covers is refused, so there is no denied grant. Demoting a grant from ask removes it. A step's own grants, when it has any, take the place of its kind's, so a step is narrowed by listing what it may call. This replaces D44's \"wins over its kind's\". |"," | D49 | A grant on `sandbox::exec` may name a command, and then it covers only a line that starts with those words and has no shell operators. A turn may call the four sandbox tools and every function its step's grants name. |"," | D50 | A constraint may be a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before each matching call at its steps, after the charter's hooks, unless it is only told. Exit 2 refuses the call. An owner's constraint can be removed; a charter's changes in its repository. |","-| D51 | A constraint may name a reviewer from `.agents/agents/`. When its step finishes, the reviewer reads the step's change in a turn that only reads, and its fail fails the step as D47 says. |","+| D51 | A constraint may name a reviewer from `.agents/agents/`. When its step finishes, the reviewer reads the step's change in a turn with no tools, from its file at the job's base, and its fail fails the step as D47 says. A reviewer that can't run leaves the job with a person. |"," | D52 | A server's MCP servers reach a turn through `workers/bastion-mcp`, which registers each tool as `mcp::<server>::<tool>`. Only MCP servers over HTTP: a stdio server would run on the host, outside the VM. |"," "," ## Open questions"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":67,"oldLines":8,"newStart":67,"newLines":19,"lines":[" - The reviewer answers pass or fail with its reasons. A fail fails the","   step, so the job goes along the failure link or back to the fixer, as","   D47 says. The step's revisions bound the loop.","-- The reviewer's turn reads only. Its verdict is an artifact on the step,","-  and the job page shows it.","+- The reviewer's turn has no tools: it reads its agent file as the job's","+  base has it, the request, and the change, on the server's plan model. A","+  turn under review can't rewrite its reviewer.","+- Its reply is an artifact on the step, and its cost counts toward the","+  step's budget. A reviewer that can't run, or gives no verdict, leaves","+  the job with a person.","+- The step editor adds a reviewer and removes one made for that step.","+","+Done 2026-11-11. Live, a `strict` agent that fails every change, on Short's","+plan step: the job waited with \"The reviewer strict failed it\", and the","+review was kept as \"Review by strict\". A plan step only reads, so a fail","+there has no step to go back to and waits for a person. In the app, Bug","+fix's build step added `strict` as a reviewer and removed it."," "," ### C4. MCP servers (D52)"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"58a645f3-5618-4b7d-832e-268d9821a952","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":14,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"121176e9-0b6e-48f6-8639-9a77c2a409fc","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
