t.rs:299:        ctx.iii.register_function(function(\"stream\"), on_stream),\nworkers/bastion-openai-compat/src/host.rs:301:            .register_function(function(\"abort\"), on_abort.metadata(internal.clone())),\nworkers/bastion-openai-compat/src/host.rs:303:            .register_function(function(\"refresh_models\"), on_refresh),\nworkers/bastion-openai-compat/src/host.rs:305:            .register_function(function(\"on_router_ready\"), on_ready.metadata(internal)),\nworkers/bastion-openai-compat/src/host.rs:308:    let ready = ctx.iii.register_trigger(bind).ok();\nworkers/bastion-openai-compat/src/main.rs:14:use iii_sdk::iii::WorkerMetadata;\nworkers/bastion-openai-compat/src/main.rs:15:use iii_sdk::{Error, InitOptions, RegisterFunction, register_worker};\nworkers/bastion-openai-compat/src/main.rs:57:/// Make the registered hosts match `hosts`: drop every host, retire the\nworkers/bastion-openai-compat/src/main.rs:58:/// ones no longer listed, register each.\n  provider-openrouter:\n    worker: package://provider-openrouter\n    version: \"0.1.16\"\n  # This signs in with a ChatGPT subscription, not a key.\n  provider-openai-codex:\n    worker: package://provider-openai-codex\n    version: \"0.4.30\"\n  # Bastion's own: one provider per OpenAI-compatible host listed in\n  # Settings. `cargo run` builds it when the source changed.\n  bastion-openai-compat:\n    worker: path://./workers/bastion-openai-compat\n    working_dir: .\n    start_after: [state, llm-router]\n    scripts:\n      run: cargo run -q -p bastion-openai-compat\n  # What `harness` calls: sessions, context, the function directory, `fp`,\n  # `judge` and `approval-gate` (found in its binary, 2026-11-09).\n  session-manager:\n    worker: package://session-manager\n    version: \"1.0.35\"\n  context-manager:\n    worker: package://context-manager\n    version: \"1.1.25\"\n  iii-directory:\n    worker: package://iii-directory\n    version: \"1.2.44\"\n3:members = [\n4-    \"crates/bastion-core\",\n5-  