{"parentUuid":"e7884015-82ec-4c81-90a4-45e61c1a524c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxBfJk8Rx34YSenXG8sb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1019,"cache_read_input_tokens":383122,"output_tokens":1135,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":98},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1019,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1135,"cache_read_input_tokens":383122,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1019},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c1b6a033-9a50-4063-a4cc-f47184abde83","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgxBfJHqkvPq1FwVMopqF","type":"assistant","uuid":"cf90baf1-c9a5-4e81-b405-f46acaf7066a","timestamp":"2026-11-12T01:42:30.320Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"cf90baf1-c9a5-4e81-b405-f46acaf7066a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxBfJk8Rx34YSenXG8sb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The capabilities and constraints plan is done. All four phases (C1 to C4) passed CI and the Code Health safeguard, were checked live in the app, and are committed. Nothing is pushed.\n\n| Commit | Phase | What it adds |\n|---|---|---|\n| `6f56e5f` | C1 (D49) | A grant on `sandbox::exec` can name a command, such as `sandbox::exec cargo test`. It covers only a line that starts with those words and has no shell operators. A turn may call every function its step's grants name. |\n| `54a5228` | C2 (D50) | A constraint can carry a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before matching calls at its steps. Exit 2 refuses the call. You can now remove a constraint you added; a charter's constraint is refused. |\n| `840526d` | C3 (D51) | A constraint can name a reviewer agent from `.agents/agents/`. When the step finishes, the reviewer reads its change in a turn with no tools. A fail sends the work back as a failure does (D47). A reviewer that can't run leaves the job with a person. |\n| `adf8825` | C4 (D52) | `workers/bastion-mcp`, Bastion's own MCP bridge. Each tool of an MCP server listed in Settings becomes the function `mcp::<server>::<tool>`, and a step's grant on `mcp::<server>::*` lets its agent call it. |\n\n**A security hole, fixed in the same series.** C1 let a turn call any function its step grants. But the gate's hook bound only `sandbox::*`, so in C4's first live run the MCP call skipped the gate completely: no judgment and no audit entry. The hook now binds every function a turn calls. In the rerun, the audit shows \"continue mcp::calc::add\". The hole existed only between C1 and C4, which are local commits.\n\n**What the live checks showed:**\n- **C1:** `git log` ran under a `sandbox::exec git` grant, and `ls -la` was refused.\n- **C2:** a hook refused `git log` with its own output as the reason.\n- **C3:** a reviewer that fails everything stopped a plan step, and its reply was kept as \"Review by strict\".\n- **C4:** with a small test MCP server, a job called `mcp::calc::add` and got 5.\n- **The open question:** the harness accepts a pattern such as `mcp::calc::*` in `functions.allow`, so the plan no longer lists it.\n\n**Limits:**\n- I didn't test an MCP server that needs a token. The tests cover making the bridge a consumer of the secret, but no live job has used a token.\n- MCP servers work over HTTP only. A stdio server would run on your machine, outside the VM, so it is still an open question in `PLAN.md`.\n- Plugins are still left out.\n- A reviewer reads only the change in its message and can't open other files.\n\n**Clean-up:** every test job is stopped, and every test grant, hook, reviewer and MCP server is removed. The test agent `strict.md` is still committed in the scratch `demo-local` repository.\n\n**To push:** five local commits, from `3b3370e` to `adf8825`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1019,"cache_read_input_tokens":383122,"output_tokens":1135,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":98},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1019,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1135,"cache_read_input_tokens":383122,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1019},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c1b6a033-9a50-4063-a4cc-f47184abde83","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgxBfJHqkvPq1FwVMopqF","type":"assistant","uuid":"bcf26eac-534