{"parentUuid":"ecc1d3c9-19c2-4fca-8866-6aa5af04bea2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyBQkktMBbq86nfD4PNh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"An MCP server that needs a token works end to end, and the token never passed through me. No code changed, so there is nothing to commit.\n\n**How I kept the token from me:** the test server made a random token and wrote it to a file with mode 600. A shell command copied it into the vault as `MCP_TEST_TOKEN` without printing it. I saw only the vault's masked hint. One limit: `iii trigger` takes its payload only as an argument, so the token was in that command's argv for about a second.\n\n**What happened:**\n1. **Without the token:** Settings showed \"not connected: the server answered 401 Unauthorized\".\n2. **With `MCP_TEST_TOKEN` named:** the server answered \"connected, 1 tools\", and the vault listed `bastion-mcp` as the secret's only consumer.\n3. **In a job:** a test job called `mcp::locked::add` with 4 and 5. The gate judged the call (\"continue mcp::locked::add\"), and the server received it with the right token. The server's log holds only the one refusal from step 1.\n4. **Removing the server** took `bastion-mcp` off the secret's consumers, which went back to `[]`.\n\n**Clean-up:** I stopped the test job, removed the test grants and the server, deleted the secret, stopped the test server, and deleted the token file.\n\nOne grant on a single step is still there, and I didn't add it this session: `bug-fix/plan` has `sandbox::*` allowed. I left it alone. Remove it in the step editor if you don't want it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1105,"cache_read_input_tokens":394798,"output_tokens":590,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":98},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1105,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":590,"cache_read_input_tokens":394798,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1105,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1105},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c1d8a845-9cfd-4b53-88ba-a17213a6fb84","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgyBQkUmtqthJhRsXw6ru","type":"assistant","uuid":"50396485-c341-44f7-a803-da301b8c8555","timestamp":"2026-11-12T14:19:45.751Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
