{"parentUuid":"84ea7356-255a-42ca-98dc-479704a8027d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ec4cfade-0cac-443c-ac72-d13b4b549392","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AQNtCVxu8mEvmham3vT6KB","type":"tool_result","content":"//! The engine console: containers from compose, functions and\n//! trigger types from the engine, queues with their depth, and one container's\n//! logs. Each read goes through the Engine seam.\n\nuse bastion_protocol::{\n    Console, Container, LogCursor, LogLine, LogPage, LogRequest, Queue, Registered,\n};\nuse serde_json::{Value, json};\n\nuse crate::engine::NS;\nuse crate::engine::{DEFAULT_NAMESPACE, Engine};\n\n/// The namespace the compose daemon and the queue worker answer in.\n/// How long a log read waits for new lines. compose allows 5000.\nconst LOG_WAIT_MS: u64 = 5_000;\nconst LOG_TAIL: u64 = 200;\n\npub async fn read(engine: &dyn Engine) -> Result<Console, String> {\n    let status = engine.call(NS, \"compose::status\", json!({})).await?;\n    let functions = engine\n        .call(DEFAULT_NAMESPACE, \"engine::functions::list\", json!({}))\n        .await?;\n    let triggers = engine\n        .call(DEFAULT_NAMESPACE, \"engine::triggers::list\", json!({}))\n        .await?;\n    let topics = engine\n        .call(NS, \"engine::queue::list_topics\", json!({}))\n        .await?;\n    let mut queues = Vec::new();\n    for name in topics\n        .as_array()\n        .into_iter()\n        .flatten()\n        .filter_map(|t| t[\"name\"].as_str())\n    {\n        let stats = engine\n            .call(NS, \"engine::queue::topic_stats\", json!({ \"topic\": name }))\n            .await?;\n        queues.push(queue(name, &stats));\n    }\n    Ok(Console {\n        containers: containers(&status),\n        functions: registered(&functions[\"functions\"], \"function_id\"),\n        trigger_types: registered(&triggers[\"triggers\"], \"id\"),\n        queues,\n    })\n}\n\nfn text(value: &Value) -> String {\n    value.as_str().unwrap_or_default().to_string()\n}\n\nfn containers(status: &Value) -> Vec<Container> {\n    let rows = status[\"containers\"].as_array().cloned().unwrap_or_default();\n    rows.iter()\n        .map(|c| Container {\n            name: text(&c[\"container\"]),\n            version: c[\"version\"].as_str().map(String::from),\n            state: text(&c[\"state\"]),\n            owned: c[\"owned\"] == true,\n            last_error: c[\"last_error\"].as_str().map(String::from),\n        })\n        .collect()\n}\n\nfn registered(rows: &Value, id_field: &str) -> Vec<Registered> {\n    let mut out: Vec<Registered> = rows\n        .as_array()\n        .into_iter()\n        .flatten()\n        .map(|r| Registered {\n            id: text(&r[id_field]),\n            namespace: text(&r[\"namespace\"]),\n            worker: text(&r[\"worker_name\"]),\n            description: text(&r[\"description\"]),\n        })\n        .collect();\n    out.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));\n    out\n}\ncrates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs:114:bare!(Console, \"GET\", \"/console\", crate::Console);\ncrates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs:115:with!(ContainerLogs, \"POST\", \"/console/logs\", LogRequest, LogPage);\ncrates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs:116:at!(ContainerStop, \"POST\", \"/console/{name}/stop\", name, ());\ncrates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs:117:at!(ContainerStart, \"POST\", \"/console/{name}/start\", name, ());\ncrates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs:580:        Console,\ncrates/bastion-server/src/http.rs:65:        .route(\"/console\", get(console))\ncrates/bastion-server/src/http.rs:66:        .route(\"/console/logs\", post(container_logs))\ncrates/bastion-server/src/http.rs:67:        .route(\"/console/{name}/stop\", post(container_stop))\ncrates/bastion-server/src/http.rs:68:        .route(\"/console/{name}/start\", post(container_start))\ncrates/bastion-server/src/http.rs:356:async fn console(State(app): State<App>) -> Response {","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fc7faa65-579c-427a-a428-c73243a56fd6","timestamp":"2026-11-12T14:25:37.470Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"//! The engine console: containers from compose, functions and\n//! trigger types from the engine, queues with their depth, and one container's\n//! logs. Each read goes through the Engine seam.\n\nuse bastion_protocol::{\n    Console, Container, LogCursor, LogLine, LogPage, LogRequest, Queue, Registered,\n};\nuse serde_json::{Value, json};\n\nuse crate::engine::NS;\nuse crate::engine::{DEFAULT_NAMESPACE, Engine};\n\n/// The namespace the compose daemon and the queue worker answer in.\n/// How long a log read waits for new lines. compose allows 5000.\nconst LOG_WAIT_MS: u64 = 5_000;\nconst LOG_TAIL: u64 = 200;\n\npub async fn read(engine: &dyn Engine) -> Result<Console, String> {\n    let status = engine.call(NS, \"compose::status\", json!({})).await?;\n    let functions = engine\n        .call(DEFAULT_NAMESPACE, \"engine::functions::list\", json!({}))\n        .await?;\n    let triggers = engine\n        .call(DEFAULT_NAMESPACE, \"engine::triggers::list\", json!({}))\n        .await?;\n    let topics = engine\n        .call(NS, \"engine::queue::list_topics\", json!({}))\n        .await?;\n    let mut queues = Vec::new();\n    for name in topics\n        .as_array()\n        .into_iter()\n        .flatten()\n        .filter_map(|t| t[\"name\"].as_str())\n    {\n        let stats = engine\n            .call(NS, \"engine::queue::topic_stats\", json!({ \"topic\": name }))\n            .await?;\n        queues.push(queue(name, &stats));\n    }\n    Ok(Console {\n        containers: containers(&status),\n        functions: registered(&functions[\"functions\"], \"function_id\"),\n        trigger_types: registered(&triggers[\"triggers\"], \"id\"),\n        queues,\n    })\n}\n\nfn text(value: &Value) -> String {\n    value.as_str().unwrap_or_default().to_string()\n}\n\nfn containers(status: &Value) -> Vec<Container> {\n    let rows = status[\"containers\"].as_array().cloned().unwrap_or_default();\n    rows.iter()\n        .map(|c| Container {\n            name: text(&c[\"container\"]),\n            version: c[\"version\"].as_str().map(String::from),\n            state: text(&c[\"state\"]),\n            owned: c[\"owned\"] == true,\n            last_error: c[\"last_error\"].as_str().map(String::from),\n        })\n        .collect()\n}\n\nfn registered(rows: &Value, id_field: &str) -> Vec<Registered> {\n    let mut out: Vec<Registered> = rows\n        .as_array()\n        .into_iter()\n        .flatten()\n        .map(|r| Registered {\n            id: text(&r[id_field]),\n            namespace: text(&r[\"namespace\"]),\n            worker: text(&r[\"worker_name\"]),\n            description: text(&r[\"description\"]),\n        })\n        .collect();\n    out.sort_by(|a, b| a.id.cmp(&b.id));\n    out\n}\ncrates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs:114:bare!(Console, \"GET\", \"/console\", crate::Console);\ncrates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs:115:with!(ContainerLogs, \"POST\", \"/console/logs\", LogRequest, LogPage);\ncrates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs:116:at!(ContainerStop, \"POST\", \"/console/{name}/stop\", name, ());\ncrates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs:117:at!(ContainerStart, \"POST\", \"/console/{name}/start\", name, ());\ncrates/bastion-protocol/src/api.rs:580:        Console,\ncrates/bastion-server/src/http.rs:65:        .route(\"/console\", get(console))\ncrates/bastion-server/src/http.rs:66:        .route(\"/console/logs\", post(container_logs))\ncrates/bastion-server/src/http.rs:67:        .route(\"/console/{name}/stop\", post(container_stop))\ncrates/bastion-server/src/http.rs:68:        .route(\"/console/{name}/start\", post(container_start))\ncrates/bastion-server/src/http.rs:356:async fn console(State(app): State<App>) -> Response {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"80fe73da-38d2-405d-a320-7d4c50fe060c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/U