{"parentUuid":"625cd64c-58b6-4049-8dc4-5d658a6d4b84","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyCbCV6b2cE9L7Xsbx5g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The workflows page is reworked and committed as `2debf96`. It passed CI and the safeguard, and I checked each part in the app. Nothing is pushed.\n\n- **Cards:** each card now shows the step's name, its kind and what it runs, its dial and model, its budget when it has one, and whether it only reads, plus its results. Empty lines collapse. The canvas fills the page's width. The job page draws the same cards, so they're richer there too.\n- **Layout:** the step form is now a panel with the step's name, its kind, and \"Remove step\" at the top. Below that, four tabs show one part at a time:\n  - **Step:** name, kind, dial and text;\n  - **Options:** reach, model, budget and results;\n  - **Constraints · n**;\n  - **Capabilities · n**.\n\n  A shell step has only the first two tabs.\n- **Function search:** under Capabilities, \"Add\" has three forms, one at a time:\n  - **A function:** a search over the engine's functions, by name or by what they do. Name matches come first, and each result shows its worker and the first sentence of its description, with Ask and Allow buttons. A pattern such as `sandbox::fs::*` can be granted as typed.\n  - **A command:** type its words, and it grants `sandbox::exec` for that command.\n  - **An MCP server:** each server listed in Settings, granted as `mcp::<id>::*`.\n- **Capabilities:** each grant says in words what it covers, with an Ask | Allowed switch and Remove. The old Demote and Promote buttons are gone.\n- **Constraints:**\n  - Each row has a kind badge (Rule, Hook or Reviewer) and a colored rung: enforced red, checked amber, told gray.\n  - The list is sorted with enforced first, and a filter appears past five.\n  - \"Add\" offers one form at a time (a hook, a reviewer, or a constraint from another step), each with a line saying what it does.\n\nTo check the switch in the app, I gave Bug fix's build step its own grants and added `sandbox::fs::read`. Then I put it back on its kind's grants. The `bug-fix/plan` grant I mentioned last time is still there; I didn't touch it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":897,"cache_read_input_tokens":500025,"output_tokens":786,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":68},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":897,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":786,"cache_read_input_tokens":500025,"cache_creation_input_tokens":897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":897},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7add66d4-b3bb-414c-a9cf-e4308594f9ad","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgyCbC14rgMu31aQw2qCz","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fc50280-84cc-4cd2-b3c4-68567b16dfde","timestamp":"2026-11-12T14:35:16.496Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
