{"parentUuid":"d3b1f9f4-ff74-4fa8-a945-692995263743","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyDPUBw9gbgzz8T9qeHJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Result names are now checked when you type them and again when you save. The change is committed as `c169e53` and passed CI and the safeguard. Nothing is pushed.\n\n- **The rule:** a result name is one word made of letters, digits, `-` and `_`, such as `root-cause` or `design_notes`. Agent names already follow that rule. The workflow check on the server refuses any other name with \"the result name \"root cause\" must be one word: letters, digits, - and _\". It also still refuses a name that another step already gives.\n- **The form:** under \"Results it gives\", a red line names each entry that will be refused, as you type. I didn't disable the Save button, so a bad save still goes to the server and shows its refusal.\n- **Live check:** I typed `root cause` on Bug fix's plan step. The red line appeared, Save was refused with the message above, and Bug fix stayed at version 2 with `root-cause`. I restarted the app to drop that unsaved draft.\n- **Your saved workflows:** every saved result name on both servers already fits the rule, so none of them will refuse its next save.\n\nThe desktop doesn't depend on `bastion-core`, so the one-line rule lives in both places, and each copy has its own test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":272,"cache_read_input_tokens":538959,"output_tokens":390,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":272,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":390,"cache_read_input_tokens":538959,"cache_creation_input_tokens":272,"cache